{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:13:59.119Z","ordinal":490957,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18866-1ff5-7d90-876e-24d672df144c","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae370c400ec81a0b7e4815f47bc602a","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Campaign status: `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE` — acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS.** No RC has been accepted and v1.0.0 has not been published.\n\n- **Terminal scope:** DEC-20 on `origin/main` (`14be4b8`) waives the manual §5.3 matrix for v1.0.0. Automated §5.1 and scripted installed-RC §5.2 remain mandatory.\n- **PR #318 evaluator fix** (`1682dcb`): Node 22 and Node 24 CI failed on compiler-exposure scanning timing out and refusing qualification. The exact-head local full suite is still running under its existing SUITE claim. I recorded the failure and left the evaluator file claim with its owner.\n- **PR #326 dependency fix** (`d7997b8`): Node 22, Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL passed. Linux packaging/reproducibility and Entire Gates are still running; it is not ready to merge.\n- **RC10 scripted PTY evidence:** The current evidence record is `PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED`: it retains a Ctrl-C cancellation outlier above the five-second limit and marks accessibility coverage partial. This does not satisfy §5.2.\n- **Coordination:** I logged the exact-head findings. A request to relay the PR #318 failure is awaiting Agent Mail contact approval, so no message was delivered; the existing claim was not taken over.\n- **Held-out qualification:** Still blocked on corpus completion/custody acceptance; qualification has not started.\n\nThe shared dirty checkout remains untouched. The terminal waiver and CI findings are recorded in the existing claims log."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793290436042,"completed_at_ms":1793290439119}}
