{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:23:13.324Z","ordinal":491255,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18871-74a8-7bc3-9805-31344cd738a3","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c8d45418-7e38-4505-b601-699d3d88efb9","process_id":"28923","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -C 3 '5\\.1|5\\.2|5\\.3|manual|waiv|terminal'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | rg -n -C 4 'DEC-19|terminal|waiv'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/README.md | rg -n -C 2 'terminal|§5'; git status --porcelain=v1 --branch | head -50; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v7 status --short --branch 2>/dev/null; cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v7/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/disposition.json 2>/dev/null"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -C 3 '5\\.1|5\\.2|5\\.3|manual|waiv|terminal'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | rg -n -C 4 'DEC-19|terminal|waiv'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/README.md | rg -n -C 2 'terminal|§5'; git status --porcelain=v1 --branch | head -50; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v7 status --short --branch 2>/dev/null; cat /home/mike/nexus-wt/qualify-all-accepted-v7/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/disposition.json 2>/dev/null"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"24-1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n25-2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n26-3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n28-5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n29-\n30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n31-\n32-Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n33-\n--\n48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\n52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n54-\n--\n78-|---|---|---|\n79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n--\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n--\n156-| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n157-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n158-\n159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n160-\n161:### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n162-\n163-These must pass:\n164-\n--\n173-- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n174-- new: the package PTY smoke\n175-\n176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n177-\n178-These are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n179-\n--\n187-| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n189-\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n191-\n192:**Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix below is not a release gate; no operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell evidence are required, and none are claimed. Automated CI checks in §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n193-\n194:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n195-\n196:For each terminal × size, check:\n197-\n198-1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n199-2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n200-3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n201-4. Resize during streaming.\n202-5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n203:6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n204-7. NO_COLOR.\n205-\n206:Record PASS/FAIL per cell and the observed outcomes for each check, bound to the exact installed RC artifact, terminal environment, and size. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver); this does not waive any interactive check, safety gate, per-cell verdict, or evidence record.\n207-\n208-**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n209-\n--\n277-| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n278-| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n279-| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n280:| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n281-| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n282-| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n283-| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n--\n333-- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n334-- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n335-- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n337-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n338-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n339-- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\n50-## DEC-02: Role of the REPL\n51-\n52-**Options.** (A) Remove the REPL. **(B, chosen)** The REPL is a supported secondary surface: used for non-TTY input, scripting and fallback, with its approvals fixed to the TUI's standard. (C) The REPL stays the default.\n53-\n54:**Rationale.** The REPL is the only interactive surface when stdin or stdout is not a terminal, and when the Rust TUI is missing. Removing it loses a fallback. Keeping it as the default contradicts UI-004.\n55-\n56-**Also decided.** The top-level flags `--approve`, `-r/--resume [id]`, `--repl` and `--live` are **implemented** rather than removed from the docs, because USER_MANUAL already teaches them.\n57-\n58-**Affected requirements:** REQ-REL-101, REQ-REL-102, REQ-SEC-103.\n--\n237-**Rejected alternatives.** (A) Lower the floor to satisfy the band — rejected: reintroduces under-estimation and the context-overflow class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent. (B) Drop the CJK/Hangul corpora from the fixture — rejected: removes the evidence. (C) Change the pinned tokenizer — out of scope; the fixture pins the qualification worker.\n238-\n239-**Affected:** REQ-AGT-118; SPEC-11 §2.7 and ACC-VER-07; REQUIREMENTS ledger row REQ-AGT-118; `cli/test/fixtures/token_calibration.json` and `cli/test/tokens.test.ts`. No change to `cli/src/tokens.ts` behaviour.\n240-\n241:## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\n242-\n243:**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\n244-\n245:**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\n246-\n247-**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\n248-\n249:## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n250-\n251:**Status: withdrawn.** The waiver described in this decision is not in effect.\n252-\n253:**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n254-\n255:**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n256-\n257:**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n258-\n259-**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n260-\n261:## DEC-20: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n262-\n263:**Status: accepted by the release owner, 2026-10-29.** This decision supersedes DEC-19 for v1.0.0.\n264-\n265:**Direction.** The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No manual operator run, cell verdict, or per-cell evidence is required, and the waiver does not claim that any cell passed. The automated CI gate in §5.1 and the scripted installed-RC PTY gate in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n266-\n267:**Scope.** This waiver applies only to ACC-TUI-MANUAL and only for v1.0.0. It does not waive ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, exact-RC identity, any §5.1 or §5.2 scenario, safety checks, or any other release gate. DEC-18's screenshot-artifact waiver remains recorded; no screenshots are required for a matrix that is not run.\n268-\n269:**Qualification applicability:** REQ-QUAL-108 = ACC-TUI-STEER and ACC-TUI-A11Y remain required; ACC-TUI-MANUAL is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n270-\n271:**Disclosure.** Report ACC-TUI-MANUAL as waived by this decision, not passed and not outstanding. Preserve historical operator observations as observations only; do not promote them to cell results.\n272-\n273:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §§1.1, 3.1, 5, and 10; REQ-QUAL-108 exact-RC evidence mapping; stable v1.0.0 release notes; READINESS; terminal-matrix worksheet disposition.\n274-\n275-## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n276-\n277-| # | Action | Why | When |\n3-This package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n4-\n5:**Historical verdict: v1.0.0 readiness was BLOCKED at the 2026-10-16 source-suite checkpoint.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. At that checkpoint, held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remained incomplete. For v1.0.0, the manual matrix was later waived by DEC-20; see [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for the current disposition and remaining gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n6-\n7-## How to read it\n## main...origin/main [ahead 1, behind 1565]\n M .claude/settings.json\n M AGENTS.md\n M cli/dist/agent.js\n M cli/dist/core/state.js\n M cli/package.json\n M cli/src/agent.ts\n M cli/src/checkpoint.ts\n M cli/src/core/durable_file.ts\n M cli/src/core/persistence_protection.ts\n M cli/src/core/state.ts\n M cli/src/flight.ts\n M cli/src/knowledge.ts\n M cli/src/session.ts\n M cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts\n M core/tests/adversarial_path_traversal.rs\nA  docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nA  docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\nA  scripts/check_requirements.mjs\n?? .entire/agent-guide.md\n?? CLAUDE.md\n?? check_in_agents.py\n?? checkin-agents.md\n?? checkin.py\n?? cli/test/agent_prompt.test.ts\n?? cli/test/helpers/setup.ts\n?? cli/test/home_isolation.test.ts\n?? cli/test/persistence_hygiene.test.ts\n?? docs/codebase-review-enhancements.md\n?? docs/enhancement-opportunities.md\n?? docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/README.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/SHA256SUMS\n?? docs/v1.0.0/agents/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/evidence/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/plans/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/specs/\n?? jsf/\n?? nexus-continuity-validation/\n?? nexus-session-session_20261014_091558_9m78.json\n?? nexus-session-session_20261023_134635_z1dnlfek.json\n?? nexus-session-session_20261026_162439_34f2cnrn.json\n?? package-lock.json\n?? send_message_snippet.txt\n## v1/qualify-all-accepted-v7...origin/main [ahead 22, behind 155]\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":11587587}},"started_at_ms":1793290993312,"completed_at_ms":1793290993324}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:23:14.590Z","ordinal":491256,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18879-039e-78d0-97b7-1daefdd392fa","call_id":"call_fee6fc4aa7bb49a3977e8e0ad38933f1","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"[\"mcp__mcp_search__work_state_read\",\"mcp__mcp_search__work_state_write\"]"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 4439)\nTotal output lines: 199\n\n24-1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n25-2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n26-3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n27:4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n28-5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n29-\n30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n31-\n32-Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n33-\n--\n48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\n52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n54-\n--\n78-|---|---|---|\n79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81:| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n--\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n--\n156-| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n157-| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n158-\n159:## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n160-\n161:### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n162-\n163-These must pass:\n164-\n--\n173-- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n174-- new: the package PTY smoke\n175-\n176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n177-\n178-These are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n179-\n--\n187-| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n189-\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n191-\n192:**Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix below is not a release gate; no operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell evidence are required, and none are claimed. Automated CI checks in §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n193-\n194:Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n195-\n196:For each terminal × size, check:\n197-\n198-1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n199-2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n200-3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n201-4. Resize during streaming.\n202-5. Esc durin…439 tokens truncated…ource commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n335-- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n337-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n338-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n339-- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\n50-## DEC-02: Role of the REPL\n51-\n52-**Options.** (A) Remove the REPL. **(B, chosen)** The REPL is a supported secondary surface: used for non-TTY input, scripting and fallback, with its approvals fixed to the TUI's standard. (C) The REPL stays the default.\n53-\n54:**Rationale.** The REPL is the only interactive surface when stdin or stdout is not a terminal, and when the Rust TUI is missing. Removing it loses a fallback. Keeping it as the default contradicts UI-004.\n55-\n56-**Also decided.** The top-level flags `--approve`, `-r/--resume [id]`, `--repl` and `--live` are **implemented** rather than removed from the docs, because USER_MANUAL already teaches them.\n57-\n58-**Affected requirements:** REQ-REL-101, REQ-REL-102, REQ-SEC-103.\n--\n237-**Rejected alternatives.** (A) Lower the floor to satisfy the band — rejected: reintroduces under-estimation and the context-overflow class REQ-AGT-118 exists to prevent