{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:27:11.080Z","ordinal":491395,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1887c-9f68-7dc1-a680-0cc90b9f44cd","call_id":"call_58fa60b843c24b89969318b8b3482235","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No ownership or handoff change is visible. At `origin/main` `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`, issue #1 remains open and unassigned; its latest comment (#6483900189) reports no custodian update and no qualification runs. The Agent Mail directory shows no active project windows or designated custodian, and the public claims log has no held-out handoff record.\\n\\nThe remaining external dependency is a reachable owner identifying the designated custodian or assigning a replacement, followed by an acknowledged handoff. That custodian must handle the legacy-to-`blackbox-v1` conversion or replacement, private validation, and renewed custody acceptance before qualification. I did not contact anyone or access private corpus material.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — uncommitted diff SHA-256: `2a6a9bef7f44a95f4341ed09dd71a6927b4f4a29a9daaad42486491e014870a9` on `e85fecfdc4a49004dca9eca0097f595534912c9b`.\\n\\nThe narrowed `find` predicates retain the prior checks: executable regular files need a compiler-like name, while symlinks are inspected when either their name or link target looks compiler-like. The existing inspection still resolves the target and filters by executable status and compiler identity before masking. The reported focused test results are consistent with the inspected change, though I did not run tests. No actionable findings.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1887a-3678-7eb0-a65c-0231eb513ce7","create_time":1793291231.0802836}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"f