{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:27:27.038Z","ordinal":491410,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1887a-3678-7eb0-a65c-0231eb513ce7","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9d335422-ddd3-44f5-a5d2-77e50f07f1cf","process_id":"23110","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -n -i -E 'custodian|held.out|T2 custody' origin/main -- docs/v1.0.0 docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification | head -70"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"git grep -n -i -E 'custodian|held.out|T2 custody' origin/main -- docs/v1.0.0 docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification","query":"custodian|held.out|T2 custody","path":"main"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/resource-limits-20261021T0500Z-synthetic.json:251:    \"filesystemBoundary\": \"direct and /proc/1/root probes could not reach operator home, held-out path, or root-owned canary\"\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/resource-limits-20261021T0500Z-synthetic.json:254:    \"Synthetic infrastructure evidence only; not a held-out or qualification result.\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/resource-limits-20261021T0500Z-synthetic.md:11:| Host-path boundary | Bubblewrap user/PID/net namespaces | Direct paths and `/proc/1/root` paths to operator home, held-out location, and root-owned canary | All paths inaccessible | canary, HOME, mount, and workspace removed |\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/resource-limits-20261021T0500Z-synthetic.md:15:This is host infrastructure evidence, not held-out qualification or custody acceptance. The path-canary test exercises the production candidate Bubblewrap sandbox but does not exercise end-to-end `eval/run.mjs` task staging with Git object canaries. Those custody and runner-path gates remain open.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261018T1311Z.json:40:      \"name\": \"the evaluator cannot reach operator files or the held-out store\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T0338Z-synthetic.json:45:      \"name\": \"the evaluator cannot reach operator files or the held-out store\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T0338Z-synthetic.md:14:The store argument was a temporary synthetic directory containing a canary file. The evaluator could not access that directory or the isolated operator home. No held-out store, task, answer, validator, or private corpus material was accessed. This run verifies the current host controls and denial of the synthetic path; it does not establish custodian-store permissions, corpus custody acceptance, or qualification readiness.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T1457Z-setup-failure.json:45:      \"name\": \"the evaluator cannot reach operator files or the held-out store\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T1457Z-setup-failure.md:9:The only failure was test setup: the command set `TMPDIR` to a path inside the isolated temporary home but did not create that directory. The fixture returned `ENOENT` while trying to create its temporary test directory. The evaluator account, resource controls, cgroup cleanup, process-tree reaping, synthetic-store denial, and workspace cleanup checks passed. No held-out data was used. This run is preserved, excluded from the successful result, and superseded by [the corrected 10/10 run](validate-20261020T1457Z-synthetic.md), which creates the temporary directory before execution.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T1457Z-synthetic.json:45:      \"name\": \"the evaluator cannot reach operator files or the held-out store\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261020T1457Z-synthetic.md:12:The `--heldout` argument pointed only to a temporary root-owned directory containing a synthetic canary. The validator checked access by path and did not read its contents. No held-out corpus, task, answer, validator, or private custody material was accessed. This evidence does not establish custodian-store access controls, corpus acceptance, or qualification readiness.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261021T0443Z-synthetic.json:45:      \"name\": \"the evaluator cannot reach operator files or the held-out store\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261021T0443Z-synthetic.md:16:The store argument was a temporary root-owned synthetic directory containing one canary. The validator checked that the evaluator could not access its path; no held-out corpus, task, answer, validator, or private custody data was accessed. The synthetic store and temporary probe home were removed after the run.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-20261021T0443Z-synthetic.md:18:This result verifies the host controls and the existing host preflight behavior at the tested revision. It does **not** demonstrate deliberate CPU, memory, process-count, or storage-limit violations under the separate evaluator UID, nor the full `eval/run.mjs` orchestration path with Git solution canaries. Those remain qualification-preflight evidence gaps; held-out qualification has not started.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-exact-head.json:40:      \"name\": \"the evaluator cannot reach operator files or the held-out store\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/host/validate-main-8935918-synthetic.json:45:      \"name\": \"the evaluator cannot reach operator files or the held-out store\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md:11:- Workspace: fresh synthetic repository under `/tmp/nexus-rc10-openrouter-live-js-v2-20261027/workspace`; no user project, held-out content, corpus, or private validator was used.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md:29:This evidence establishes one synthetic OpenRouter live task on the installed RC10 artifact. It does not establish held-out, standalone long-task, provider recovery, T3/T4, cross-runner, manual terminal, exact-RC acceptance, or stable-release completion. OpenRouter's separate provider verification receipts and result are in [`../providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl`](../providers/openrouter-receipts-20261027T022710Z.jsonl) and [`../providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json`](../providers/openrouter-verify-20261027T022710Z.json).\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/providers/README.md:28:These records cover the provider verification path only. The synthetic task and its failed attempts are separately documented, and all held-out, long-task, fault-injection, terminal, cross-runner, independent acceptance, and stable-release gates remain outside this result.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/README.md:5:All workspaces and gateway responses were synthetic. No user workspace, credentials, held-out tasks, or real provider inference were used. Runtime and dependency identity are in runtime.txt and requirements.txt. Raw terminal streams, readable screen captures, scenario scripts, and mock gateway logs are retained and checksummed.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/README.md:29:This evidence does not establish the manual five-terminal by three-size human matrix, full ACC-TUI-A11Y acceptance, standalone gateway qualification, real-provider qualification, held-out T2/T3, T4 fault injection, independent X5 acceptance, or power-loss recovery. Application process-death recovery is a separate gate and is not labeled power-loss evidence.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md:3:Candidate: `v1.0.0-rc.10`, source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The installed package was invoked through its installed TUI launcher. Each workspace and outer HOME/XDG tree was isolated. Gateway and workspace contents were synthetic; no credentials, held-out tasks, or provider access were used.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027/README.md:3:Candidate: `v1.0.0-rc.10`, source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The probe used the installed RC10 launcher, a synthetic local mock gateway, isolated HOME/XDG/workspaces, and no provider credentials or held-out data.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027/corrected-approval-path/README.md:5:This focused probe used the installed RC10 launcher, a synthetic localhost mock gateway, an isolated HOME/XDG tree, and a disposable Git workspace. It used `TERM=dumb`, 40×14. No live provider, credential, held-out task, or private evaluation data was involved.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/platform-e2/README.md:3:This evidence covers the exact workflow-produced RC9 installer and package on four prepared Linux images: Ubuntu 22.04, Ubuntu 24.04, Debian 12, and Fedora 40. Containers ran as non-root UID/GID 10001 with disposable `/home/nexus-e2`; no held-out payloads, user data, or credentials were used.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/README.md:3:This evidence records scripted pseudo-terminal scenarios against the workflow-produced, installer-installed Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.9 package. The launcher used was the installed `nexus` command, which starts the packaged TUI, sidecar, and `harness-core`. The synthetic mock gateway and synthetic workspaces are included in the test scripts; no user workspace or held-out task payload was used.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/README.md:19:These results cover scripted mock-gateway PTY scenarios only. They do not establish the manual five-terminal × three-size matrix (`ACC-TUI-MANUAL`), all-state accessibility, real provider qualification, held-out task quality, standalone gateway qualification, independent acceptance, or power-loss recovery. The partial installed-RC9 `NO_COLOR` / `TERM=dumb` probe is recorded under [`accessibility/`](accessibility/README.md): the `NO_COLOR=1` cells pass, but `TERM=dumb` emits color reset SGR sequences and fails that criterion. Failed or superseded harness attempts remain preserved outside this evidence directory under `/var/tmp/nexus-rc9-pty-4cae11c/attempt*`; they are not counted as passing evidence.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/manifest.json:49:    \"held-out task-quality qualification\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc10-chatgpt-verification-20261027T174805Z.json:76:    \"It does not establish standalone engineering-task correctness, held-out qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, terminal acceptance, or independent RC acceptance.\",\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:20:The source tests cover the applicable source acceptance criteria. They do not claim installed-RC qualification, held-out qualification, cross-runner qualification, or human terminal acceptance. Those release gates remain pending.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:33:This revalidation confirms source-level evidence on the rebased candidate only. It does not satisfy exact-RC, held-out, cross-runner, or human terminal qualification.\norigin/main:docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/sec101-119-pty-20261025.md:41:This is a local source-test result on commit `93d0fa460517bf60fe5817cf4b51278498ec8d0e`; fresh exact-head hosted CI is still required. Exact-RC, held-out, cross-runner, and human terminal qualification remain pending.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:49:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:142:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:214:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:219:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:343:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:67:7. **Qualified.** Held-out matched evaluation, plus fault injection, meeting the pre-registered thresholds in DEC-05.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:109:| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:115:- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:13:| [DEC-05](#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds) | Evaluation protocol and thresholds | 40 held-out T2 tasks, 5 runs, 2 peers, thresholds below | Needs an external author (see actions) |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:84:- 40 held-out T2 tasks, at least 20 from external repositories at pinned commits, across JS/TS, Python, Rust and Go, with at least 6 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:99:| Held-out T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | **≥ 60% absolute** and **≥ (best matched peer − 10 points)** |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:110:**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:97:- **No product qualification exists.** \"Blocked\" is established, from reproduced defects. \"Qualified\" cannot be: there is no held-out, fault-injection or standalone evidence, and the tasks used in the historical pilot were tuned.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:15:**Held-out custody and qualification:** The latest public metadata update on issue #1 (06:02 UTC) records unresolved custody ownership: a historical handoff log names SageBridge as an accepted successor, while the active custody record still names OpenCode. The latest posted T2 count is 20/40 tasks; no new custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. The custodian identity and acknowledged transfer must be reconciled before qualification. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:29:**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The claims identify OpenCode as the prior/current custodian workflow, but do not verify the responsible human identity; SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The successor T2 store remains 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust tasks need the reviewed, pinned-toolchain change integrated. Reported T3 digest/schema/isolation checks are 8/8, which is not full T3 task-quality qualification. At 04:23 UTC the OpenCode custodian holds SUITE for two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted tasks with isolated HOME; a live validator child process was observed. This is custody revalidation, not held-out qualification; no result or custody acceptance is recorded. Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; the latest metadata-only correction was posted at 04:18 UTC. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, full T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:33:**Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:45:**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned (last updated 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC); no custodian acceptance or held-out T2/T3/T4 qualification is established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user waived screenshot artifacts, while terminal behavior checks remain unrun. Standalone/provider, fault-injection, successor-RC qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:61:Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Held-out/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider and standalone coverage, successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:75:**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed or qualification run. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; the final installed RC does not exist. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, provider and standalone coverage, cross-runner reproducibility, human terminal evidence, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:77:**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. PR integration is blocked by required Entire review findings/approvals; exact-RC qualification is additionally blocked by independent held-out custody and the required human terminal matrix. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated. The checkpoint below is retained as the 13:34 UTC snapshot and is superseded for current CI, requirements, PR checks, local suite result, and release status.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:89:**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` is still the latest release (published 2026-10-27); the package at `b293b44` is also `1.0.0-rc.10`, so source changes require a successor RC before installed-RC qualification. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 exists. Held-out issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public status request was posted 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC, with no custodian response as of this checkpoint. The public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance, and no held-out qualification has started. T2/T3/T4, evaluator/custody acceptance, remaining provider and standalone gates, cross-runner reproducibility, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix remains 0/15; the Ubuntu desktop has setup evidence only, with no qualifying screenshots or cell verdicts recorded.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:101:**Lifecycle, scheduler, and evaluation evidence:** `cli/test/convergence_integration.test.ts` covers end-to-end scheduling and execution scenarios. `cli/test/convergence_scheduler_properties.test.ts` runs generated DAG invariants over 100 fixed seeds; this is reproducible generated coverage, not a claim that every scheduler property or arbitrary graph has been proven. PR #297’s regression tests for the TDD diagnostic paths are merged and its required CI passed. The `eval/` pilot suite does not satisfy held-out acceptance: the independent 40-task corpus, custody acceptance, and exact-RC qualification remain required and open.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:105:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Held-out T2/T3/T4, remaining live-provider and standalone gates, successor-RC artifact qualification, cross-runner evidence, the 15-cell human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on these mandatory checks.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:119:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease, built from immutable source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and was last updated 2026-10-27 18:47 UTC; no custodian acceptance or compatible sealed held-out corpus is recorded, and no held-out payload has been accessed. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining live provider and standalone gates, qualification of a candidate built from current source, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15 formally recorded cell verdicts**, with no screenshots. The operator reports successful rendering at tested sizes but a 43×13 lower limit for tmux inside GNOME Terminal; this is partial observation, not completion of the prescribed matrix. The available `mike-dev` shell is headless, and its configured `ubuntu-desktop` host name does not resolve, so I could not produce real-terminal screenshots or verdicts from this session. Stable publication remains gated on every required acceptance gate.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:133:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest release and is still a prerelease; its immutable source is `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`. No stable `v1.0.0` exists. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without an independent custodian acceptance or a compatible sealed held-out corpus; no held-out payload has been accessed. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining live provider and standalone gates, qualification of a candidate built from current source, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The required five-terminal by three-size matrix has **0/15 formally recorded cell verdicts** and no screenshots. The operator reports that the client rendered at the sizes tried, but tmux inside GNOME Terminal could not be reduced below 43×13; this does not establish every prescribed interaction or matrix cell. Stable publication remains gated on all required acceptance gates.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:149:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the newest prerelease on source `16ee8ca`; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Held-out custody acceptance and compatible frozen T2 data remain unresolved (issue #1 is open with no custodian response); T2/T3/T4, evaluator-host acceptance, the remaining live provider and standalone gates, and independent exact-RC acceptance are incomplete. The human five-environment by three-size terminal matrix remains **0/15**, pending the operator; no per-cell verdict or evidence is recorded. Keep stable publication gated on every required acceptance gate.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:161:**Qualification and publication:** RC10 remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release is claimed. Exact cross-runner reproducibility passed for immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca`; a successor candidate from current main still requires its own reproducibility run. Held-out custodian acceptance, T2/T3/T4, remaining live provider and standalone qualification, independent exact-RC acceptance, and human terminal evidence remain open. The five-environment by three-size operator terminal matrix remains **0/15**; no cell result or screenshot is recorded. Automated PTY evidence does not substitute for these human cells. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on all mandatory acceptance criteria.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:173:**Other release-path PRs:** PR [#276](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/276) records a synthetic-only qualification-host preflight (10/10) bound to `ceabfcc`; its Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks pass, while Linux CI remains in progress. Its evidence does not establish custodian access, held-out qualification, or acceptance. PR [#277](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/277) addresses configured Git-hook execution during checkpoint and retention operations. Its exact diff received conflicting review dispositions: a GitHub review comment requested changes for a hook-discovery race and retention error accounting, while a separate read-only review returned ACCEPT. The findings remain unresolved pending the claimed implementation owner's response; no acceptance or merge is claimed. Node 22/24, CodeQL, and JavaScript/TypeScript checks pass; Linux CI remains in progress.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:175:**Requirements and qualification:** A clean disposable snapshot of `origin/main@ceabfccf466ab39fc80c274400bae5aa0744a227` passed `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals) and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.10`. The first requirements invocation on the documentation-dirty readiness worktree was correctly refused by its clean-worktree preflight and is not treated as a gate result. The existing [RC10 OpenRouter evidence bundle](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/openrouter-live-task/README.md) establishes a pinned provider verification and one passing synthetic small task; this does not establish the broader provider/standalone matrix. Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains an unaccepted prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without independent custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody/host acceptance, remaining provider/standalone profiles, cross-runner exact-RC reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance, and scripted terminal gates remain incomplete.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:190:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains a prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` is listed. The human five-terminal by three-size matrix remains **0/15** and pending. The user's informal observation is that rendering works at tested sizes except tmux in GNOME Terminal, where the smallest usable size is 43×13; there are no per-cell records or screenshots, so human acceptance is not established. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open, last updated 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC, with no custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, evaluator custody and host acceptance, live provider/standalone, independent exact-RC, scripted terminal, and human acceptance gates remain incomplete. Publication authorization remains gated on every required acceptance gate.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:202:**Release and acceptance gates:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains a prerelease; stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. The human real-terminal matrix remains 0/15; the user's report of rendering at 43×13 in tmux on GNOME Terminal is not the full matrix and had no captured screenshots. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN, last updated 2026-10-26 17:37:53 UTC, with no recorded custodian acceptance. T2/T3/T4, live provider/standalone, independent exact-RC, and human acceptance gates remain incomplete. Publication authorization remains gated on all required acceptance.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:218:**Candidate and gates:** The latest public release remains prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` with archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. Stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. The required real-terminal matrix remains **0/15**; scripted terminal evidence does not replace operator evidence. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no recorded custodian acceptance; no private payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, exact-current-RC provider/standalone and cross-runner qualification, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization is granted but gated. The distribution target is the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:230:**Installed RC and qualification:** The latest public release remains prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0` with archive SHA-256 `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. No stable `v1.0.0` release appears among the current public releases. The human five-terminal, three-size matrix remains **0/15**; scripted terminal evidence is partial and does not replace the operator matrix. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) has no custodian response to the latest metadata-only request (2026-10-26); no held-out payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, standalone/provider qualification, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:242:**Remaining exact-RC and release gates:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264) archives RC10 scripted observations and keeps the manual matrix separate; its remote head is `73bdc7d91b1b8925b522b052d89228d99bad4893` on a stale base, with all reported exact-head checks successful. Its manual worksheet is blank. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) still lacks custodian acceptance; the sealed public manifest alone is not private custody acceptance, and no held-out payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, standalone qualification, full installed-RC provider coverage, exact-RC cross-runner checks, the manual matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release is published; publication authorization remains granted but gated by acceptance.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:254:**RC and remaining acceptance:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains an unaccepted prerelease from source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, not the current main source. PR #265's merged OpenRouter evidence covers one pinned-model verification and one synthetic small task. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open without custodian acceptance; no held-out task payload was accessed or run. Installed exact-RC qualification, standalone/provider matrix coverage, T2/T3/T4, the complete terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release is published. Existing publication authorization remains gated on every mandatory acceptance gate.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:268:**Held-out and human gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open with no custodian acceptance recorded; no held-out payload was accessed and T2/T3/T4 acceptance is not established. The manual terminal matrix still requires operator evidence across five environments and three sizes. At 2026-10-27 03:49 UTC, I verified over SSH to `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`) that `/home/mike/nexus-rc10-manual-evidence/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md` exists and contains an unfilled 15-cell template with directories for every environment/size pair. No cell evidence is present; the installed candidate identity is blank. Any matrix run must use the eventual installed RC. Scripted PTY output is not a substitute.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:287:**Custody and remaining acceptance:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN and its latest update is 17:37:53 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded. No private held-out payload was accessed, and held-out qualification has not started. The repository's latest human terminal matrix status is 0/15; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute for those operator cells. Current-source provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC9 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; the existing publication authorization remains gated on every required release acceptance.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28721}},"started_at_ms":1793291247037,"completed_at_ms":1793291247037}}
