{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:28:29.276Z","ordinal":491473,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1887d-d0db-7d30-9375-c3be16479135","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — combined review fingerprint (tracked diff plus untracked helper): `b949bac71bfc8280f1c7bc5f895e85f465f2eb81f991d9d7188f95858818a844`. The tracked `eval/isolate.mjs` diff is `8f40cb5c…`; untracked `eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs` is `de113afa…`.\n\nIn [`scan-compiler-exposure.mjs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs:46), repeated `stopAll()` calls clear and restart the SIGKILL timer. The stderr and output-limit handlers call it for each subsequent chunk (lines 78–90). A continuing `find` stream can therefore keep postponing escalation after SIGTERM, undermining the scanner’s bounded shutdown. Keep shutdown idempotent: schedule SIGKILL once, and don’t reset that deadline on later error or overflow events.\n\nI did not run tests. The owner’s reported focused test results were not independently verified."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1887a-3678-7eb0-a65c-0231eb513ce7","create_time":1793291309.2759922}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23024}}
