{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:31:04.748Z","ordinal":491618,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18880-302c-7833-8992-a0eca5127bf6","call_id":"call_4a9ac4e4e86e40ec803f913a7f54184c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---claim-protocol---\n26-if mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n27-  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\n29-else\n30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\n31-fi\n32-```\n--\n44-| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n45-| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n46:| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n47-| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n48-| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n--\n53-## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n54-\n55:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n56-\n57-| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n--\n85-3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n86-4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n87:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n88-6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n89-\n--\n93-|---|---|---|\n94-| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n95:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n96-| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n97-| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---claim-owner---\n{\"agent\":\"codex-root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/eval-agent-toolchain-binds\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds\",\"base\":\"1682dcb325cea7078e193d0ed0b5af5325ce8ca8\",\"since\":\"2026-10-29T16:31:15Z\",\"scope\":\"focused evaluator compiler exposure inventory validation for uncommitted PR318 patch; synthetic fixtures only; no held-out tasks\",\"head\":\"1682dcb325cea7078e193d0ed0b5af5325ce8ca8\"}\ntotal 24\ndrwxrwxr-x   2 mike mike  4096 Oct 29 16:30 .\ndrwxrwxr-x 155 mike mike 16384 Oct 29 16:30 ..\n-rw-rw-r--   1 mike mike   412 Oct 29 16:30 owner.json\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"---suite-path---\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/quickstart.md\n2026-10-29T15:39 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/deny.toml\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/check_notices.mjs\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/generate_sbom.sh\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/smoke-package.sh\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/ensure-ci-bubblewrap.sh\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/sync-version.mjs\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/release-tools/package.json\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/release-tools/package-lock.json\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/doc_commands.mjs\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/package-smoke-server.mjs\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/installer-smoke.sh\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/ensure-ci-user-cgroups.sh\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/install-evaluator-toolchains.sh\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/test-configure-github-community.py\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/package-linux.sh\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/repro-identity.mjs\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/check_requirements.mjs\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/check_deprecated_lock.mjs\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\n2026-10-29T15:40 /home/mike/nexus-wt/pr318-full-feHVov/scripts/terminal-acceptance