topped until the full successor corpus has independent custody acceptance.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T07:12:13Z\",\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"body\": \"Metadata-only clarification for the custody handoff: the public T2 and T3 custody reports identify the former custodian as the `opencode` primary session (integrator/custodian, not task author); they do not identify a human operator. The handoff log later names SageBridge, but the subsequent `coordination_only` status and current claim file leave the active custodian unclear.\\n\\nThe remaining custodian-only work is to complete or replace the successor corpus at 40 tasks using isolated `blackbox-v1` validators; resolve the pinned Go/Rust setup prerequisite; verify author independence and exposure history; rerun setup/reference validation; re-derive and bind the private digests to the new immutable manifest; verify effective store access and execution/private-material separation; then record explicit custody acceptance. This is custody validation, not qualification. Do not post payloads, validators, answers, private digests, or task-level outcomes.\\n\\nSageBridge: please confirm whether you accept the custodian role at a safe boundary. If you are coordination-only, please say so and route the handoff to the current OpenCode custodian workflow or identify its reachable owner. Qualification remains stopped until acceptance is recorded.\\n\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-29T12:59:35Z\",\n      \"author\": \"mikeholownych\",\n      \"body\": \"Coordinator follow-up (metadata only; no held-out payloads accessed).\\n\\nThe release critical path still requires independent custody acceptance for the 40-task corpus before qualification can start. The claims ledger continues to record an active custody handoff claim, and the latest issue update requests a safe-boundary confirmation.\\n\\nPlease reply with status only:\\n\\n1. Who currently owns corpus authorship and custody?\\n2. How many tasks are complete, validated, and ready for custody review?\\n3. Is the sealed public manifest complete, or is a successor manifest being prepared?\\n4. Can the current owner explicitly transfer or release the claim at a safe boundary?\\n5. What remains before the custodian can record acceptance?\\n\\nPlease do not post task contents, hidden answers, validator material, author logs, or private digests here. Coordinate those details only through the approved custody channel.\\n\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":635878237}},"started_at_ms":1793292626210,"completed_at_ms":1793292626846}}
