small synthetic bug-fix task with independent local validation; no repository or held-out content, no credential inspection or output, no gateway inference.\",\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:6:- **Eval:** the harness is sound for matched T2 fixture runs. The only results come from a 6-task pilot that is self-declared as tuned. No held-out set, no T3/T4, no fault injection. It cannot qualify v1 task quality as it stands.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:92:| EVL-001 | S1 (v1 task-quality claim) | Qualification evidence | eval/README.md:42,47-58; docs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/RESULT.md:62-63 | DOC-CLAIM + SOURCE. The only scored evidence is 6 in-repo T2 fixture tasks. RESULT.md itself says \"These six tasks were used to find and fix the issues … it does not qualify Nexus. Qualification needs a fresh task set.\" Missing: held-out tasks, the T3 long-task set, the T4 fault injector, the T3 fact-sheet scorer, and runs on the release candidate. The measured builds are 76f4081, ed17e99 and 4fcbe68-dirty; their rebased equivalents (fe576f1, d116e99, 0090f9c) are on main, but db1ca55 itself was never evaluated. | No basis for a v1 claim about task quality. The pilot verdict was \"NOT QUALIFIED (false VERIFIED=2)\". The rerun had 0 false VERIFIED, but on tuned tasks. | A v1 protocol is in §7. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:128:- **Credential custody in the broker is careful.** Checks on owner, 0400 mode, nlink and inode-before/after; O_NOFOLLOW; buffers zero-filled after use; a reflection scan over all git objects; error output limited to an allowlist of codes (demo-transport.mjs:152-185,375-391). Executables are bound by file descriptor (linux-bound-exec). Git config is hardened (no system or global config, no hooks, no credential helper, `followRedirects=false`, protocol allowlist) at :192-212. Tests are RUNTIME-verified: demo-transport 8/8; artifact-token-response 14 revoke cases plus 8 post-revoke cases; credential-lifecycle 25 assertions; linux-bound-exec; classify-revoke 11 cases; worker token-response 10/10; work-state-contract 2/2.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:154:- **G6: task difficulty and discrimination.** 4 of 6 pilot tasks were 10/10 for Nexus (ceiling). To qualify, calibrate a held-out set so that no task is solved by every agent 5/5.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:176:| EVL-R1 | **Held-out set:** at least 40 T2 tasks (proposal). At least 50% from external repos at pinned commits (JS/TS, Python, Rust, Go). The held-out half is authored by someone other than the Nexus developer and kept outside the repo (encrypted or private) until the freeze. The 6 pilot tasks plus the routing engx T01-T12 count as a *development* set only. | workflow | BLOCKER for any v1 quality claim | The manifest lists task sha256s committed *before* the release-candidate (RC) freeze. Tasks are revealed after scoring. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:183:| EVL-R8 | **Pass thresholds (proposal, owner input needed):** false VERIFIED = 0 (hard). Held-out T2 pooled correctness ≥ best matched peer − 10 points, and ≥60% absolute (proposal). No task class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) below 40%. Crash rate ≤2%. T4 truthful = 100%. Regression rate ≤5%. | release gate | BLOCKER | Scorer verdict table, signed off before the RC run. |\n.git/nexus-claims/archived/REDACTED.json:1:{\"agent\":\"/root\",\"host\":\"mike-dev\",\"branch\":\"v1/plan-10-host-preflight-main-1f3c655\",\"worktree\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-host-preflight-main-1f3c655\",\"base\":\"92d7a62f0fa20f4f2f3b91786c737fd6d5517075\",\"head\":\"0027ccccb1fbe3bac98bf53a8dd7c1c4bec3e8d3\",\"since\":\"2026-10-23T13:54:06Z\",\"scope\":\"record exact-main synthetic evaluator host preflight; do not access held-out corpus; no qualification acceptance claim\",\"status\":\"PR #163 updated and pushed at exact head 0027ccc, base main 6383623. Synthetic exact-source host preflight 10/10 PASS; independent review ACCEPT; JS/TS and CodeQL PASS; Node 22/24 exact-head CI running. No private corpus access.\",\"review\":\"Independent ACCEPT by plan05_readonly_review at exact head 0027ccccb1fbe3bac98bf53a8dd7c1c4bec3e8d3. All 16 source digests, profile/manifest digests, 10/10 results, exact clean source identity, and README scope independently verified; no private corpus access.\",\"report\":\"docs/reviews/evidence/v1/plan-10-host-preflight-current/validate-6383623-20261023T193626Z.json\"}\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:65:7. **Qualified.** Held-out matched evaluation, plus fault injection, meeting the pre-registered thresholds in DEC-05.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:31:| 8 | Author tasks (owner action X2). Development set: the existing 6 plus routing engx T01–T12. Held-out set: 40 T2 tasks, of which at least 20 are external, at least 6 per class, across 4 languages. Plus 8 T3 tasks. The sha256 manifest is committed before RC freeze. Calibrate on the development set only. | external store; `eval/heldout-manifest.json` | 7 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:34:| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (8×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:71:- The T2 held-out run shows 0 false VERIFIED (SPEC-10).\ndocs/v1.0.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:303:| Overfitting to eval tasks | Dataset splits (train/val/test); held-out tasks per DEC-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:48:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:141:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:211:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:216:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:337:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:108:| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:114:- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:116:- An implementing agent never edits `eval/heldout-manifest.json`, scorer thresholds or ACCEPTANCE §6.4 after the freeze.\n.git/nexus-claims/archived/GATEWAY-E5-rc3-openrouter-complete-20261023T221357Z/owner.json:6:  \"scope\": \"One small synthetic live engineering task through installed Nexus 1.0.0-rc.3 using the pinned OpenRouter free model; no repository or held-out content; independent local test validation; record raw task transcript and safe provider receipt only.\",\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_.github_workflows_ci.yml/owner.json:8:  \"scope\": \"PR #318 remediation: exact Go/Rust toolchain version pinning and oracle compiler isolation; no held-out tasks or payloads\",\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_.github_workflows_ci.yml/owner.json:11:  \"status\": \"PR #318 exact head f43f