{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:52:13.809Z","ordinal":492701,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1888f-e991-7d30-9330-bb330592dfef","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ed244069-efb5-4917-9ac1-e25ba3ea7314","process_id":"96685","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '70,130p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; sed -n '88,120p' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md; rg -n \"CUSTODY_HANDOFF|custodian.*(owner|accept)|held-out.*custodian|CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION|SageBridge\" .git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log .git/nexus-claims 2>/dev/null | tail -n 100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '70,130p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; sed -n '88,120p' docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md; rg -n \"CUSTODY_HANDOFF|custodian.*(owner|accept)|held-out.*custodian|CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION|SageBridge\" .git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log .git/nexus-claims 2>/dev/null | tail -n 100"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n| `package.json`, `cli/package.json`, `core/Cargo.toml`, lockfiles | 01, 06, 07, 08 | **Only one agent at a time.** Version fields are written only by `scripts/sync-version.mjs`. Dependency changes are separate commits that touch only the lockfile and manifest. |\n| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n| `cli/dist/**` | all, while tracked | Do not commit `cli/dist` from slices. PLAN-07 PR-7d untracks it (DEC-10). Until that merges, only the merging agent rebuilds and commits dist, in a final separate commit, after rebasing. |\n| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n\n### Ledger updates (`docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md`)\n\nA slice changes only the rows for its own requirement IDs: the status, test-reference and evidence cells, in place. It never reorders, adds or removes rows, and never edits another slice's rows. New requirements discovered during work go to §6, not into the ledger. Because rows are independent lines, git merges these edits cleanly. If a conflict appears anyway, resolve it row by row, keeping both changes.\n\n## 5. Commit and merge discipline\n\n1. Before **every** commit, compare `git rev-parse HEAD` with the commit you last made. Then run `git log <yours>..HEAD` on the branch. If anything foreign appears, stop and reconcile. Never commit generated artifacts (evidence, dist, lockfiles) over a branch that moved (lessons 2026-10-13).\n2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\n3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n\n## 6. Coordination records\n\n| Record | Where | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n\n## 7. Safe parallel lanes\n\nThe following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n\n| Phase | Parallel lanes |\n|---|---|\n| M0 | (a) PLAN-08 PR-8a, which must merge first. Then in parallel: (b) PLAN-06 PR-6a, (c) PLAN-09 PR-9a. |\n| M1 | (a) PLAN-01 PR-1a → PR-1b → PR-1c (sequential, owns `capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts` dispatch). (b) PLAN-02 PR-2a (Rust only). (c) PLAN-03 PR-3a → PR-3b (config/egress). (d) PLAN-11 PR-11a (`parser.ts`) and PR-11b (`tester.ts`, after PR-1c). Lanes (b), (c) and (d) do not touch `capabilities.ts`. |\n| M2 (alongside M1) | (a) PLAN-07 PR-7a/7b/7c (workflows, scripts). (b) PLAN-06 PR-6b after PLAN-01 PR-1b (shares `index.ts` flags). |\n| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\n| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n\n## 8. Independence constraints\n\n- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\n- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\n- An implementing agent never edits `eval/heldout-manifest.json`, scorer thresholds or ACCEPTANCE §6.4 after the freeze.\n\n| Metric | Threshold |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED | **0** (hard) |\n| Held-out T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | **≥ 60% absolute** and **≥ (best matched peer − 10 points)** |\n| Correctness per task class | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 outcome truthfulness | 100% |\n| T4 hangs beyond budget + 5 min | 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| `run`-mode operator interventions | 0 |\n\n**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\n\n**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connections (ChatGPT sign-in, OpenRouter) may be used for small-spend checks, but are not used for matched comparisons. One reason: `openrouter/free` routed 3 requests to 3 different models in the 2026-10-14 verify run, which breaks model matching.\n\n**Rationale.** These figures are the pilot's pre-registered thresholds (eval/README), tightened where the pilot showed weakness: false VERIFIED, crash accounting. The absolute floor prevents \"beat a weak peer\" from passing. Thresholds are fixed **before** the RC run.\n\n## DEC-06: Supported providers for v1\n\n| Tier | Providers | Condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Supported** | OpenAI-compatible local servers (llama.cpp server, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama) | The release notes name the server kinds that pass the standalone matrix (≥ 2 required). Others are listed as \"compatible, not qualified\". |\n| **Supported (optional integration)** | homelab-ai gateway | Never required (standalone gate). |\n| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\n| **Experimental → Supported if live-verified at RC** | OpenAI API key (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic compatible cloud | Not connected on the owner's install. They stay experimental unless keys are added and `nexus providers verify` passes at RC. |\n| **Experimental (always)** | ChatGPT sign-in (the owner's OpenAI OAuth connection), Copilot sign-in | They use unofficial OAuth flows with terms-of-service and stability risk. Opt-in with a visible warning. ChatGPT sign-in was live-verified on 2026-10-14 (`evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json`), and a live end-to-end run reached a correct VERIFIED (`evidence/live/run1_chatgpt_bugfix.log`). It is still labelled experimental because the sign-in flow is unofficial. |\n\n## DEC-07: Experimental surfaces (`nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles)\n\n- **`nexus eval`.** Labelled experimental. Its scoring is not fixed in v1, but its unsafe `git checkout` in the operator's workspace **is** fixed: it must run in a worktree (VER-07a). It is excluded from all claims. The SPEC-10 harness (`eval/`) is the qualification tool.\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:34:2026-10-21T11:01:00Z HELDOUT_CUSTODIAN_FOLLOWUP issue=1 comment=6314196186 scope=metadata_only T2_manifest_sha256=50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b incompatibility=current_eval_requires_blackbox_v1_prior_custody_report_says_legacy_hidden.command status=requested_custodian_successor_or_approved_compatibility_path_owner_and_eta plus unchanged T3 identity; no payload/details requested; no private store access\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:314:2026-10-23T21:54:10Z RELEASE_PUBLISHER_STATE_RECONCILED canonical RELEASE_PUBLISHER claim updated to main=830680b, PR171 merged, postmerge CI40029976616 active (Node22/24 success, Linux lane active), CodeQL40029976741 success. RC4 note commit 0cff3c3 is ancestor of main; no tag/release exists. Outstanding qualification: custodian-approved held-out T2/T3/T4 remains unavailable; OpenRouter required live small task not complete; installed-RC gates and human acceptance remain open.\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:331:2026-10-23T23:36:00Z MAIN_POST_MERGE_CI_SUCCESS sha=4bf6e2b041dc2efb54af551a73796aacc54494a3 run=40036791796 codeql=40036791830 all_jobs=success, including exact-main check_requirements. Active security slices: PR175 HTML control injection is being refreshed by codex-root against 4bf6e2b; tar symlink backslash traversal is separately claimed by opencode-defect-scan. Their files are not taken. No RC4 tag/release; installed-RC qualification, custodian-approved held-out tasks, OpenRouter live task, human acceptance remain incomplete.\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:342:2026-10-23 23:50:27Z RELEASE_GATES_STATUS main=4bf6e2b041dc2efb54af551a73796aacc54494a3 NodeFloor=>=22 verified; PR175=head7f202f7 base4bf6e2b owner=/root exact CI40040769503 in progress Node22/24 npm CLI test, CodeQL and JS/TS pass, independent ACCEPT; PR176=head ec98bb6 base4bf6e2b owner=opencode-defect-scan exact CI40040813520 in progress Node22/24 npm CLI test, CodeQL and JS/TS pass, fresh review found escape-return case isSymlinkSafe('../../nexus/file','nexus/dir/link') accepted by normalization; prior same-head ACCEPT conflicts; comment #6376992733 posted because GitHub blocks formal REQUEST_CHANGES on own PR. No RC4 or stable release. Held-out custodian Issue1 latest reply remains 2026-10-23T10:23Z; T2/T3 custody/format acceptance open; live OpenRouter task and final RC4/human acceptance pending.\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:1960:2026-10-29T01:55:48Z PR313_INTEGRATED candidate_base=v1/qualify-all-accepted-v9 merge=742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954 exact_head_checks_Node22_Node24_Linux=PASS review=ACCEPT PR311_head=742d00871c311d6829e8a4d0a1a3a1800701b954 PR311_exact_checks=RUNNING combined_independent_review=PENDING REDACTED REDACTED heldout_contact=SageBridge_message_130_pending_reply acceptance=IN_PROGRESS\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:2000:2026-10-29T04:25:46Z RELEASE_LOOP_REFRESH main=b10a85ad6305a4a3564a81d9bc66e88f55036c8d main_CI=PASS_40802654248 PR316=2e9ad10d review=ACCEPT Node24=PASS Node22=RUNNING Entire=RUNNING PR317=ff7698d3 review=ACCEPT Node22+24=RUNNING Entire=RUNNING suite_snapshot=03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c FINAL_EXIT=0_not_exact_current_head heldout_custodian_validation=ACTIVE process_4033762 evaluator_toolchain_owner=BlueFalcon_claim_protected REDACTED evaluator_implementation=uncommitted_owner_handoff_pending manual_terminal_matrix=0_of_15 acceptance=IN_PROGRESS\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:2006:2026-10-29T04:33:02Z CUSTODIAN_SAFE_BOUNDARY_REQUEST prior_heldout_validator_pid=4033762 process_handle_absent owner_result_not_recorded_current_SUITE_owner=SageBridge_scope=focused_checkpoint_restore_and_operation_git_tests; request custodian to report only exit/coverage/validation disposition and release or renew custody claim at safe boundary; no payload accessed, no claim takeover\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:2014:2026-10-29T04:53:30Z CUSTODY_SAFE_BOUNDARY_STATUS_REQUEST recipient=SageBridge process=477896/477925 confirmed_live request=metadata_only completion_or_checkpoint_and_claim_release_or_renewal contact_approval_pending message_not_delivered no_task_content_requested no_payload_access\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:2018:2026-10-29T04:59:45Z CUSTODY_SAFE_BOUNDARY_REFRESH prior_process_477896_477925=absent current_SUITE_owner=SageBridge_pid492960_scope=checkpoint_restore_and_operation_git_focused_tests previous_T2_result=UNKNOWN no_custody_acceptance_inferred Agent_Mail_safe_boundary_request_delivered_message=211 aggregate_outcome_only no_payloads_or_logs_requested\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:2046:2026-10-29T06:50:25Z\tCUSTODY_CONTACT_RECONCILIATION operator_identified=SageBridge_as_reachable_contact historical_custodian=opencode_primary_session current_custodian=UNRESOLVED REDACTED agent_mail_active_windows=0 registration_token_unavailable issue1_latest_status=2026-10-29T06:02:22Z_no_handoff_ack no_private_corpus_access qualification=STOPPED\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:2047:2026-10-29T06:54:16Z\tCUSTODY_HANDOFF_FOLLOWUP issue1_comment=6490082242 operator_contact=SageBridge asks explicit safe-boundary accept/release/renew; metadata_only=true no_payload_access=true qualification=STOPPED\n.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:2054:2026-10-29T07:12:28Z CUSTODY_HANDOFF_CLARIFIED issue_comment=6490405248 historical_custodian=opencode_primary_session transfer=SageBridge_unresolved requirements=40_blackbox_v1_tasks_pinned_toolchain_setup_independence_exposure_setup_reference_revalidation_digest_integrity_access_separation_acceptance public_metadata_only=true no_payload_access=true qualification=STOPPED\n.git/nexus-claims/RELEASE_PUBLISHER/owner.json:59:  \"qualification_status\": \"RC10 published; acceptance IN_PROGRESS; T2 custody unresolved; held-out issue #1 no custodian reply; human terminal matrix 0/15 and user unavailable for current cell; exact-source gates and successor-RC qualification remain open\",\n.git/nexus-claims/RELEASE_PUBLISHER/owner.json:75:  \"rc9_source_status\": \"Source gates PASS exact main 4cae11c; no RC9 candidate artifact yet because custodian acceptance is required before candidate construction/qualification.\",\n.git/nexus-claims/CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION/owner.json:1:{\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"role\":\"held-out corpus custodian (handoff accepted per claims.log CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED)\",\"branch\":null,\"worktree\":null,\"bound_manifest\":\"50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b\",\"since\":\"2026-10-29T02:24:10Z\",\"pid\":3848937,\"corpus_access\":\"custodian workflow only\",\"progress\":{\"successor_store\":\"/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-blackbox1\",\"tasks_built\":20,\"cases\":218,\"go_rust_blocked\":\"oracle sandbox exposes no Go/Rust toolchain; disposition recorded\",\"t3_acceptance\":\"PASS 8/8 digests+schema+isolation vs 85fb9caf\",\"revalidation\":\"batch waiting on SUITE (held by codex-root)\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":74789275}},"started_at_ms":1793292733734,"completed_at_ms":1793292733809}}
