{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:52:23.489Z","ordinal":492710,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a18893-b341-7ff0-92b1-08d7997259a9","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Current: 2026-10-29 4:52pm UTC\nThis file has prior observations — supplementary context follows. The Read result below is the full requested section.\n- **Need details on a past observation?** get_observations([IDs]) — ~300 tokens each.\n- **Need a structural map first?** smart_outline(\"docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md\") — line numbers only, cheaper than re-reading.\n### Oct 21, 2026\n20854 10:42p 🔵 Stale Claims Confirmed on RC2 Target Files — All Three Eligible for Breaking per CONCURRENCY Rules\n### Oct 29, 2026\n24284 2:26a 🔵 T2/T3 Custodian Identity Undocumented — User Unaware of Requirements\n24210 2:30a 🔵 CI Workflow Provisions Both NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT and NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_RUNTIME_ROOT via tmpfs + /opt Directory\n24270 4:22a 🔵 CONCURRENCY.md Documents Multi-Agent Claim Protocol — Slice-Based Atomic mkdir Claims\n\n---\n\nCurrent: 2026-10-29 4:52pm UTC\nThis file has prior observations — supplementary context follows. The Read result below is the full requested section.\n- **Need details on a past observation?** get_observations([IDs]) — ~300 tokens each.\n- **Need a structural map first?** smart_outline(\"docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\") — line numbers only, cheaper than re-reading.\n### Oct 18, 2026\n18348 1:02a 🔵 DEC-05 Qualification Thresholds and Peer Protocol Fully Documented\n19240 5:32p 🔵 T4 Spec Conflict Resolved by DEC-05 Amendment — ACCEPTANCE.md Now Says 9 Fault Classes × 5 Runs\n### Oct 29, 2026\n24204 2:24a 🔵 V1.0.0 Eval Blockers Confirmed — T2/T3/T4 Full Runs Not Complete, opencode Plugin Import Is Security Gap\n24239 2:36a 🔵 Composite Tree 25e9d9ba Already Contains DEC-19 Waiver in All Six Documentation Files\n24368 4:30a 🔵 DEC-19 Full Text Confirmed Withdrawn — Prior Waiver Conflicted With Release Requirement\n24256 6:51a ⚖️ DEC-19