{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:52:41.491Z","ordinal":492725,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1888f-e991-7d30-9330-bb330592dfef","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae379d6b1a881a099bb0a842b0caf1b","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The previous custodian is identifiable in the **private claims history**, though the public release docs don’t name a person. It records **OpenCode** as the custodian, including an earlier 40/40 reference-validation run. On Oct 29, the log records a handoff accepted by **SageBridge**, followed by an OpenCode custody claim.\n\nThe current custodian is less clear: a later entry says SageBridge reported **WhiteReef** as the current custodian, but no matching WhiteReef claim or explicit handoff appears in the claims records I checked. So there is a documented history, but the current rights holder needs to be confirmed before custody work proceeds. The corpus stores remain root-owned and inaccessible to this account; I did not inspect their contents.\n\nThe relevant records are [CONCURRENCY.md](/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:112), [DECISIONS.md](/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:102), and the shared [claims log](/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims.log:5742).\n\nI can’t save new claude-mem notes right now: “Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.”\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":753,"lineEnd":766,"note":"used prior Nexus custody and release-boundary context"}],"rolloutIds":["0199e7b5-8e62-7415-91e2-6e7bba099c31"]}},"started_at_ms":1793292758720,"completed_at_ms":1793292761491}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:52:41.495Z","ordinal":492726,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae379d6b1a881a099bb0a842b0caf1b","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The previous custodian is identifiable in the **private claims history**, though the public release docs don’t name a person. It records **OpenCode** as the custodian, including an earlier 40/40 reference-validation run. On Oct 29, the log records a handoff accepted by **SageBridge**, followed by an OpenCode custody claim.\n\nThe current custodian is less clear: a later entry says SageBridge reported **WhiteReef** as the current custodian, but no matching WhiteReef claim or explicit handoff appears in the claims records I checked. So there is a documented history, but the current rights holder needs to be confirmed before custody work proceeds. The corpus stores remain root-owned and inaccessible to this account; I did not inspect their contents.\n\nThe relevant records are [CONCURRENCY.md](/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:112), [DECISIONS.md](/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:102), and the shared [claims log](/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims.log:5742).\n\nI can’t save new claude-mem notes right now: “Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.”\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:753-766|note=[used prior Nexus custody and release-boundary context]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n0199e7b5-8e62-7415-91e2-6e7bba099c31\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1888f-e991-7d30-9330-bb330592dfef","create_time":1793292758.6959467,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae379d6b1a881a099bb0a842b0caf1b","turn_id":"01a1888f-e991-7d30-9330-bb330592dfef","role"