{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:55:15.090Z","ordinal":492850,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18894-e451-7fe2-b11c-0a0394ebbc6f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-72c71fd5-4326-471b-a933-5518433378be","process_id":"15754","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git grep -n -i -E 'manual (real[- ]terminal|terminal)|15[- ]cell|5.?x.?3|ACC-TUI-MANUAL|§5\\.3' origin/main -- docs/v1.0.0 docs/release* 2>/dev/null | head -n 120; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json | sort | rg 'release|readiness|notes|terminal|decisions'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git grep -n -i -E 'manual (real[- ]terminal|terminal)|15[- ]cell|5.?x.?3|ACC-TUI-MANUAL|§5\\.3' origin/main -- docs/v1.0.0 docs/release* 2>/dev/null | head -n 120; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json | sort | rg 'release|readiness|notes|terminal|decisions'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"origin/main:docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md:33:- Readiness, terminal and qualification records were refreshed through 2026-10-29. The manual real-terminal matrix is **required** for v1.0.0; the earlier matrix-waiver record was withdrawn (DEC-19). Screenshot artifacts alone are waived (DEC-18).\norigin/main:docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md:49:This is a candidate, not an accepted release. The installed-RC gates — platform and lifecycle evidence, the fifteen-cell manual terminal matrix, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — remain outstanding for this artifact. Passing source CI does not satisfy them.\norigin/main:docs/releases/v1.0.0.md:159:- **Manual real-terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** No manual five-terminal by three-size runs or per-cell evidence are claimed. The automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory release gates and must pass.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:243:**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:247:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:249:## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:257:**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:259:**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:261:## DEC-20: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:265:**Direction.** The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No manual operator run, cell verdict, or per-cell evidence is required, and the waiver does not claim that any cell passed. The automated CI gate in §5.1 and the scripted installed-RC PTY gate in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:267:**Scope.** This waiver applies only to ACC-TUI-MANUAL and only for v1.0.0. It does not waive ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, exact-RC identity, any §5.1 or §5.2 scenario, safety checks, or any other release gate. DEC-18's screenshot-artifact waiver remains recorded; no screenshots are required for a matrix that is not run.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:269:**Qualification applicability:** REQ-QUAL-108 = ACC-TUI-STEER and ACC-TUI-A11Y remain required; ACC-TUI-MANUAL is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:271:**Disclosure.** Report ACC-TUI-MANUAL as waived by this decision, not passed and not outstanding. Preserve historical operator observations as observations only; do not promote them to cell results.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:5:The release owner accepted DEC-20: the manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in Acceptance §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell results are required or inferred. Automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory. This update changes the terminal disposition only; the release, PR, CI, and custody details in the checkpoint below remain the historical 06:18 UTC snapshot and are not refreshed here.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:17:**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires actual operator execution for xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. There are **0/15 accepted cells**. The operator's partial RC10 report says the client rendered at tested sizes except tmux inside GNOME Terminal, which could not be resized below 43×13; other results “seemed okay.” The report lacks test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes, so it does not complete any cell. Automated PTY results do not count. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal programs; the successor RC is not yet available for the matrix. Screenshots are waived by DEC-18 only; all interactive checks and per-cell verdicts remain mandatory under DEC-19. The latest public release at this checkpoint is `v1.0.0-rc.10`; the selected distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:31:**Terminal gate:** The release owner requires all 15 manual terminal cells (five environments × three sizes) on the exact installed RC. The latest verified worksheet status is 0/15 accepted cells; blank cells remain incomplete. Actual operator execution and per-cell outcomes are mandatory; automated CI or PTY results do not substitute. [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waives screenshots only. [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal applications, but the manual matrix remains outstanding. This 04:23 snapshot predates DEC-20 and is superseded by the current checkpoint above.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:61:Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Held-out/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider and standalone coverage, successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:75:**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed or qualification run. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; the final installed RC does not exist. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, provider and standalone coverage, cross-runner reproducibility, human terminal evidence, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:105:**Qualification and publication:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Held-out T2/T3/T4, remaining live-provider and standalone gates, successor-RC artifact qualification, cross-runner evidence, the 15-cell human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; stable publication remains gated on these mandatory checks.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:252:**Terminal observation and acceptance:** The user reports that the client rendered at the sizes they tried except in tmux inside GNOME Terminal; the smallest observed tmux window was 43×13. They said the remaining observations may take several days. No screenshots, exact installed-package identity, or cell-by-cell results were supplied. The 15-cell worksheet therefore remains 0/15 and unaccepted; the report is retained as provisional operator context only. Do not prompt while other gates can progress.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:264:**Current convergence PRs:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264), head `73bdc7d91b1b8925b522b052d89228d99bad4893` on base `2622663313132864677cfdc93c94944d26a3ac06`, has independent ACCEPT; Node 22, Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while its Linux package job remains in progress. It records scripted terminal evidence only and does not complete the manual terminal gate. PR [#266](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/266), head `11fc29ba39bc76624c55d34a1fc12b4d7544522a` on the same prior base, has Node 24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passing; its Node 22 TUI test failure is being rerun, currently in progress. PR [#267](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/267), head `d0cac8b959e3da8595a41651a60a2fcd3738d034` on current base `14a9c15`, carries the malformed credential-origin fix. Its exact two-file diff has independent ACCEPT (SHA-256 `2da500d09522bc059f63b07251953c552ac2270168c72d43920b181e44fd89d3`) and the focused provider connection suite passed 37/37 after rebase; its Node 22 and Node 24 jobs are running and CodeQL passed. None of these PRs is integrated yet. PR #265 merged at `14a9c152`; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed. Its OpenRouter evidence covers one pinned-model verification and one synthetic small task, not full provider or standalone qualification.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:266:**RC10 artifact boundary:** The latest published prerelease is [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10), built from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, not current main. Its Linux archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. Previously completed RC10 artifact, installation, provenance and cross-runner checks apply only to that immutable artifact. Scripted terminal coverage remains partial; the required manual real-terminal matrix is 0/15. No exact-RC acceptance is established. Further source changes require constructing and qualifying a new candidate.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:268:**Held-out and human gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open with no custodian acceptance recorded; no held-out payload was accessed and T2/T3/T4 acceptance is not established. The manual terminal matrix still requires operator evidence across five environments and three sizes. At 2026-10-27 03:49 UTC, I verified over SSH to `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`) that `/home/mike/nexus-rc10-manual-evidence/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md` exists and contains an unfilled 15-cell template with directories for every environment/size pair. No cell evidence is present; the installed candidate identity is blank. Any matrix run must use the eventual installed RC. Scripted PTY output is not a substitute.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:326:**Terminal environment preparation:** A strict known-host SSH connection to the configured Ubuntu/GNOME desktop succeeded. Read-only inventory found xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1; an active GNOME Wayland session is present. This is environment availability only. No manual terminal cell was run, no screenshot was captured, and the §5.3 matrix remains **0/15**. It still requires each of the five terminals at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60, with approval-panel and post-exit screenshots for every cell and genuine operator verdicts.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:328:**Acceptance and remaining gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest public metadata-only custody request at 12:18 UTC has no custodian response. Private custody acceptance and evaluator-compatible sealed corpus readiness remain unestablished; no held-out payload was accessed or run. PR [#256](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/256) remains open at c3bb2235, based on b73b6ec; it needs refresh onto ff349383 after remediation. Exact-head CI run [40338957629](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957629) failed on both Node 22 and Node 24 at `npm --prefix cli test`; CodeQL [40338957381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40338957381) passed on the old candidate. This failure is on PR head c3bb2235 based on b73b6ec, not current main; refresh after remediation before using CI as evidence. A local, unpushed commit 8655ca87 fixes request-correlated local-setup cancellation (focused Node 34/34, Rust 4/4, build and diff checks passed), but the independent rereview recorded other unresolved credential/configuration findings; it is not integrated or accepted. T2/T3/T4, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, exact-candidate reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no stable v1.0.0 release exists. Publication authority remains granted and gated by acceptance.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:421:**Remaining qualification and disposition:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public update is the coordinator request from 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no custodian response or new custody acceptance. Held-out qualification has not started. Provider/standalone qualification remains incomplete, including OpenRouter; T2/T3/T4 qualification remains incomplete; the five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; RC7 is unaccepted and no stable `v1.0.0` release is published. Publication authorization remains granted and gated on all required acceptance evidence.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:431:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest comment is coordinator-authored at 2026-10-25 06:51 UTC, with no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible held-out corpus disposition. Held-out T2 has not started, and no private payload was accessed. Provider/standalone qualification and T3/T4 evidence remain incomplete. The five-environment by three-size manual terminal matrix remains 0/15, with no per-cell verdicts or required screenshots. The `cli/src/agent.ts` remediation handoff remains with KimiCode-defect-scan; implementation is still pending in that claimed lane.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:445:**Qualification and human evidence:** Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; the latest status has no independent custodian acceptance or evaluator-compatible corpus disposition. No held-out qualification is evidenced. The Ubuntu/GNOME terminal host is now connected and its five requested terminal applications were found in a setup-only preflight; the worksheet still has all 15 cells blank, no exact RC is installed there, and no screenshot evidence exists. The five-environment by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; independent exact-RC acceptance and stable-release gates are incomplete.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:447:**Next evidence:** Finish the RC7 Release workflow and verify its exact artifact identity and provenance. Finish exact-head CI for PRs #243–245, integrate only after required review and checks, and requalify resulting main before constructing a subsequent candidate. The `cli/src/agent.ts` defect-remediation handoff is recorded for KimiCode-defect-scan; its implementation is not yet present in that branch. Resolve independent held-out custody and evaluator compatibility before beginning protected qualification; then qualify an eligible installed RC and complete the manual terminal matrix. Keep source gates, RC construction, installed-RC qualification, and stable-release checks distinct.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:505:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` was `fa16045a6351ce61763bc3fcc93b562c50849285`, the merge of PR #152. PR #152 carried the readiness checkpoint refresh and terminal worksheet wording separating the §5.3 disposition gate from `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`; its exact head `deaf56fdb074df3f5cd3b62d50f811a2f14ca101` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 package/repro/install-smoke CI in run `39881805268`; CodeQL `39881805274` passed. The independent reviewer accepted that exact head. Post-merge CI run `39885102002` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/smoke/install; post-merge CodeQL `39885101945` passed. These checks are bound to exact main `fa16045`. Retained post-merge check summary: [CI and CodeQL result](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/post-merge-ci-main-fa16045.txt).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:586:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:720:| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:741:5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:758:- Ubuntu/GNOME is reachable and has all five required terminal applications, but `gh auth status` there reports no GitHub login. The RC5 installer stopped before creating files; the version-scoped desktop install prefix is absent. The manual terminal matrix is **0/15**.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:763:- The installed-package startup PTY smoke reached the Nexus prompt under isolated HOME. This does not satisfy the §5.2 scripted PTY set or the §5.3 human matrix. An attempted legacy §5.2 driver was invalid: its checkout-layout paths and wait condition do not match the current RC startup/trust prompt; its mock gateway recorded zero requests. No product pass/fail was inferred.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:775:| Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:789:- **Qualification and release:** Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`. The installed-RC evidence remains tied to RC10, not this source revision. Held-out custody and evaluator compatibility are unresolved; no protected payload was accessed or run. The manual real-terminal matrix remains 0/15, with two screenshots and human verdicts required per cell. Current exact-RC provider, standalone, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner and independent acceptance are not established. Stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated by acceptance.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/README.md:5:**Historical verdict: v1.0.0 readiness was BLOCKED at the 2026-10-16 source-suite checkpoint.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. At that checkpoint, held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remained incomplete. For v1.0.0, the manual matrix was later waived by DEC-20; see [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for the current disposition and remaining gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | Automated CI and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual real-terminal matrix is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.2 | TEST (PTY suites in CI) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.2; manual matrix disposition: DEC-20 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:1:# Manual real-terminal acceptance worksheet\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:3:For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3).\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:76:§5.3 matrix disposition: WAIVED for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. Optional observations do not change that disposition.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:80:This worksheet records manual terminal evidence only. It does not replace the separate CI PTY, installed-RC, or independent acceptance gates in `ACCEPTANCE.md`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/rc9_artifact_install.md:40:This records artifact identity, published checksums, provenance verification results, and an installed-package version/self-test. It does not establish provider behavior, upgrade behavior from RC6, held-out results, standalone engineering correctness, T3/T4 results, cross-runner reproducibility, the manual terminal matrix, or independent RC acceptance. Acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:36:| 12 | Manual terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-20](../DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver); no manual cells or per-cell evidence are required or implied. Automated CI PTY (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) remain mandatory and must pass. | ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.3; DEC-20 | RC build |\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:184:- **DEC-02** is resolved: the REPL stays a supported secondary surface, so §5.3 is required.\norigin/main:docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:83:8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal acceptance.** Automated CI checks in ACCEPTANCE §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 are mandatory. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-20](../DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver); no operator runs or cell results are required or implied. Screenshot artifacts are separately waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) is superseded for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_releases_v1_0_0-rc_6_md/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.3_terminal_installed-identity-20261024T0133Z/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1-qualification_rc.7_terminal-matrix/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/REDACTED.md/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_reviews_evidence_v1_qualification_rc10_terminal_scripted/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_release-tools_package-lock.json/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_release-tools_package.json/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_terminal-acceptance_run-cell.sh/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_terminal-acceptance_summarize.mjs/owner.json\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_terminal-acceptance_t