{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:55:20.859Z","ordinal":492858,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a18894-e451-7fe2-b11c-0a0394ebbc6f","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-dade8136-5c04-40ae-9dd3-a19a999dc5d8","process_id":"41814","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json -print0 | xargs -0 rg -n -i 'rc.11|release note|docs/releases|READINESS.md' | head -n 100; git show origin/main:docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md | sed -n '1,75p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | sed -n '240,273p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json -print0 | xargs -0 rg -n -i 'rc.11|release note|docs/releases|READINESS.md' | head -n 100; git show origin/main:docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md | sed -n '1,75p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | sed -n '240,273p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":".git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json:9:  \"scope\": \"Reconcile docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md with current main, DEC-20 manual §5.3 waiver, mandatory §5.1/§5.2 PTY gates, and exact live CI/PR state; no source or qualification changes\",\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_releases_v1_0_0-rc_6_md/owner.json:5:  \"file\": \"docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.6.md\",\n.git/nexus-claims/RELEASE_PUBLISHER/owner.json:74:  \"rc9_review\": \"Independent ACCEPT by rc5_candidate_review on exact diff a421f209015253ce7c574d675e06abbeb1028319a1a88d81c4e72570aef591b8; all package versions rc9; release notes accurate; Node>=22 retained.\",\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.11 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest. No successor-RC qualification has been run yet.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It is a version-only candidate built from current `main`; it contains the post-RC10 source changes below.\n\n## Changes since RC10\n\n### Durable operations\n\n- **Test-first work units (opt-in):** `NEXUS_TDD=1` (or `AgentWorkUnitExecutor({ tdd: true })`) runs implementer units as a RED turn that must record a failing, executed verifier and a changed test, then a GREEN turn. RED evidence is a private sidecar keyed by the unit task and prompt; the verifier baseline is rebased only onto the added tests, and a RED that narrows the operator's tests or verifier is refused. See `docs/v1.0.0/TDD-WORK-UNITS.md`.\n- **Read-only operation view:** `nexus operation status --dag [--json]` and `nexus operation watch` project the unit DAG, resource eligibility, open decisions and the event tail without taking the operation lock or writing a transition. Operation text is sanitised for terminal control sequences. See `docs/v1.1.0/OPERATION_OBSERVABILITY.md`.\n- **Git-aware isolated operations (opt-in):** `spec.git = { isolate: true, baseRef? }` gives each unit its own worktree and branch, integrates completions into an operation branch with receipts, re-verifies the merged tree, and blocks with `MERGE_CONFLICT` / `INTEGRATION_FAILED` decisions. Recovery is idempotent and fails closed when integration history is missing or rewritten. See `docs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md`.\n- **Per-unit context budget and checkpoints:** `units[].contextBudget` blocks a unit before inference when the operator's cap is the binding limit and offers to lift it; `nexus operation checkpoint|checkpoints|restore` snapshots a unit's task state and conversation journals as a hash-verified bundle, with a pre-restore backup. See `docs/v1.1.0/CONTEXT_MANAGEMENT.md`.\n- **Operation policy configuration:** durable operation policy defaults can be set in the operator config; scheduler and runner internals were split (scheduler extraction, runner decomposition) with bounded diagnostics, and recovered merged operations now require verification evidence.\n\n### Reliability and security\n\n- Checkpoint restore is fail-closed on content mismatch; incomplete or duplicate checkpoint bundles are reused/cleaned correctly, and restoring a conversation removes stale journals.\n- Configured Git hooks are guarded consistently for checkpoint and retention operations, including a fail-closed race path.\n- Malformed operator configuration is reported by `nexus doctor` with recovery guidance instead of an unhandled failure.\n- Clean-checkout build identity is recorded correctly, and packaged smoke startup no longer races its log.\n- CLI terminal output sanitises control characters in corrupt-resume errors; batch read paths preserve lossy UTF-8 and propagate read errors instead of continuing.\n- Credential handling: malformed credential origins can no longer be rebound, and credential-store writes are failure-atomic under the file guard.\n- Recovery: pre-fix worktree tasks are recovered from the repository root, and upgrades recover state from the configured state directory.\n- Tooling: `update_plan` no longer mutates the workspace, and ambiguous Python verifier imports are rejected.\n- CI provisions the pinned evaluator toolchains for the qualification suites.\n\n### Release records\n\n- Readiness, terminal and qualification records were refreshed through 2026-10-29. The manual real-terminal matrix is **required** for v1.0.0; the earlier matrix-waiver record was withdrawn (DEC-19). Screenshot artifacts alone are waived (DEC-18).\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.11` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n\n## Qualification status\n\nThis is a candidate, not an accepted release. The installed-RC gates — platform and lifecycle evidence, the fifteen-cell manual terminal matrix, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — remain outstanding for this artifact. Passing source CI does not satisfy them.\n\n## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\n\n**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\n\n**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\n\n**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\n\n## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n\n**Status: withdrawn.** The waiver described in this decision is not in effect.\n\n**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n\n**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n\n**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n\n**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n\n## DEC-20: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n\n**Status: accepted by the release owner, 2026-10-29.** This decision supersedes DEC-19 for v1.0.0.\n\n**Direction.** The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No manual operator run, cell verdict, or per-cell evidence is required, and the waiver does not claim that any cell passed. The automated CI gate in §5.1 and the scripted installed-RC PTY gate in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n\n**Scope.** This waiver applies only to ACC-TUI-MANUAL and only for v1.0.0. It does not waive ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, exact-RC identity, any §5.1 or §5.2 scenario, safety checks, or any other release gate. DEC-18's screenshot-artifact waiver remains recorded; no screenshots are required for a matrix that is not run.\n\n**Qualification applicability:** REQ-QUAL-108 = ACC-TUI-STEER and ACC-TUI-A11Y remain required; ACC-TUI-MANUAL is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n\n**Disclosure.** Report ACC-TUI-MANUAL as waived by this decision, not passed and not outstanding. Preserve historical operator observations as observations only; do not promote them to cell results.\n\n**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §§1.1, 3.1, 5, and 10; REQ-QUAL-108 exact-RC evidence mapping; stable v1.0.0 release notes; READINESS; terminal-matrix worksheet disposition.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27967}},"started_at_ms":1793292920859,"completed_at_ms":1793292920859}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T16:55:22.116Z","ordinal":492859,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18896-6d03-7440-814b-51a2070edb5d","call_id":"call_ef0debfd2f0a4355a11cb0c7163f0b62","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":".git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_v1.0.0_READINESS.md/owner.json:9:  \"scope\": \"Reconcile docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md with current main, DEC-20 manual §5.3 waiver, mandatory §5.1/§5.2 PTY gates, and exact live CI/PR state; no source or qualification changes\",\n.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_releases_v1_0_0-rc_6_md/owner.json:5:  \"file\": \"docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.6.md\",\n.git/nexus-claims/RELEASE_PUBLISHER/owner.json:74:  \"rc9_review\": \"Independent ACCEPT by rc5_candidate_review on exact diff a421f209015253ce7c574d675e06abbeb1028319a1a88d81c4e72570aef591b8; all package versions rc9; release notes accurate; Node>=22 retained.\",\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0-rc.11 release candidate\n\n**Maturity:** release candidate; prerelease, not stable.\n\n**Status:** this candidate is for exact-artifact qualification. It does not establish independent acceptance or authorize stable v1.0.0 promotion. Qualification results must identify the workflow-produced package and its digest. No successor-RC qualification has been run yet.\n\nThis release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and sidecar, production Node dependencies, Rust `harness-core`, and Ratatui `nexus-tui`. It is a version-only candidate built from current `main`; it contains the post-RC10 source changes below.\n\n## Changes since RC10\n\n### Durable operations\n\n- **Test-first work units (opt-in):** `NEXUS_TDD=1` (or `AgentWorkUnitExecutor({ tdd: true })`) runs implementer units as a RED turn that must record a failing, executed verifier and a changed test, then a GREEN turn. RED evidence is a private sidecar keyed by the unit task and prompt; the verifier baseline is rebased only onto the added tests, and a RED that narrows the operator's tests or verifier is refused. See `docs/v1.0.0/TDD-WORK-UNITS.md`.\n- **Read-only operation view:** `nexus operation status --dag [--json]` and `nexus operation watch` project the unit DAG, resource eligibility, open decisions and the event tail without taking the operation lock or writing a transition. Operation text is sanitised for terminal control sequences. See `docs/v1.1.0/OPERATION_OBSERVABILITY.md`.\n- **Git-aware isolated operations (opt-in):** `spec.git = { isolate: true, baseRef? }` gives each unit its own worktree and branch, integrates completions into an operation branch with receipts, re-verifies the merged tree, and blocks with `MERGE_CONFLICT` / `INTEGRATION_FAILED` decisions. Recovery is idempotent and fails closed when integration history is missing or rewritten. See `docs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md`.\n- **Per-unit context budget and checkpoints:** `units[].contextBudget` blocks a unit before inference when the operator's cap is the binding limit and offers to lift it; `nexus operation checkpoint|checkpoints|restore` snapshots a unit's task state and conversation journals as a hash-verified bundle, with a pre-restore backup. See `docs/v1.1.0/CONTEXT_MANAGEMENT.md`.\n- **Operation policy configuration:** durable operation policy defaults can be set in the operator config; scheduler and runner internals were split (scheduler extraction, runner decomposition) with bounded diagnostics, and recovered merged operations now require verification evidence.\n\n### Reliability and security\n\n- Checkpoint restore is fail-closed on content mismatch; incomplete or duplicate checkpoint bundles are reused/cleaned correctly, and restoring a conversation removes stale journals.\n- Configured Git hooks are guarded consistently for checkpoint and retention operations, including a fail-closed race path.\n- Malformed operator configuration is reported by `nexus doctor` with recovery guidance instead of an unhandled failure.\n- Clean-checkout build identity is recorded correctly, and packaged smoke startup no longer races its log.\n- CLI terminal output sanitises control characters in corrupt-resume errors; batch read paths preserve lossy UTF-8 and propagate read errors instead of continuing.\n- Credential handling: malformed credential origins can no longer be rebound, and credential-store writes are failure-atomic under the file guard.\n- Recovery: pre-fix worktree tasks are recovered from the repository root, and upgrades recover state from the configured state directory.\n- Tooling: `update_plan` no longer mutates the workspace, and ambiguous Python verifier imports are rejected.\n- CI provisions the pinned evaluator toolchains for the qualification suites.\n\n### Release records\n\n- Readiness, terminal and qualification records were refreshed through 2026-10-29. The manual real-terminal matrix is **required** for v1.0.0; the earlier matrix-waiver record was withdrawn (DEC-19). Screenshot artifacts alone are waived (DEC-18).\n\n## Runtime requirements\n\n- Linux x86-64 with glibc 2.35 or newer.\n- Node.js 22 or newer.\n- An OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint, local or explicitly selected provider.\n\nThe archive does not include Node.js. Rust and Cargo are not required at runtime. No other OS or architecture is claimed.\n\n## Candidate assets\n\nThe release workflow for `v1.0.0-rc.11` is expected to produce the version-matched Linux archive, `SHA256SUMS`, SBOM, notices, installer, and provenance. The workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and qualification evidence must be recorded before this candidate can be accepted. Local builds are not interchangeable with the workflow-produced artifacts.\n\n## Qualification status\n\nThis is a candidate, not an accepted release. The installed-RC gates — platform and lifecycle evidence, the fifteen-cell manual terminal matrix, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — remain outstanding for this artifact. Passing source CI does not satisfy them.\n\n## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\n\n**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\n\n**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\n\n**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\n\n## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n\n**Status: withdrawn.** The waiver described in this decision is not in effect.\n\n**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n\n**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n\n**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n\n**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n\n## DEC-20: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n\n**Status: accepted by the release owner, 2026-10-29.** This decision supersedes DEC-19 for v1.0.0.\n\n**Direction.** The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No manual operator run, cell verdict, or per-cell evidence is required, and the waiver does not claim that any cell passed. The automated CI gate in §5.1 and the scripted installed-RC PTY gate in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n\n**Scope.** This waiver applies only to ACC-TUI-MANUAL and only for v1.0.0. It does not waive ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, exact-RC identity, any §5.1 or §5.2 scenario, safety checks, or any other release gate. DEC-18's screenshot-artifact waiver remains recorded; no screenshots are required for a matrix that is not run.\n\n**Qualification applicability:** REQ-QUAL-108 = ACC-TUI-STEER and ACC-TUI-A11Y remain required; ACC-TUI-MANUAL is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n\n**Disclosure.** Report ACC-TUI-MANUAL as waived by this decision, not passed and not outstanding. Preserve historical operator observations as observations only; do not promote them to cell results.\n\n**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §§1.1, 3.1, 5, and 10; REQ-QUAL-108 exact-RC evidence mapping; stable v1.0.0 release notes; READINESS; terminal-matrix worksheet disposition.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18894-e451-7fe2-b11c-0a0394ebbc6f","create_time":1793292922.1159484}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
