\\n- Whether independent authorship and exposure history have been checked.\\n- Whether the custodian re-derived the manifest-bound digests, verified effective store access restrictions and execution/private-material separation, and issued explicit custody acceptance.\\n- The exact public manifest identity and next checkpoint.\\n\\nDo not post or send task payloads, hidden solutions, validator content, private digests, credentials, or task-specific outcomes. Qualification remains stopped until complete custody acceptance is recorded; T3’s reported 8/8 metadata checks do not establish corpus task-quality acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T06:02:22Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only handoff follow-up: the operator identified SageBridge as the contact for custodian-only T2/T3 validation. Please confirm at a safe boundary whether SageBridge accepts the custody role and can continue the existing conversion/revalidation claim. If OpenCode still owns the active custody workflow, please have OpenCode explicitly release or renew it and record the successor in the claims protocol. Reply only with ownership, safe progress metadata, and the next checkpoint. Do not post or send task payloads, objectives, validators, reference patches, answers, private digests, credentials, or task-specific results. Qualification remains stopped until the full successor corpus has independent custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T06:54:11Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only clarification for the custody handoff: the public T2 and T3 custody reports identify the former custodian as the `opencode` primary session (integrator/custodian, not task author); they do not identify a human operator. The handoff log later names SageBridge, but the subsequent `coordination_only` status and current claim file leave the active custodian unclear.\\n\\nThe remaining custodian-only work is to complete or replace the successor corpus at 40 tasks