{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:09:11.377Z","ordinal":493306,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1889d-bec2-7bc0-bdf5-e197ccf19111","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae37db55e8c81a09169a93a33437222","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The §5.3 manual terminal matrix is **waived for v1.0.0**—it is neither passed nor outstanding. The automated CI PTY gate (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY gate (§5.2) remain mandatory. This matches DEC-20 on `origin/main` at `7fad87d`.\n\nMain’s exact-head CI, including §5.1, passed. PR #327 updates the RC11 release notes to match DEC-20; it is independently reviewed and its Node 22/24 and Entire checks are still pending. PR #318’s checks are also pending. PR #325’s CI passed, but its Entire gate failed because no reviewer formally approved its trail; I’ve asked the independent reviewer to resolve that and PR #327’s approval gate.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. No exact-RC acceptance or stable release is claimed.\n\nOperational note: Claude memory capture is unavailable: “Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.”\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":731,"lineEnd":764,"note":"release gate context; exact-RC acceptance remains separate from green source CI"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1793293749502,"completed_at_ms":1793293751377}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:09:11.438Z","ordinal":493307,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae37db55e8c81a09169a93a33437222","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The §5.3 manual terminal matrix is **waived for v1.0.0**—it is neither passed nor outstanding. The automated CI PTY gate (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY gate (§5.2) remain mandatory. This matches DEC-20 on `origin/main` at `7fad87d`.\n\nMain’s exact-head CI, including §5.1, passed. PR #327 updates the RC11 release notes to match DEC-20; it is independently reviewed and its Node 22/24 and Entire checks are still pending. PR #318’s checks are also pending. PR #325’s CI passed, but its Entire gate failed because no reviewer formally approved its trail; I’ve asked the independent reviewer to resolve that and PR #327’s approval gate.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. No exact-RC acceptance or stable release is claimed.\n\nOperational note: Claude memory capture is unavailable: “Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.”\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:731-764|note=[release gate context; exact-RC acceptance remains separate from green source CI]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1889d-bec2-7bc0-bdf5-e197ccf19111","create_time":1793293749.4628947,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae37db55e8c81a09169a93a33437222","turn_id":"01a1889d-bec2-7bc0-bdf5-e197ccf19111","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a188a3-148d-78a2-9bbf-98beccd79251","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23080}}
