{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:21:14.201Z","ordinal":493732,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188a4-0127-7a81-8e81-27e7b0f92787","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae38087a54481a09c1c93a31da98ded","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The §5.3 manual 5×3 terminal matrix is **waived for v1.0.0** under DEC-20. It is recorded as waived, not passed. The §5.1 CI PTY and §5.2 scripted installed-RC PTY gates remain mandatory.\n\n**Current evidence**\n\n- `origin/main` is `7fad87d`; its exact CI run `40910552951` passed on Node 22, Node 24, and Linux, including §5.1.\n- PR #327 updates the RC11 notes to match DEC-20. Node 22 and 24 pass; Linux and Entire checks are still pending.\n- PR #318’s exact CI failed on both Node versions: the compiler-exposure scan timed out and correctly failed closed. A separate Codex process had an uncommitted scanner change in the claimed worktree; I left it untouched while its test run was active.\n- PR #325’s CI passes, but its Entire gate lacks an approval from a reviewer distinct from the PR author.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. RC-specific §5.2 qualification and other exact-RC gates are still outstanding; no accepted RC or stable release is claimed.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":731,"lineEnd":764,"note":"release qualification distinguishes source CI from exact-RC acceptance"}],"rolloutIds":["01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0"]}},"started_at_ms":1793294471669,"completed_at_ms":1793294474201}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:21:14.206Z","ordinal":493733,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","status":"completed","id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae38087a54481a09c1c93a31da98ded","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The §5.3 manual 5×3 terminal matrix is **waived for v1.0.0** under DEC-20. It is recorded as waived, not passed. The §5.1 CI PTY and §5.2 scripted installed-RC PTY gates remain mandatory.\n\n**Current evidence**\n\n- `origin/main` is `7fad87d`; its exact CI run `40910552951` passed on Node 22, Node 24, and Linux, including §5.1.\n- PR #327 updates the RC11 notes to match DEC-20. Node 22 and 24 pass; Linux and Entire checks are still pending.\n- PR #318’s exact CI failed on both Node versions: the compiler-exposure scan timed out and correctly failed closed. A separate Codex process had an uncommitted scanner change in the claimed worktree; I left it untouched while its test run was active.\n- PR #325’s CI passes, but its Entire gate lacks an approval from a reviewer distinct from the PR author.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. RC-specific §5.2 qualification and other exact-RC gates are still outstanding; no accepted RC or stable release is claimed.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:731-764|note=[release qualification distinguishes source CI from exact-RC acceptance]\n</citation_entries>\n<rollout_ids>\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n</rollout_ids>\n</oai-mem-citation>","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a188a4-0127-7a81-8e81-27e7b0f92787","create_time":1793294471.6476476,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae38087a54481a09c1c93a31da98ded","turn_id":"01a188a4-0127-7a81-8e81-27e7b0f92787","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a188ae-1bdd-73b2-b635-1a58193b424a","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23090}}
