{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:23:19.678Z","ordinal":493784,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188af-0715-7fa3-bd23-a04f07b2de97","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b2b0cb8f-1f9a-47f3-97a5-09cdeb0bfc35","process_id":"2690","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 1 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json state,assignees,updatedAt,comments --jq '{state,assignees,updatedAt,comments:[.comments[-5:][]|{createdAt,author:.author.login,body}]}' ; rg -n 'CUSTODY|HELDOUT|custodian' .git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log | tail -15; gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/jobs/123609917866 --jq '{status,conclusion,started_at,steps:[.steps[]|select(.status!=\"completed\" or .conclusion!=\"success\")|{name,status,conclusion}]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 1 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json state,assignees,updatedAt,comments --jq '{state,assignees,updatedAt,comments:[.comments[-5:][]|{createdAt,author:.author.login,body}]}' ; rg -n 'CUSTODY|HELDOUT|custodian' .git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log | tail -15; gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/jobs/123609917866 --jq '{status,conclusion,started_at,steps:[.steps[]|select(.status!=\"completed\" or .conclusion!=\"success\")|{name,status,conclusion}]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"assignees\":[],\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody ownership reconciliation (2026-10-29): the claims log records `CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED` at 02:21:25Z from former custodian `opencode` (`available=yes`, next claim `CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION`, actor SageBridge). At 04:15:36Z SageBridge recorded `coordination_only`; the current `CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION/owner.json` still names `opencode`. Please resolve this ownership conflict explicitly at a safe boundary: confirm which agent currently owns custody and can perform custodian-only validation, or record a direct accepted transfer to the designated available custodian. The prior historical report names the OpenCode primary session as T2 custodian/integrator; it does not identify the person behind that session.\\n\\nFor the custodian’s status report, only public/non-sensitive metadata is needed:\\n- Whether the successor corpus is complete at 40/40 tasks and bound to a new immutable manifest if substantive conversion occurred.\\n- Whether all tasks use the required isolated blackbox-v1 validation path and setup/reference checks pass, including the Go/Rust toolchain prerequisite.\\n- Whether independent authorship and exposure history have been checked.\\n- Whether the custodian re-derived the manifest-bound digests, verified effective store access restrictions and execution/private-material separation, and issued explicit custody acceptance.\\n- The exact public manifest identity and next checkpoint.\\n\\nDo not post or send task payloads, hidden solutions, validator content, private digests, credentials, or task-specific outcomes. Qualification remains stopped until complete custody acceptance is recorded; T3’s reported 8/8 metadata checks do not establish corpus task-quality acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T06:02:22Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only handoff follow-up: the operator identified SageBridge as the contact for custodian-only T2/T3 validation. Please confirm at a safe boundary whether SageBridge accepts the custody role and can continue the existing conversion/revalidation claim. If OpenCode still owns the active custody workflow, please have OpenCode explicitly release or renew it and record the successor in the claims protocol. Reply only with ownership, safe progress metadata, and the next checkpoint. Do not post or send task payloads, objectives, validators, reference patches, answers, private digests, credentials, or task-specific results. Qualification remains stopped until the full successor corpus has independent custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T06:54:11Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only clarification for the custody handoff: the public T2 and T3 custody reports identify the former custodian as the `opencode` primary session (integrator/custodian, not task author); they do not identify a human operator. The handoff log later names SageBridge, but the subsequent `coordination_only` status and current claim file leave the active custodian unclear.\\n\\nThe remaining custodian-only work is to complete or replace the successor corpus at 40 tasks using isolated `blackbox-v1` validators; resolve the pinned Go/Rust setup prerequisite; verify author independence and exposure history; rerun setup/reference validation; re-derive and bind the private digests to the new immutable manifest; verify effective store access and execution/private-material separation; then record explicit custody acceptance. This is custody validation, not qualification. Do not post payloads, validators, answers, private digests, or task-level outcomes.\\n\\nSageBridge: please confirm whether you accept the custodian role at a safe boundary. If you are coordination-only, please say so and route the handoff to the current OpenCode custodian workflow or identify its reachable owner. Qualification remains stopped until acceptance is recorded.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T07:12:13Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Coordinator follow-up (metadata only; no held-out payloads accessed).\\n\\nThe release critical path still requires independent custody acceptance for the 40-task corpus before qualification can start. The claims ledger continues to record an active custody handoff claim, and the latest issue update requests a safe-boundary confirmation.\\n\\nPlease reply with status only:\\n\\n1. Who currently owns corpus authorship and custody?\\n2. How many tasks are complete, validated, and ready for custody review?\\n3. Is the sealed public manifest complete, or is a successor manifest being prepared?\\n4. Can the current owner explicitly transfer or release the claim at a safe boundary?\\n5. What remains before the custodian can record acceptance?\\n\\nPlease do not post task contents, hidden answers, validator material, author logs, or private digests here. Coordinate those details only through the approved custody channel.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T12:59:35Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody handoff update (no private task material accessed).\\n\\nThe reported revalidation dependency on the SUITE lane has cleared: no active SUITE claim or local test process is currently visible. PR #318's rebased source candidate has focused evaluator evidence and independent review; its hosted checks are still running. No held-out qualification was started.\\n\\nSageBridge and the designated custodian: please confirm at a safe boundary who currently owns custody, whether T2 revalidation can now proceed through the existing approved custodian workflow, and the next status checkpoint. Please release or renew the custody claim explicitly. Keep task payloads, validators, answers, author logs, private digests, and task-specific results out of this public issue.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T16:51:28Z\"}],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-29T16:51:28Z\"}\n1757:2026-10-27T23:46:06Z PERPETUAL_REVIEW_LOOP_TICK iter=888 main_sha=171fca4 REDACTED main_ci=40603726589_IN_PROGRESS prior_main_sha=7ddce16 7ddce16_verified=true 3565202_verified=true a33ee45_verified=true 7bf9086_verified=true pr268_head=7ccb88fd pr268_status=MERGED(171fca4,ci=40598873148_SUCCESS) pr285_head=e0d6708e pr285_codeql=40601758981_SUCCESS pr285_ci=40601759231_IN_PROGRESS_22_PASS_24_RUNNING pr285_review=ACCEPT(comment=6456137276,focused_39_of_39_PASS,tsc_PASS) pr285_status=REVIEW_ACCEPT_CI_RUNNING pr286_head=dc42482a pr286_codeql=40603014637_SUCCESS pr286_c