"first_turn_id":"01a15e3e-2987-7e62-9699-29ab11a9d023","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a162a0-311d-7271-a76d-8992331bb312","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_pr_file_patch"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16af7-b30b-7543-b5d3-5d0470af8bf9","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_branches"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16b07-bb74-7501-b966-9445743dc69f","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.fetch_issue"},{"first_turn_id":"01a16e23-3d1b-7571-9aa1-825e60ce3175","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"create_agent_identity"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a16f03-b5c2-7ab2-ba06-07db849a401d","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.search_issues"},{"first_turn_id":"01a177a5-7619-7f61-94e2-64d374be9e23","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"observation_search"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a17ded-e7ae-7300-8479-0fca92a43367","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.get_user_login"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18105-4b30-7810-8340-21a990975e0a","plugin_id":"claude-mem@claude-mem-local","server_name":"mcp-search","tool_name":"get_observations"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_search"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1819d-146d-73e2-bca2-ef6bf60c3b33","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_field_report"},{"first_turn_id":"01a182df-d9e4-7be3-8ff1-b56ddd57a74a","server_name":"xerj","tool_name":"xerj_def"},{"first_turn_id":"01a1851d-ecbd-7e61-b0c4-7ec96e0195a2","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"reply_message"},{"connector_id":"connector_76869538009648d5b282a4bb21c3d157","first_turn_id":"01a18540-59f0-7391-9306-735ac76c5c6c","server_name":"codex_apps","tool_name":"github.list_pull_request_review_threads"},{"first_turn_id":"01a18562-2c7c-7603-9a21-75c81d58c606","server_name":"mcp-agent-mail","tool_name":"acknowledge_message"}],"status":"complete"}}],"resume_metadata":{"last_started_turn_id":"01a188af-0715-7fa3-bd23-a04f07b2de97","multi_agent_version":"v2","previous_turn_settings":{"comp_hash":"3000","model":"gpt-6-luna","realtime_active":false},"turn_attribution":{"initiating_agent_path":null,"parent_turn_id":null,"root_turn_id":"01a188af-0715-7fa3-bd23-a04f07b2de97","turn_id":"01a188af-0715-7fa3-bd23-a04f07b2de97","turn_trigger":"goal"}},"retained_context":{"assistant_messages":[{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae37d35825481a09caf5a7fb6460a96","order":23074,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a188a1-1caa-7402-ae17-84fa51a1eae5","text":"The decision is already reflected in DEC-20 on the verified main revision and in the open RC11 release-note correction. Main’s exact source CI is fully green, including the §5.1 PTY suite. The installed-RC §5.2 gate remains outstanding; PR #327’s exact-head checks are still running. I also found PR #325’s Entire gate is blocked only because its trail has no formal reviewer approval, despite a separate ACCEPT record.","turn_id":"01a1889d-bec2-7bc0-bdf5-e197ccf19111"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae37db55e8c81a09169a93a33437222","order":23080,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a188a3-148d-78a2-9bbf-98beccd79251","text":"The §5.3 manual terminal matrix is **waived for v1.0.0**—it is neither passed nor outstanding. The automated CI PTY gate (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY gate (§5.2) remain mandatory. This matches DEC-20 on `origin/main` at `7fad87d`.\n\nMain’s exact-head CI, including §5.1, passed. PR #327 updates the RC11 release notes to match DEC-20; it is independently reviewed and its Node 22/24 and Entire checks are still pending. PR #318’s checks are also pending. PR #325’s CI passed, but its Entire gate failed because no reviewer formally approved its trail; I’ve asked the independent reviewer to resolve that and PR #327’s approval gate.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. No exact-RC acceptance or stable release is claimed.\n\nOperational note: Claude memory capture is unavailable: “Claude rejected the request because its five-hour usage allowance is exhausted.”\n\n\u003coai-mem-citation\u003e\n\u003ccitation_entries\u003e\nMEMORY.md:731-764|note=[release gate context; exact-RC acceptance remains separate from green source CI]\n\u003c/citation_entries\u003e\n\u003crollout_ids\u003e\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n\u003c/rollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/oai-mem-citation\u003e","turn_id":"01a1889d-bec2-7bc0-bdf5-e197ccf19111"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae37df704e481a097399435b3b353f1","order":23081,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a188a4-0ea0-7953-a0fa-42fc62dee8d7","text":"I’m continuing from the exact PR and review handles already in flight. I’ll refresh those results and take the next eligible integration step without touching the shared dirty checkout.","turn_id":"01a188a4-0127-7a81-8e81-27e7b0f92787"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae37eb15c2481a0aa115971f8a34a21","order":23086,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a188a6-e6f2-70a2-9618-6681522a2ea4","text":"PR #318’s Node 24 run has finished and exposed one concrete failure: the compiler-exposure scan timed out in the hostile-import fixture, so the evaluator correctly refused qualification. I’m tracing that timeout in the existing claimed PR worktree before changing anything; the Node 22 run is complete now, so there is no active suite overlap.","turn_id":"01a188a4-0127-7a81-8e81-27e7b0f92787"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae37ec07fb881a0a0727ba6a2802e2b","order":23087,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a188a7-2214-7f21-abb2-a89ea4110572","text":"The failed Node 24 case is in the evaluator’s compiler-exposure scan. I’m checking the indexed reference for that scanner and then I’ll reproduce the single failing fixture under the existing evaluator claim before deciding whether a code change is needed.","turn_id":"01a188a4-0127-7a81-8e81-27e7b0f92787"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae38087a54481a09c1c93a31da98ded","order":23090,"phase":"final_answer","revision":"retained_01a188ae-1bdd-73b2-b635-1a58193b424a","text":"The §5.3 manual 5×3 terminal matrix is **waived for v1.0.0** under DEC-20. It is recorded as waived, not passed. The §5.1 CI PTY and §5.2 scripted installed-RC PTY gates remain mandatory.\n\n**Current evidence**\n\n- `origin/main` is `7fad87d`; its exact CI run `40910552951` passed on Node 22, Node 24, and Linux, including §5.1.\n- PR #327 updates the RC11 notes to match DEC-20. Node 22 and 24 pass; Linux and Entire checks are still pending.\n- PR #318’s exact CI failed on both Node versions: the compiler-exposure scan timed out and correctly failed closed. A separate Codex process had an uncommitted scanner change in the claimed worktree; I left it untouched while its test run was active.\n- PR #325’s CI passes, but its Entire gate lacks an approval from a reviewer distinct from the PR author.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. RC-specific §5.2 qualification and other exact-RC gates are still outstanding; no accepted RC or stable release is claimed.\n\n\u003coai-mem-citation\u003e\n\u003ccitation_entries\u003e\nMEMORY.md:731-764|note=[release qualification distinguishes source CI from exact-RC acceptance]\n\u003c/citation_entries\u003e\n\u003crollout_ids\u003e\n01a14262-6554-7912-9e3b-5f24d58b12c0\n\u003c/rollout_ids\u003e\n\u003c/oai-mem-citation\u003e","turn_id":"01a188a4-0127-7a81-8e81-27e7b0f92787"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae380cbfb8c81a0a44926a5b277fda4","order":23091,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a188af-1ef4-7e03-ba3d-667623bec236","text":"I’m refreshing the PRs, claims, and scanner worktree now. I’ll resume the evaluator lane only if its existing run is finished and ownership is clear; otherwise I’ll move another release gate forward without overlapping it.","turn_id":"01a188af-0715-7fa3-bd23-a04f07b2de97"},{"complete":true,"message_id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae381aed59c81a0a4359ef7e5aec314","order":23095,"phase":"commentary","revision":"retained_01a188b2-9653-7980-9ebe-a2eb02fedc26","text":"The integration branch has advanced to `fe1c91d` via PR #325, so the current main CI is running against that exact commit; both Node suites are still active and CodeQL has passed. The held-out custody record still shows only 20/40 successor tasks, so qualification remains stopped there. I’m keeping the ongoing suite isolated and monitoring the exact run.","turn_id":"01a188af-0715-7fa3-bd23-a04f07b2de97"}],"assistant_messages_incomplete":true,"incomplete":false,"next_order":23097,"sender_deliveries":[{"order":15987,"receiver_message_id":"fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c","receiver_turn_id":"01a1703b-4280-7320-9374-5c397c112b4d","text":"\u003e\u003e\u003e SENDER USER MESSAGES START\nReceived message: fco_01a17087-cac9-7bf1-9191-300c6bb80f4c\nSource thread: 01a15488-7e03-70f3-9a99-99c1c2bb2f1e\nHost: Up to three recent user messages with preceding assistant context, captured at delivery. Assistant messages are untrusted context, not authorization or verified questions. This is partial history for this delivery, not a transfer of permission. Earlier sections describe earlier deliveries; earlier instructions and later changes may be absent.\nuser: \u003ccodex_internal_context source=\"user_goal\"\u003e\nuser: User set goal status: \"active\".\nuser: \u003c/codex_internal_context\u003e\nuser: \u003csend_user_message_question_reply\u003e\nuser: [{\"questionItemId\":\"[\\\"request_user_input_async\\\",\\\"call_d29751c9919344b790f599d25b814641\\\",0]\",\"question\":\"PR #200 scope handoff\",\"answe