tual runtime scan; synthetic/local runtime only, no heldout\",\"since\":\"2026-10-29T17:20:00Z\",\"status\":\"review finding addressed; source uncommitted and under focused validation\"}\n=== /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION/owner.json\n{\"agent\":\"opencode\",\"role\":\"held-out corpus custodian (handoff accepted per claims.log CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED)\",\"branch\":null,\"worktree\":null,\"bound_manifest\":\"50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b\",\"since\":\"2026-10-29T02:24:10Z\",\"pid\":3848937,\"corpus_access\":\"custodian workflow only\",\"progress\":{\"successor_store\":\"/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-blackbox1\",\"tasks_built\":20,\"cases\":218,\"go_rust_blocked\":\"oracle sandbox exposes no Go/Rust toolchain; disposition recorded\",\"t3_acceptance\":\"PASS 8/8 digests+schema+isolation vs 85fb9caf\",\"revalidation\":\"batch waiting on SUITE (held by codex-root)\"}}\n=== decisions\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-27-4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-28-5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-29-\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:30:The final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-31-\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-32-Exact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-33-\n--\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-47-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-48-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-49-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:50:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-51-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-52-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-53-\n--\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-117-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-118-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-119-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:120:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-121-\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md-122-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ