SS_matrix22_finishing disposition=ACCEPT m5_blocker=blackbox_v1_custodian_sealing\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:1023:2026-10-26T04:05:00Z PERPETUAL_REVIEW_LOOP_TICK iter=365 main_sha=468646b pr247_head=5cec729 ci_40265422295=matrix22_matrix24_SUCCESS_packaging_active active_step=\"npm test in linux-x86_64\" disposition=ACCEPT m5_blocker=blackbox_v1_custodian_sealing\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log-1024-2026-10-26T04:09:36Z VALIDATION DEFECT_UPGRADE_BACKUP_LATENCY_20261026 candidate=1cce2f48af32633cf9b3df36aa9c37ec4c2fce6f diff_sha256=8234b6c8ce573754042f5b552fd1447194553070d5eab637c06ffb214465534c upgrade_safety=35/35 upgrade_transaction_recovery=47/47 tsc=PASS npm_build=PASS requirements_enforce=PASS sync_version=rc.7 diff_check=PASS working_tree=clean; full candidate CI pending PR after PR247 CI concludes.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:1025:2026-10-26T04:10:00Z PERPETUAL_REVIEW_LOOP_TICK iter=366 main_sha=468646b pr247_head=5cec729 ci_40265422295=packaging_job_running active_step=\"npm test in linux-x86_64 (7m)\" disposition=ACCEPT m5_blocker=blackbox_v1_custodian_sealing\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log-1026-2026-10-26T04:02:00Z FULL_SUITE_DIAGNOSTIC branch=v1/defect-provider-stream-integration head=b5b28b6 snapshot=/home/mike/nexus-wt/provider-stream-suite-b5b28b6 command='make test with isolated HOME/XDG' result='1736 tests; 1732 pass; 3 fail; 1 skipped; cargo tests passed before CLI; exit 2' failures='eval_integrity resource contract oomKills 3 expected 0; eval_version_probe_storage missing dedicated capped fixture; upgrade_tui historical bin/nexus not official release/fetch failed' classification='same three known environment/fixture classes; no provider-test failure; SUITE ownership changed mid-run so clean rerun still required; security_gates not reached after npm failure'\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log-1027-2026-10-26T04:02:00Z REVIEW_REMEDIATION branch=v1/defect-checkpoint-untracked-integration head=6c24d50 prior=889d7b1 findings='empty copied directory destination escape; ignored untracked checkout/deletion collisions' red='0/3 then 3/3' six_file='89/89' tsc=PASS spec_re_review=pending_agent-21\n## DEC-18: v1.0.0 terminal screenshot-artifact waiver\n\n**Context.** The v1.0.0 manual terminal matrix requires real interaction in five terminal environments at three sizes. The release owner waived screenshot artifacts for this release.\n\n**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\n\n**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12.\n\n## DEC-19: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n\n**Status: withdrawn.** The waiver described in this decision is not in effect.\n\n**History.** A prior revision of this decision recorded that the release owner waived the manual matrix. That record conflicted with the explicit release requirement for five terminal environments × three sizes. The waiver is withdrawn and must not be used to disposition any v1.0.0 gate.\n\n**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\n\n**Disclosure.** Do not describe the manual matrix as waived. Until all fifteen cells have verified operator evidence, ACC-TUI-MANUAL remains incomplete and v1.0.0 acceptance remains blocked.\n\n**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n\n## DEC-20: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n\n**Status: accepted by the release owner, 2026-10-29.** This decision supersedes DEC-19 for v1.0.0.\n\n**Direction.** The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No manual operator run, cell verdict, or per-cell evidence is required, and the waiver does not claim that any cell passed. The automated CI gate in §5.1 and the scripted installed-RC PTY gate in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n\n**Scope.** This waiver applies only to ACC-TUI-MANUAL and only for v1.0.0. It does not waive ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, exact-RC identity, any §5.1 or §5.2 scenario, safety checks, or any other release gate. DEC-18's screenshot-artifact waiver remains recorded; no screenshots are required for a matrix that is not run.\n\n**Qualification applicability:** REQ-QUAL-108 = ACC-TUI-STEER and ACC-TUI-A11Y remain required; ACC-TUI-MANUAL is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n\n**Disclosure.** Report ACC-TUI-MANUAL as waived by this decision, not passed and not outstanding. Preserve historical operator observations as observations only; do not promote them to cell results.\n\n**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §§1.1, 3.1, 5, and 10; REQ-QUAL-108 exact-RC evidence mapping; stable v1.0.0 release notes; READINESS; terminal-matrix worksheet disposition.\n\n## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":28181}},"started_at_ms":1793295482253,"completed_at_ms":1793295482254}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:38:03.630Z","ordinal":494387,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a188bd-82ee-7472-85b9-4f806a1c7b50","call_id":"call_232e66df9c124d2dbd0be21680728a43","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 10028)\nTotal output lines: 353\n\nWarning: truncated output (original token count: 20295)\nTotal output lines: 457\n\neval/run.mjs:165:      killGroup(\"SIGTERM\");\ncli/test/helpers/sidecar_recorder.mjs:28:for (const signal of [\"SIGTERM\", \"SIGINT\", \"SIGHUP\"]) {\n/**\n * Hardened legacy hidden tests (owner decision 2026-10-18) and the sealed heldout-v2 corpus binding: test\n * infrastructure is never carried from the agent's workspace into the checks, test-runner configuration changes refuse\n * the checks, and the custodian's task/hidden digests bind the selected corpus exactly.\n */\nimport { test } from \"node:test\";\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { createHash } from \"node:crypto\";\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport os from \"node:os\";\nimport path from \"node:path\";\nimport { spawn, spawnSync } from \"node:child_process\";\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \"node:url\";\nimport { startGateway } from \"./helpers/fixtures.js\";\n\nconst ROOT = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), \"../..\");\nconst hardened = () => import(path.join(ROOT, \"eval/hardened_check.mjs\"));\nconst gitEnv = { PATH: \"/usr/bin:/bin\", HOME: os.tmpdir(), GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM: \"1\", GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL: \"/dev/null\" };\nconst git = (cwd: string, ...argv: string[]) => {\n  const r = spawnSync(\"git\", [\"-c\", \"user.name=t\", \"-c\", \"user.email=t@example.invalid\", \"-c\", \"init.defaultBranch=main\", ...argv], { cwd, env: gitEnv, encoding: \"utf8\" });\n  assert.equal(r.status, 0, r.stderr);\n  return r.stdout.trim();\n};\n\ntest(\"runAsAclArgs scopes evaluator and operator permissions with directory defaults\", async () => {\n  const { runAsAclArgs } = await import(path.join(ROOT, \"eval/isolate.mjs\"));\n  assert.deepEqual(runAsAclArgs(\"nexus-eval\", 1000, \"/workspace\", true), {\n    access: [\"-R\", \"-m\", \"u:nexus-eval:rwX,u:1000:rwX\", \"/workspace\"],\n    defaults: [\"-m\", \"d:u:nexus-eval:rwx,d:u:1000:rwx,d:m::rwx\", \"/workspace\"],\n  });\n  assert.deepEqual(runAsAclArgs(\"nexus-eval\", 1000, \"/workspace/file\", false), {\n    access: [\"-R\", \"-m\", \"u:nexus-eval:rwX,u:1000:rwX\", \"/workspace/file\"],\n    defaults: null,\n  });\n});\n\ntest(\"asUserSpec preserves timeout metadata and isolated processes reject missing timeouts\", async () => {\n  const { asUserSpec } = await import(path.join(ROOT, \"eval/validate.mjs\"));\n  const { runIsolatedProcess } = await import(path.join(ROOT, \"eval/isolate.mjs\"));\n  const spec = { cmd: \"/usr/bin/bwrap\", argv: [\"--version\"], timeoutMs: 1200, marker: \"preserved\" };\n  assert.deepEqual(asUserSpec(\"nexus-eval\", spec), {\n    ...spec,\n    cmd: \"/usr/bin/sudo\",\n    argv: [\"-n\", \"-u\", \"nexus-eval\", \"--\", \"/usr/bin/bwrap\", \"--version\"],\n  });\n  assert.throws(() => runIsolatedProcess({ cmd: \"/usr/bin/true\", argv: [] }), /isolated process spec has no timeoutMs/);\n  assert.throws(() => runIsolatedProcess({ cmd: \"/usr/bin/true\", argv: [], timeoutMs: 0 }), /isolated process spec has no timeoutMs/);\n});\n\ntest(\"test infrastructure is recognised across Python, Go, JS/TS and Rust layouts\", async () => {\n  const { isTestInfraPath } = await hardened();\n  for (const p of [\"conftest.py\", \"pkg/conftest.py\", \"pytest.ini\", \"tox.ini\", \"setup.cfg\", \"sitecustomize.py\", \"x.pth\", \"tests/test_a.py\", \"src/test_a.py\", \"a_test.py\",\n    \"pkg/x_test.go\", \"src/x.test.ts\", \"web/a.spec.jsx\", \"__tests__/a.js\", \"jest.config.js\", \"vitest.config.mts\", \".mocharc.json\", \"build.rs\", \".cargo/config.toml\", \".github/workflows/ci.yml\", \"Makefile\", \".env.local\",\n    \"karma.conf.js\", \"jest-preset.js\", \"vitest.workspace.ts\", \"globalSetup.ts\", \"setup-tests.js\", \"test-helpers.ts\", \"internal/testhelper/x.go\", \"pkg/_testing.py\",\n    \".npmrc\", \".yarnrc.yml\", \".pnpmfile.cjs\", \"go.work\", \"rust-toolchain.toml\", \"tsconfig.json\", \".coveragerc\", \".gitattributes\", \"node_modules/x/i.js\", \".venv/lib/x.py\", \"a/__pycache__/m.pyc\"]) {\n    assert.equal(isTestInfraPath(p), true, p);\n  }\n  for (const p of [\"src/app.py\", \"pkg/server.go\", \"src/index.ts\", \"src/lib.rs\", \"README.md\", \"package.json\", \"pyproject.toml\", \"Cargo.toml\", \"contest.py\"]) {\n    assert.equal(isTestInfraPath(p), false, p);\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"hidden test staging preserves workspace files and mounts only copied hidden files\", async () => {\n  const { stageHiddenFiles, hiddenOutputHasTests } = await import(path.join(ROOT, \"eval/isolate.mjs\"));\n  const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"hidden-stage-\"));\n  try {\n    const source = path.join(root, \"task/hidden\");\n    const ws = path.join(root, \"workspace\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(source, { recursive: true });\n    fs.mkdirSync(path.join(ws, \"test\"), { recursive: true });\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(source, \"private.test.js\"), \"hidden\\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(ws, \"existing.js\"), \"keep root\\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(ws, \"test/existing.js\"), \"keep test\\n\");\n    assert.deepEqual(stageHiddenFiles(source, ws, \".\", { readOnlyHidden: true }), [\"private.test.js\"]);\n    assert.deepEqual(stageHiddenFiles(source, ws, \"test\", { readOnlyHidden: true }), [\"test/private.test.js\"]);\n    assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ws, \"existing.js\"), \"utf8\"), \"keep root\\n\");\n    assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ws, \"test/existing.js\"), \"utf8\"), \"keep test\\n\");\n    assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ws, \"private.test.js\"), \"utf8\"), \"hidden\\n\");\n    assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ws, \"test/private.test.js\"), \"utf8\"), \"hidden\\n\");\n    const outsideDir = path.join(root, \"outside\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(outsideDir);\n    fs.symlinkSync(outsideDir, path.join(ws, \"sym\"));\n    assert.throws(() => stageHiddenFiles(source, ws, \"sym/newparent\", { readOnlyHidden: true }), /unsafe hidden test parent directory/);\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(outsideDir, \"newparent\")), false);\n    assert.equal(hiddenOutputHasTests(\"Ran 0 tests\"), false);\n    assert.equal(hiddenOutputHasTests(\"[no test files]\"), false);\n    assert.equal(hiddenOutputHasTests(\"Ran 1 test\\n\\nOK\"), true);\n    assert.equal(hiddenOutputHasTests(\"?   example/cmd [no test files]\\nok  example/pkg 0.01s\"), true);\n    assert.equal(hiddenOutputHasTests(\"test result: ok. 5 passed; 0 failed\\ntest result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed\"), true);\n    assert.equal(hiddenOutputHasTests(\"?   example/cmd [no test files]\"), false);\n    assert.equal(hiddenOutputHasTests(\"test result: ok. 0 passed; 0 failed\"), false);\n    assert.equal(hiddenOutputHasTests(\"Ran 0 tests\"), false);\n    assert.equal(hiddenOutputHasTests(\"\"), false);\n    assert.equal(hiddenOutputHasTests(\"hello\"), false);\n    assert.equal(hiddenOutputHasTests(\"hidden: all assertions passed\"), true, \"a validator-produced summary is used only for development scoring\");\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"Python oracle preload keeps saved source out of module globals and sys.path\", () => {\n  const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"python-oracle-preload-\"));\n  try {\n    const runner = path.join(root, \"runner\");\n    const hidden = path.join(root, \"test_hidden.py\");\n    fs.mkdirSync(runner);\n    fs.copyFileSync(path.join(ROOT, \"eval/hide_oracle.py\"), path.join(runner, \"sitecustomize.py\"));\n    fs.writeFileSync(hidden, 'SECRET = \"PY_ORACLE_CANARY_881\"\\n');\n    const script = `import importlib.machinery, pathlib, sys\npath = ${JSON.stringify(hidden)}\nmodule = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(\"test_hidden\", path).load_module()\nassert module.SECRET == \"PY_ORACLE_CANARY_881\"\nassert open(path).read() == \"\"\nassert \"sitecustomize\" not in sys.modules\nassert ${JSON.stringify(runner)} not in sys.path\nassert ${JSON.stringify(runner)} not in __import__(\"os\").environ.get(\"PYTHONPATH\", \"\").split(__import__(\"os\").pathsep)\nassert all(\"PY_ORACLE_CANARY_881\" not in repr(getattr(obj, \"_saved\", None)) for obj in sys.modules.values())\n`;\n    const result = spawnSync(\"python3\", [\"-c\", script], {\n      cwd: root,\n      env: { PATH: \"/usr/bin:/bin\", HOME: os.tmpdir(), PYTHONPATH: runner, NEXUS_HIDDEN_FILES: JSON.stringify([hidden]) },\n      encoding: \"utf8\",\n    });\n    assert.equal(result.status, 0, `${result.stderr}\\n${result.stdout}`);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"pytest candidate imports cannot inspect hidden Python sources\", { timeout: 30_000 }, async () => {\n  const { runIsolated } = await import(path.join(ROOT, \"eval/isolate.mjs\"));\n  const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"pytest-oracle-e2e-\"));\n  const ws = path.join(root, \"ws\");\n  fs.mkdirSync(path.join(ws, \"tests\"), { recursive: true });\n  try {\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(ws, \"app.py\"), `import gc, importlib.machinery, pathlib, sys\npaths = [pathlib.Path(\"/workspace/tests/__init__.py\"), pathlib.Path(\"/workspace/tests/test_hidden.py\"), pathlib.Path(\"/workspace/tests/unused_hidden.py\")]\nassert importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader.get_data.__closure__ is None\nassert \"sitecustomize\" not in sys.modules\nassert all(p.read_text() == \"\" for p in paths)\ngc.collect()\nneedles = (\"PYTEST_HIDDEN_COMMENT_CANARY_116\", \"PYTEST_UNUSED_COMMENT_CANARY_227\")\nassert not any(isinstance(obj, (bytes, bytearray, str)) and any(needle in (obj.decode(errors=\"ignore\") if isinstance(obj, (bytes, bytearray)) else obj) for needle in needles) for obj in gc.get_objects())\n`);\n    const hiddenSource = `# PYTEST_HIDDEN_COMMENT_CANARY_116\\nimport unittest\\nimport app\\nclass HiddenTest(unittest.TestCase):\\n    def test_candidate_import_is_safe(self):\\n        self.assertTrue(True)\\ndef test_candidate_import_is_safe():\\n    assert True\\n`;\n    const unusedSource = `# PYTEST_UNUSED_COMMENT_CANARY_227\\nSECRET = \"REDACTED\"\\n`;\n    const hiddenPaths = [\"tests/__init__.py\", \"tests/test_hidden.py\", \"tests/unused_hidden.py\"];\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(ws, hiddenPaths[0]), \"\\n\");\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(ws, hiddenPaths[1]), hiddenSource);\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(ws, hiddenPaths[2]), unusedSource);\n    const unittestResult = await runIsolated(\"python3 -m unittest tests/test_hidden.py\", { cwd: ws, hiddenSubpaths: hiddenPaths });\n    assert.equal(unittestResult.status, 0, `${unittestResult.stderr}\\n${unittestResult.stdout}`);\n    assert.match(`${unittestResult.stdout}${unittestResult.stderr}`, /Ran 1 test\\b/);\n    const pytestModule = fs.existsSync(\"/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/pytest\");\n    const rustPytest = fs.existsSync(\"/usr/local/nexus-qual/rust/bin/pytest\");\n    if (pytestModule || rustPytest) {\n      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(ws, hiddenPaths[0]), \"\\n\");\n      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(ws, hiddenPaths[1]), hiddenSource);\n      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(ws, hiddenPaths[2]), unusedSource);\n      const pytestCommand = pytestModule ? \"python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_hidden.py\" : \"pytest -q tests/test_hidden.py\";\n      const pytestResult = await runIsolated(pytestCommand, { cwd: ws, hiddenSubpaths: hiddenPaths });\n      assert.equal(pytestResult.status, 0, `${pytestResult.stderr}\\n${pytestResult.stdout}`);\n      assert.match(pytestResult.stdout, /\\b[12] passed\\b/);\n    }\n  } finally { fs.rmSync(root, { recursive: true, force: true }); }\n});\n\ntest(\"Rust and Go compile-time file inclusion directives refuse hardened checks\", async () => {\n  const { applyAgentChanges, testConfigChange } = await hardened();\n  const rust = \"pub fn value() -> usize { 1 }\\n\";\n  const go = \"package app\\n\";\n  for (const addition of [\n    'const SECRET: &str = include_str!(\"tests/hidden.rs\");',\n    'const SECRET: &[u8] = include_bytes!(\"tests/hidden.rs\");',\n    'include!(\"tests/hidden.rs\");',\n    '#[path = \"../tests/hidden.rs\"] mod hidden;',\n  ]) {\n    assert.match(testConfigChange(\"src/lib.rs\", rust, `${rust}${addition}\\n`) ?? \"\", /adds compile-time file inclusion/);\n  }\n  assert.match(testConfigChange(\"src/main.go\", go, `${go}//go:embed hidden_test.go\\nvar hidden string\\n`) ?? \"\", /adds \\/\\/go:embed directive/);\n\n  const base = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"embed-directive-\"));\n  try {\n    const agent = path.join(base, \"agent\");\n    const fresh = path.join(base, \"fresh\");\n    for (const dir of [agent, fresh]) {\n      fs.mkdirSync(path.join(dir, \"src\"), { recursive: true });\n      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"src/lib.rs\"), rust);\n      fs.writeFileSync(path.join(dir, \"src/main.go\"), go);\n    }\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(agent, \"src/lib.rs\"), `${rust}const SECRET: &str = include_str!(\"tests/hidden.rs\");\\n`);\n    fs.writeFileSync(path.join(agent, \"src/main.go\"), `${go}//go:embed hidden_test.go\\nvar hidden string\\n`);\n    const result = applyAgentChanges(agent, fresh);\n    assert.match(result.configChanges.join(), /src\\/lib\\.rs adds compile-time file inclusion/);\n    assert.match(result.configChanges.join(), /src\\/main\\.go adds \\/\\/go:embed directive/);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(base, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"only the agent's source changes reach the fresh check workspace; adversarial workspace state never does\", async () => {\n  const { applyAgentChanges } = await hardened();\n  const base = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), \"hardened-\"));\n  const write = (root: string, rel: string, content: string) => { fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(path.join(root, rel)), { recursive: true }); fs.writeFileSync(path.join(root, rel), content); };\n  try {\n    const agent = path.join(base, \"agent\");\n    const fresh = path.join(base, \"fresh\");\n    for (const dir of [agent, fresh]) {\n      write(dir, \"src/__init__.py\", \"\\n\");\n      write(dir, \"src/app.py\", \"def f(): return 1\\n\");\n      write(dir, \"src/old.py\", \"x = 1\\n\");\n      write(dir, \"package.json\", JSON.stringify({ name: \"x\", main: \"src/index.js\", scripts: { test: \"node --test\" }, dependencies: { a: \"1\" } }));\n      write(dir, \"Cargo.toml\", \"[package]\\nname = \\\"x\\\"\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nserde = \\\"1\\\"\\n\");\n      write(dir, \"go.mod\", \"module x\\n\\ngo 1.22\\n\");\n      write(dir, \"node_modules/jest/index.js\", \"real\\n\");\n    }\n    // Legitimate source work.\n    write(agent, \"src/app.py\", \"def f(): return 2\\n\");\n    fs.rmSync(path.join(agent, \"src/old.py\"));\n    write(agent, \"src/new.py\", \"y = 2\\n\");\n    // Adversarial state: git hooks/config/filters, ignore edits, planted deps, tool config, shadowing, test files.\n    write(agent, \".git/config\", \"[core]\\n\\tfsmonitor = touch /tmp/pwned\\n\");\n    write(agent, \".gitattributes\", \"* filter=x\\n\");\n    write(agent, \".gitignore\", \"\\n\");\n    write(agent, \"node_modules/jest/index.js\", \"process.exit(0)\\n\");\n    write(agent, \".npmrc\", \"script-shell=./x.sh\\n\");\n    write(agent, \"x.sh\", \"exit 0\\n\");\n    write(agent, \"pytest.py\", \"raise SystemExit(0)\\n\");\n    write(agent, \"_pytest/__init__.py\", \"\\n\");\n    write(agent, \"conftest.py\", \"import pytest\\n\");\n    write(agent, \"tests/test_mine.py\", \"def test(): pass\\n\");\n    write(agent, \"notes.txt\", \"scratch\\n\");\n    write(agent, \"src/math.js\", \"module.exports = 1;\\n\"); // a JS file named like a Python stdlib module is ordinary source\n    const result = applyAgentChanges(agent, fresh);\n    assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(fresh, \"src/app.py\"), \"utf8\"), \"def f(): return 2\\n\");\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(fresh, \"src/old.py\")), false, \"deletions are applied\");\n    assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(fresh, \"src/new.py\"), \"utf8\"), \"y = 2\\n\", \"new source files cross over\");\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(fresh, \"src/math.js\")), true, \"shadowing rules are Python-only\");\n    for (const blocked of [\".git/config\", \".gitattributes\", \".npmrc\", \"x.sh\", \"pytest.py\", \"_pytest/__init__.py\", \"conftest.py\", \"tests/test_mine.py\", \"notes.txt\"]) {\n      assert.equal(fs.existsSync(path.join(fresh, blocked)), false, `${blocked} never reaches the checks`);\n    }\n    assert.equal(fs.readFileSync(path.join(fresh, \"node_modules/jest/index.js\"), \"utf8\"), \"real\\n\", \"dependency trees come from setup, not the agent\");\n    assert.equal(fs.existsSync(\"/tmp/pwned\"), false, \"no git command ran against the agent's workspace\");\n    assert.deepEqual(result.configChanges, []);\n  } finally {\n    fs.rmSync(base, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n});\n\ntest(\"manifest changes outside plain dependency and metadata edits refuse the checks\", async () => {\n  const { testConfigChange } = await hardened();\n  const pkg = (o: object) => JSON.stringify({ name: \"x\", main: \"src/index.js\", scripts: { test: \"node --test\" }, dependencies: { a: \"1\" }, ...o });\n  assert.equal(testConfigChange(\"package.json\", pkg({}), pkg({ dependencies: { a: \"2\" } })), null);\n  assert.match(testConfigChange(\"package.json\", pkg({}), pkg({ main: \"test/index.js\" })) ?? \"\", /\"main\"/);\n  assert.match(testConfigChange(\"package.json\", pkg({}), pkg({ exports: { \".\": \"./t.js\" } })) ?? \"\", /\"exports\"/);\n  assert.match(testConfigChange(\"package.json\", pkg({}), pkg({ dependencies: { a: \"file:../evil\" } })) ?? \"\", /local or remote source/);\n  const cargo = \"[package]\\nname = \\\"x\\\"\\n\\n[dependencies]\\nserde = \\\"1\\\"\\n\";\n  assert.equal(testConfigChange(\"Cargo.toml\", cargo, cargo.replace('serde = \"1\"', 'serde = \"1.0.200\"')), null);\n  assert.match(testConfigChange(\"Cargo.toml\", cargo, `${cargo}\\n[patch.crates-io]\\nserde = { path = \"../s\" }\\n`) ?? \"\", /patch\\.crates-io/);\n  assert.match(testConfigChange(\"Cargo.toml\", cargo, cargo.replace('serde = \"1\"', 'serde = { path = \"../s\" }')) ?? \"\", /local, git or alternate-registry source/);\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log-18-2026-10-21T02:38:00Z PR8_CI terminal_success run39531291024 exact_head=f6f74847a4580a0399b43b3a631a8a9cb33f1cf4 jobs=Node20/22/24+linux_x86_64 package/repro/SBOM/smoke/installer; run is merge-candidate evidence, not exact-source; coordinator thread 01a14cb3 owns workflow_dispatch after this terminal success; /root not dispatching duplicate\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log-19-2026-10-21T02:40:00Z EXACT_SOURCE_CI dispatched_by=01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92 run39534084841 event=workflow_dispatch branch=v1/integration reported_head=f6f74847a4580a0399b43b3a631a8a9cb33f1cf4 current_remote_head_match=yes; /root read_only_observer verifies per-job checkout SHA and terminal status; SUITE retained\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log-20-2026-10-21T07:56:30Z RELEASE SUITE owner=/root run=39561260202 exact_head=36a8a62d06b7b0bcee3a257ef5d20560572b61b8 conclusion=SUCCESS jobs=test-matrix(20,22,24)+linux-x86_64 requirements_enforce=PASS clean_detached_worktree=/home/mike/nexus-wt/req-enforce-36a8a62 output=123_rows_tested109_partial5_implemented2_open7; 11 exact-RC deferred; CodeQL pull_request+push=PASS\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log:21:mv .git/nexus-claims/SUITE/owner.json .git/nexus-claims/archived/SUITE-owner-20261021T075630Z-run39561260202.json\n/home/mike/nexus-