{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:38:09.408Z","ordinal":494393,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188b4-bcfd-7801-8430-e45b95efb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f87fbb73-e065-4c02-83e4-7295ca9b957b","process_id":"73708","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED|CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION|held-out.*custod|custodian.*(opencode|SageBridge|root)|corpus.*custodian' .git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log | tail -100; rg -n -i 'custodian|custody|held.out' docs/v1.0.0 | head -180; git status --short --branch"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n 'CUSTODY_HANDOFF_ACCEPTED|CUSTODY_T2_BLACKBOX_CONVERSION|held-out.*custod|custodian.*(opencode|SageBridge|root)|corpus.*custodian' .git/nexus-claims/nexus-claims.log | tail -100; rg -n -i 'custodian|custody|held.out' docs/v1.0.0 | head -180; git status --short --branch"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"319:2026-10-23T22:32:37Z RELEASE_PUBLISHER_UPDATE main postmerge CI/CodeQL SUCCESS exact 830680b. PR174 is the next security source gate for read-only Docker fallback, exact checks in progress, independent ACCEPT. RC4 tag/publication not started; remaining held-out custody, OpenRouter live task, installed-RC qualification, and human acceptance are not satisfied.\n1408:2026-10-27T01:36:34Z CORRECTION prior perpetual review loop PASS claims are not verified: RC10 E3 remains PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED due 27.89s Ctrl-C outlier; ACC-TUI-A11Y remains PARTIAL_NOT_ACCEPTED due intermittent TERM_dumb 100x30 cancellation timeouts and incomplete overlay coverage; no stable v1.0.0; held-out and T4 custody unresolved\n2046:2026-10-29T06:50:25Z\tCUSTODY_CONTACT_RECONCILIATION operator_identified=SageBridge_as_reachable_contact historical_custodian=opencode_primary_session current_custodian=UNRESOLVED REDACTED agent_mail_active_windows=0 registration_token_unavailable issue1_latest_status=2026-10-29T06:02:22Z_no_handoff_ack no_private_corpus_access qualification=STOPPED\n2054:2026-10-29T07:12:28Z CUSTODY_HANDOFF_CLARIFIED issue_comment=6490405248 historical_custodian=opencode_primary_session transfer=SageBridge_unresolved requirements=40_blackbox_v1_tasks_pinned_toolchain_setup_independence_exposure_setup_reference_revalidation_digest_integrity_access_separation_acceptance public_metadata_only=true no_payload_access=true qualification=STOPPED\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:46:4. M2 and M4 run in parallel with M1/M3. Held-out task authoring (agent-authored, as authorised) and the standalone proxy start during M1.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:97:- **No product qualification exists.** \"Blocked\" is established, from reproduced defects. \"Qualified\" cannot be: there is no held-out, fault-injection or standalone evidence, and the tasks used in the historical pilot were tuned.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:13:| [DEC-05](#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds) | Evaluation protocol and thresholds | 40 held-out T2 tasks, 5 runs, 2 peers, thresholds below | Needs an external author (see actions) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:81:- 40 held-out T2 tasks, at least 20 from external repositories at pinned commits, across JS/TS, Python, Rust and Go, with at least 6 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug).\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:92:| Held-out T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | **≥ 60% absolute** and **≥ (best matched peer − 10 points)** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:102:**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:56:| REQ-AGT-002 | quickstart; TOP_TIER B3; EXEC-005 | Truthful outcome taxonomy. VERIFIED requires a passing, deliverable-bound verifier run, plus fail-before/pass-after independence for discovered verifiers. UNVERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE, BLOCKED and LIMIT_REACHED are distinct, with exit codes 0/2/1/130. | `agent.ts:5726-5764`; `tester.ts:371-430,541-627`; `turn.ts:318-351` | TEST at db1ca55; candidate suite at `6151a23` passes ACC-VER-03/04/09 regression tests. Historical VER-04/05 findings and tuned-set/live evidence remain in [A2_verification.md](evidence/A2_verification.md) and the dated evidence files. | partial | N | M5 false-VERIFIED threshold remains unqualified pending held-out T2/T3/T4 evidence; historical VER-04/05 implementation defects have regression coverage at the candidate. | ACC-VER-03/04/09, ACC-QUAL-T2 | B | SPEC-11 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:234:| REQ-QUAL-101 | TOP_TIER Q1; DEC-05 | Held-out T2 evaluation: 40 tasks, ≥ 50% external, sealed manifest. | product maturity | `eval/` | HIST (6 tuned tasks) | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.1 | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:10:- **Supporting labour.** Held-out tasks are written by an agent author (authorised, DEC-05). Independent acceptance is done by a reviewer the owner provides (X5).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:20:  (from M1) held-out task authoring, standalone proxy, fixtures (parallel) ─────────────────┘\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:31:| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:41:**M0 → M1 → M3 → RC1 → M5 (T2 held-out runs) → M6**\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:52:- the 40 held-out T2 tasks and 8 T3 tasks (agent-authored), with their manifest sealed **before** RC1;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:82:| Held-out results miss the thresholds | Fix loops | Thresholds are pre-registered, so they are not moved after the fact. The fix is a code change, and the affected run classes are re-run. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:303:| Overfitting to eval tasks | Dataset splits (train/val/test); held-out tasks per DEC-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:65:7. **Qualified.** Held-out matched evaluation, plus fault injection, meeting the pre-registered thresholds in DEC-05.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:108:| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:114:- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:31:| 8 | Author tasks (owner action X2). Development set: the existing 6 plus routing engx T01–T12. Held-out set: 40 T2 tasks, of which at least 20 are external, at least 6 per class, across 4 languages. Plus 8 T3 tasks. The sha256 manifest is committed before RC freeze. Calibrate on the development set only. | external store; `eval/heldout-manifest.json` | 7 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:34:| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (8×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:6:- **Eval:** the harness is sound for matched T2 fixture runs. The only results come from a 6-task pilot that is self-declared as tuned. No held-out set, no T3/T4, no fault injection. It cannot qualify v1 task quality as it stands.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:92:| EVL-001 | S1 (v1 task-quality claim) | Qualification evidence | eval/README.md:42,47-58; docs/reviews/evidence/eval_pilot_2026-10-13/RESULT.md:62-63 | DOC-CLAIM + SOURCE. The only scored evidence is 6 in-repo T2 fixture tasks. RESULT.md itself says \"These six tasks were used to find and fix the issues … it does not qualify Nexus. Qualification needs a fresh task set.\" Missing: held-out tasks, the T3 long-task set, the T4 fault injector, the T3 fact-sheet scorer, and runs on the release candidate. The measured builds are 76f4081, ed17e99 and 4fcbe68-dirty; their rebased equivalents (fe576f1, d116e99, 0090f9c) are on main, but db1ca55 itself was never evaluated. | No basis for a v1 claim about task quality. The pilot verdict was \"NOT QUALIFIED (false VERIFIED=2)\". The rerun had 0 false VERIFIED, but on tuned tasks. | A v1 protocol is in §7. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:128:- **Credential custody in the broker is careful.** Checks on owner, 0400 mode, nlink and inode-before/after; O_NOFOLLOW; buffers zero-filled after use; a reflection scan over all git objects; error output limited to an allowlist of codes (demo-transport.mjs:152-185,375-391). Executables are bound by file descriptor (linux-bound-exec). Git config is hardened (no system or global config, no hooks, no credential helper, `followRedirects=false`, protocol allowlist) at :192-212. Tests are RUNTIME-verified: demo-transport 8/8; artifact-token-response 14 revoke cases plus 8 post-revoke cases; credential-lifecycle 25 assertions; linux-bound-exec; classify-revoke 11 cases; worker token-response 10/10; work-state-contract 2/2.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:154:- **G6: task difficulty and discrimination.** 4 of 6 pilot tasks were 10/10 for Nexus (ceiling). To qualify, calibrate a held-out set so that no task is solved by every agent 5/5.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:176:| EVL-R1 | **Held-out set:** at least 40 T2 tasks (proposal). At least 50% from external repos at pinned commits (JS/TS, Python, Rust, Go). The held-out half is authored by someone other than the Nexus developer and kept outside the repo (encrypted or private) until the freeze. The 6 pilot tasks plus the routing engx T01-T12 count as a *development* set only. | workflow | BLOCKER for any v1 quality claim | The manifest lists task sha256s committed *before* the release-candidate (RC) freeze. Tasks are revealed after scoring. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/G_contest_eval.md:183:| EVL-R8 | **Pass thresholds (proposal, owner input needed):** false VERIFIED = 0 (hard). Held-out T2 pooled correctness ≥ best matched peer − 10 points, and ≥60% absolute (proposal). No task class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) below 40%. Crash rate ≤2%. T4 truthful = 100%. Regression rate ≤5%. | release gate | BLOCKER | Scorer verdict table, signed off before the RC run. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-11-verification-and-tool-call-integrity.md:71:- The T2 held-out run shows 0 false VERIFIED (SPEC-10).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:48:| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:141:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:211:### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:216:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:337:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:339:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker verifies source/tag/artifact/evidence hash bindings; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:23:- a held-out task set;\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:41:1. **REQ-QUAL-101. Held-out matched evaluation.**\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:44:   - The held-out half is authored by someone other than the implementer and stored outside the repo until the freeze. Its manifest of sha256 hashes is committed before the RC freeze.\n## main...origin/main [ahead 1, behind 1569]\n M .claude/settings.json\n M AGENTS.md\n M cli/dist/agent.js\n M cli/dist/core/state.js\n M cli/package.json\n M cli/src/agent.ts\n M cli/src/checkpoint.ts\n M cli/src/core/durable_file.ts\n M cli/src/core/persistence_protection.ts\n M cli/src/core/state.ts\n M cli/src/flight.ts\n M cli/src/knowledge.ts\n M cli/src/session.ts\n M cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts\n M core/tests/adversarial_path_traversal.rs\nA  docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nA  docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\nA  scripts/check_requirements.mjs\n?? .entire/agent-guide.md\n?? CLAUDE.md\n?? check_in_agents.py\n?? checkin-agents.md\n?? checkin.py\n?? cli/test/agent_prompt.test.ts\n?? cli/test/helpers/setup.ts\n?? cli/test/home_isolation.test.ts\n?? cli/test/persistence_hygiene.test.ts\n?? docs/codebase-review-enhancements.md\n?? docs/enhancement-opportunities.md\n?? docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/\n?? docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md\n?? docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n?? doc