ualification exists.** \"Blocked\" is established, from reproduced defects. \"Qualified\" cannot be: there is no held-out, fault-injection or standalone evidence, and the tasks used in the historical pilot were tuned.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:13:| [DEC-05](#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds) | Evaluation protocol and thresholds | 40 held-out T2 tasks, 5 runs, 2 peers, thresholds below | Needs an external author (see actions) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:81:- 40 held-out T2 tasks, at least 20 from external repositories at pinned commits, across JS/TS, Python, Rust and Go, with at least 6 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug).\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:92:| Held-out T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | **≥ 60% absolute** and **≥ (best matched peer − 10 points)** |\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:102:**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:56:| REQ-AGT-002 | quickstart; TOP_TIER B3; EXEC-005 | Truthful outcome taxonomy. VERIFIED requires a passing, deliverable-bound verifier run, plus fail-before/pass-after independence for discovered verifiers. UNVERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE, BLOCKED and LIMIT_REACHED are distinct, with exit codes 0/2/1/130. | `agent.ts:5726-5764`; `tester.ts:371-430,541-627`; `turn.ts:318-351` | TEST at db1ca55; candidate suite at `6151a23` passes ACC-VER-03/04/09 regression tests. Historical VER-04/05 findings and tuned-set/live evidence remain in [A2_verification.md](evidence/A2_verification.md) and the dated evidence files. | partial | N | M5 false-VERIFIED threshold remains unqualified pending held-out T2/T3/T4 evidence; historical VER-04/05 implementation defects have regression coverage at the candidate. | ACC-VER-03/04/09, ACC-QUAL-T2 | B | SPEC-11 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:234:| REQ-QUAL-101 | TOP_TIER Q1; DEC-05 | Held-out T2 evaluation: 40 tasks, ≥ 50% external, sealed manifest. | product maturity | `eval/` | HIST (6 tuned tasks) | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.1 | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:10:- **Supporting labour.** Held-out tasks are written by an agent author (authorised, DEC-05). Independent acceptance is done by a reviewer the owner provides (X5).\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:20:  (from M1) held-out task authoring, standalone proxy, fixtures (parallel) ─────────────────┘\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:31:| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:41:**M0 → M1 → M3 → RC1 → M5 (T2 held-out runs) → M6**\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:52:- the 40 held-out T2 tasks and 8 T3 tasks (agent-authored), with their manifest sealed **before** RC1;\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:82:| Held-out results miss the thresholds | Fix loops | Thresholds are pre-registered, so they are not moved after the fact. The fix is a code change, and the affected run classes are re-run. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/LANGSMITH_REVIEW.md:303:| Overfitting to eval tasks | Dataset splits (train/val/test); held-out tasks per DEC-05 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:65:7. **Qualified.** Held-out matched evaluation, plus fault injection, meeting the pre-registered thresholds in DEC-05.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:108:| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modu