{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:39:02.916Z","ordinal":494444,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a188be-6a84-7bc1-b334-8887325d7950","call_id":"call_e838ea1c54444a169e7b6b72fab7d47b","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No ownership or handoff change is visible. At `origin/main` `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`, issue #1 remains open and unassigned; its latest comment (#6483900189) reports no custodian update and no qualification runs. The Agent Mail directory shows no active project windows or designated custodian, and the public claims log has no held-out handoff record.\\n\\nThe remaining external dependency is a reachable owner identifying the designated custodian or assigning a replacement, followed by an acknowledged handoff. That custodian must handle the legacy-to-`blackbox-v1` conversion or replacement, private validation, and renewed custody acceptance before qualification. I did not contact anyone or access private corpus material.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — reviewed base `fe1c91dbcb56693a34c06dd3719bea139f639833` to head `c3c0837e1d02c10f74378752ac8f140475aaa9fb`, diff SHA-256 `9ca29146f65b92c0e4e7c7cb3c7a6aec6bdb2fa71aaf3222a9b855b3198582dd`.\\n\\nThe streamed, four-worker `find` scans retain fail-closed output/error handling, byte/entry/job limits, and `-P` symlink behavior. Splitting large roots into child-directory jobs plausibly reduces scan time and avoids buffering all output in the parent at once.\\n\\nOne cancellation gap remains: `enumerateJobs()` can be blocked in `opendir`/async directory iteration at [eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-code/eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs:45). The 25-second handler calls `jobs.return()` and kills `find` children, but cannot cancel an already-pending directory read; `Promise.all(workers)` still waits for that `jobs.next()` at [eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-code/eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs:151). The caller’s 35-second `spawnSync` timeout at [eval/isolate.mjs](/home/mike/nexus-code/eval/isolate.mjs:217) sends SIGTERM, and the helper catches SIGTERM without forcing exit. A stalled filesystem read can therefore leave the preflight waiting beyond both deadlines. Make root enumeration cancellable or provide a guaranteed hard-stop path, and cover that cancellation case.\\n\\nThis is a static source review only; I did not run tests or verify CI.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a188b4-bcfd-7801-8430-e45b95efb101","create_time":1793295542.9160905}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
