.dir>` (`bin/hidden_digest.mjs`). Re-derivable by anyone holding the store. |\n22:| Seal tool | `bin/seal.mjs` (sha256 `c7fedb77420839b4796e03b05bf552034d6938411073ab2bf17567ac7dd19d0c`): merges batch manifests, re-derives every hash, refuses any task not custodian-validated, enforces composition. Output above. |\n23-| Validator | `bin/validate.py` (sha256 `62133a649b5a6715dd212840a1ff16497aa2231b92a9eb8657fc8d821ca5c2cb`): fresh clone → checkout → setup → regression (pass) → hidden (fail) → reference patch (apply) → hidden (pass) → regression (pass). Go via `/usr/local/go/bin`, `GOFLAGS=-mod=mod`, GOPATH/GOCACHE/GOMODCACHE under the store; cargo home under the store; offline after clone. |\n24-| Contract | `CONTRACT.md` sha256 `99ecef6656825cf325f33e79e382c700dc8e400e8bf02e96691741572262a057`; store `AGENTS.md` (isolation rules) sha256 `319e6eeba78871ee4c91a33e0d8db25d59c191264cc4fd74a7a2bf363c0eca12` |\n--\n30-| Batches | Author | Session / provider | Context and access | Outcome |\n31-|---|---|---|---|---|\n32:| 1–7 (31 tasks) + the `ho2-go-debug-02` repair | `author-v2` | isolated subagent spawned by the custodian's opencode session, 2026-10-17 18:0xZ – 2026-10-18 01:1xZ | inputs: `CONTRACT.md`, `bin/`, public upstream repositories; no Nexus checkout, no dev/pilot store | 31 accepted; provider usage-limited ~01:1xZ (reset 11:43Z); claim `HELDOUT_AUTHORING` left in place and **not impersonated**; transfer notice written to the store (`AUTHOR-TRANSFER-2026-10-18.md`) |\n33:| 8 (5 tasks) | `author-b8c` | OpenAI Codex `exec` 0.163 (`gpt-6-luna`), fresh non-interactive session `01a14ce0-3339-7733-8afe-d5036bac31d6`, launched with `--disable memories --disable hooks --disable skill_search -c mcp_servers={}`, cwd confined to the store; resumed twice (to finish the batch; to apply the custodian soundness repair) | inputs recorded in `MANIFEST-batch8.json#provenance`; custodian audited every exec line of the session log: no read outside the store except its own claim dir and one claim-log line; no other task's hidden/reference files | 5 accepted (3 inherited author-v2 drafts verified and re-worded; 2 new) |\n34-| 9 (4 tasks) | `author-b9c` | same launch form, fresh session `01a14ce0-fc89-7650-87b6-d39d7ec9140a`, resumed twice (selection guidance; soundness repair) | same audit, clean; `MANIFEST-batch9.json#provenance` | 4 accepted |\n35-| Rejected: batch 9 first attempt | `author-b9` | Codex `exec` launched 02:25Z **without** `--disable memories` | session read `~/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md` (contains Nexus implementation and tuning notes) and the author self-disclosed a memory-registry search plus globbing other tasks' validation logs | **Rejected for provenance** 02:37Z; all writes quarantined outside the store (`/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2-quarantine/b9-contaminated-2026-10-18T0235Z/`, never an input to any later author). Its slots were re-authored by `author-b9c`, who could not read the quarantine (audited). One slot independently reused the same upstream repository at a different commit and scenario. |\n36:| Aborted: `author-b8` (opencode subagent, died with its spawning session, no output) and `author-b8r` (Codex, aborted ~60 s after launch for the same memory exposure, no output) | — | — | recorded as broken/aborted claims in the claim log | nothing accepted |\n37-\n38:Separation: the implementation agents (codex app-server sessions and `kiro-cli` on the Nexus repository) authored nothing. The custodian authored nothing and edited task files never; it edited store bookkeeping (`ASSIGNMENT-*.md`, `AUTHOR-TRANSFER-2026-10-18.md`, `AGENTS.md`) and ran the validator. Authors never ran `bin/validate.py` and never held the `SUITE` claim.\n39-\n40-## 3. Custodian validation\n41-\n42:Every task was validated by the custodian in a bounded, atomically claimed `SUITE` window (claim log lines `CLAIM SUITE opencode v7/v8/v9/v10/v11`, each released with `RELEASE SUITE`). Rounds: batches 1–7 one round each (windows v7, v8); batches 8–9 and the repaired task two rounds each (v9–v11). Per-task logs: `reference/<id>.validation.log` in the store. Claim-log evidence: one `VALIDATED <id> rounds=N (<window>)` line per task; latest line governs.\n43-\n44:Pre-seal integrity check (custodian script, 03:05Z): for all 40 tasks, `task_sha256` and `hidden_sha256` equal the batch manifest entries, and no `task.json`, hidden file, or reference patch has a modification time later than the task's latest validation. The three batch-8 tasks whose objectives were repaired were revalidated afterwards (hidden tests and patches unchanged).\n45-\n46-Composition and schema: `bin/check_schema.mjs` OK for all 40 (authors' manifests; re-checked by `seal.mjs` through hash re-derivation); composition enforced by `seal.mjs` (≥ 40, ≥ 6 per class, ≥ 20 external) and exceeded (10/10/10/10, 40 external).\n--\n50-| Task | Finding | Disposition |\n51-|---|---|---|\n52:| `ho2-go-debug-02` (batch 4) | custodian v7 run failed: repository's own suite failed at the pinned commit on this host (Go 1.26 `go vet` rejects a pre-existing `%q` printf verb in the repo's `range_test.go`), so neither baseline nor reference could pass | author-v2 repaired it 01:11Z (before its limit) by adding a deterministic `setup` step that stages a vet-compatible verb change in that existing test file; hidden test and regression command unchanged; validated v9 (2 rounds). Restricted failure evidence given to the assigned author was limited to this task's exit codes. |\n53:| `ho2-go-refactor-03`, `ho2-rs-refactor-03` (batch 8), `ho2-rs-feature-03` (batch 9) | validated, but hidden tests bound to new API names/signatures that the objective never stated (unsolvable from the task text) | custodian hold 02:54Z / 03:03Z; authors rewrote the objectives to state the required interface (no hidden-test loosening); `ho2-rs-feature-03`'s first rewrite quoted the hidden test's exact example values and was revised to different examples; all revalidated |\n54-| `ho2-go-feature-03` | objective hinted API names only via a grep | signatures made explicit; revalidated |\n55-| `ho2-py-refactor-03` | regression command deselects one test (`tests/test_arguments.py::test_bytes_args`) | verified on the pristine baseline: fails with a pytest-9 `DontReadFromInput.encoding` setter `AttributeError`, unrelated to the task; recorded, accepted |\n--\n62-\n63-1. **Harness history leak — CLOSED (`96aeef2`, PR #18; canary `6a334fa`, PR #26).** `eval/workspace.mjs` stages external-repo tasks via `git init` + ancestor-only fetch (`--no-tags`, `--no-write-fetch-head`), with no `--shared`, alternates, remotes, tags, or post-baseline commits.\n64:2. **Kernel resource contract — SOURCE-IMPLEMENTED (`91406bd`, PR #19; dedicated-tmpfs preflight `6a334fa`, PR #26).** Host provisioning (`eval/host/provision.sh`, PR #31) and custodian reference calibration / resource-profile freeze remain required before running T2/T3/T4 qualification.\n65-3. **Evaluator hidden-test execution boundary (distinct from corpus custody; qualification blocker until independently accepted).** All 40 T2 tasks in `heldout-v2` are pinned external repositories across Go, Rust, Python, and JavaScript that use `hidden: { dir, into, command }` and `regression: { command }`. Corpus custody acceptance below covers the sealed store identity (`50895b84…`), author isolation, reference validation, and the `root:root` `0700`/`0500` store DAC boundary; it does **not** constitute evaluator execution-boundary acceptance. If post-agent hidden tests run in the same process/mount namespace as candidate-controlled code with readable hidden test files, hidden-validator confidentiality and zero-test/early-exit resistance remain open qualification blockers until the evaluator boundary is remediated and independently accepted.\n66-4. Peer calibration, Node runtime parity and the frozen run record (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) are unchanged by this seal.\n--\n68-## 7. Store access control and root-owned DAC boundary (updated 2026-10-18T10:38Z / 12:10Z)\n69-\n70:After initial tightening to `0700` `mike:mike` (03:15Z), the coordinator noted at 10:36Z that implementation agent shells also run as uid `mike` (`1000`). At 10:38Z the custodian transferred ownership of the sealed T2 store, the T2 quarantine, and the sealed T3 store to `root:root` with mode `0700` on store roots and `0500` read-only on `tasks/` and `reference/`:\n71-\n72-```\n--\n87-## 6. Claim-log pointers\n2046:2026-10-29T06:50:25Z\tCUSTODY_CONTACT_RECONCILIATION operator_identified=SageBridge_as_reachable_contact historical_custodian=opencode_primary_session current_custodian=UNRESOLVED REDACTED agent_mail_active_windows=0 registration_token_unavailable issue1_latest_status=2026-10-29T06:02:22Z_no_handoff_ack no_private_corpus_access qualification=STOPPED\n2054:2026-10-29T07:12:28Z CUSTODY_HANDOFF_CLARIFIED issue_comment=6490405248 historical_custodian=opencode_primary_session transfer=SageBridge_unresolved requirements=40_blackbox_v1_tasks_pinned_toolchain_setup_independence_exposure_setup_reference_revalidation_digest_integrity_access_separation_acceptance public_metadata_only=true no_payload_access=true qualification=STOPPED\n## main...origin/main [ahead 1, behind 1569]\n M .claude/settings.json\n M AGENTS.md\n M cli/dist/agent.js\n M cli/dist/core/state.js\n M cli/package.json\n M cli/src/agent.ts\n M cli/src/checkpoint.ts\n M cli/src/core/durable_file.ts\n M cli/src/core/persistence_protection.ts\n M cli/src/core/state.ts\n M cli/src/flight.ts\n M cli/src/knowledge.ts\n M cli/src/session.ts\n M cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts\n M core/tests/adversarial_path_traversal.rs\nA  docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nA  docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\nA  scripts/check_requirements.mjs\n?? .entire/agent-guide.md\n?? CLAUDE.md\n?? check_in_agents.py\n?? checkin-agents.md\n?? checkin.py\n?? cli/test/agent_prompt.test.ts\n?? cli/test/helpers/setup.ts\n?? cli/test/home_isolation.test.ts\n?? cli/test/persistence_hygiene.test.ts\n?? docs/codebase-