{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:44:44.070Z","ordinal":494684,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188b4-bcfd-7801-8430-e45b95efb101","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae3860b757081a091adf92169a5f442","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The independent review confirmed the cancellation fix, then found one more fail-open edge: invalid UTF-8 below a nested directory could be replaced during decoding and leave a compiler unmasked. I’m adding byte-level validation to the final scan output and a nested-path fixture. The held-out corpus remains untouched."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1793295883495,"completed_at_ms":1793295884070}}
