{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:46:52.785Z","ordinal":494835,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a188c5-95f0-7340-abbe-58292e5e1cf5","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed base `fe1c91dbcb56693a34c06dd3719bea139f639833` to HEAD `7fe2981d6e9a379ff06804b829cb9200fe7a8dbe`, including the uncommitted two-file fix. Cumulative tracked-tree diff SHA-256: `41cb848ae19bdc60dc6d4e91c7558ea444079e584ff7569ba0c841dee1e526b3`.\n\nThe new `isUtf8` check validates the complete compiler-result buffer before writing it for the caller to decode ([`scan-compiler-exposure.mjs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs:236)). The regression places an invalid-byte directory below a valid root-level directory, so it reaches the recursive compiler-result stream and exercises that exact check ([`eval_integrity.test.ts`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:579)). Invalid output causes a nonzero scanner result, which the caller treats as a failed preflight. I found no remaining fail-open path in this correction.\n\nThe earlier cancellation concern is also addressed by the killable root-enumeration child and SIGTERM/reaping regression. This is a static review only; I did not run suites or verify CI."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a188b4-bcfd-7801-8430-e45b95efb101","create_time":1793296012.7848134}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":23121}}
