{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:49:29.092Z","ordinal":494952,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188b4-bcfd-7801-8430-e45b95efb101","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cbebb4c2-0d26-4cfb-b85f-95e094311d24","process_id":"24040","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -C 3 '5\\.1|5\\.2|5\\.3|ACC-TUI|PTY|manual'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '220,360p'; rg -n \"scripted.*PTY|acceptance.*pty|installed.*RC.*PTY|ACC-TUI-SCRIPTED\" docs scripts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -C 3 '5\\.1|5\\.2|5\\.3|ACC-TUI|PTY|manual'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '220,360p'; rg -n \"scripted.*PTY|acceptance.*pty|installed.*RC.*PTY|ACC-TUI-SCRIPTED\" docs scripts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\n52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n54-\n--\n62-## 1. Rules\n63-\n64-1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n66-3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n67-4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n68-   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n--\n76-\n77-| ID | Environment | Used for |\n78-|---|---|---|\n79:| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81-| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n--\n107-\n108-| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n109-|---|---|---|\n110:| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n111:| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n114-| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n--\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n--\n158-\n159-## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n160-\n161:### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n162-\n163-These must pass:\n164-\n--\n171-- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n172-- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n173-- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n174:- new: the package PTY smoke\n175-\n176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n177-\n178-These are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n179-\n--\n187-| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n189-\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n191-\n192:**Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix below is not a release gate; no operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell evidence are required, and none are claimed. Automated CI checks in §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n193-\n194-Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n195-\n--\n277-| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n278-| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n279-| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n280:| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n281-| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n282-| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n283-| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n--\n333-- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n334-- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n335-- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n337-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n338-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n339-- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overloaded\n3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n4. output-limit truncation\n5. hanging test command\n6. disk full\n7. context overflow at 32k\n8. malformed tool-call JSON\n9. SIGTERM then `run --resume`\n\n### 6.3 T3 long tasks (ACC-QUAL-T3)\n\n- 8 tasks × 5 runs. Each run must have ≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions and scripted steering.\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\n| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n\n## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n\nThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n\nThe reviewer receives:\n\n- the RC package;\n- this file;\n- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n- SPEC-04;\n- read access to the evidence directory.\n\nThe reviewer performs:\n\n1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   - 2 T4 classes.\n2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n\n**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n\n## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n\nThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\n| CON-A2 | Broker negative tests: caller-supplied env paths and URLs are ignored. A host outside `*.artifacts.cloudflare.net` is refused. |\n| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n| CON-A4 | `sudo -l` for the demo user shows only fixed argv. `sudo setpriv --reuid=0 id` is denied. |\n| CON-A5 | One clean-account `--mode cloudflare --agents real` run, with a committed, redacted run record. |\n| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\n\n## 10. Release decision (G6)\n\nG6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\n\n- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\n- [ ] The pre-RC source gate passes from a clean source worktree: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`. Every B/RR source row outside the §1.1 qualification-only map must be ≥ `tested`. A mapped row below `tested` is reported as deferred; this result does not accept or qualify it.\n- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\n  `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce --qualification-record <record.json> --rc-artifact <installed-rc-package> --evidence-root <evidence-directory>`.\n  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\n- [ ] Docs checklist (SPEC-09 §3.2) is signed off.\n- [ ] Release notes state the standalone scope (DEC-16), the provider tiers (DEC-06), the experimental surfaces (DEC-03, DEC-07) and the known limitations.\n- [ ] Owner approval to publish (X7).\n\nAfter G6, complete source checks on the exact stable-version commit before tagging, then complete the stable artifact checks in §1.1 stage 5 before publishing the draft. A failure keeps publication blocked and requires remediation plus the applicable requalification; do not mark the campaign released until published artifacts are independently verified.\n\n**Outcome recording.** The release decision record goes in `docs/releases/v1.0.0.md`, with links to every evidence directory.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md:3:A human may run this procedure against the **installed RC** for optional terminal checks. For v1.0.0, the manual matrix is waived by DEC-20; these runs are not a release gate. Automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) remain mandatory.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:245:**Chosen (owner-confirmed 2026-10-28).** Approval-panel and post-exit screenshots are not required for v1.0.0. This waiver changes only the screenshot artifact requirement. It does not waive any interactive run, check, safety threshold, per-cell PASS/FAIL verdict, observed outcome, evidence record, exact installed-RC identity, or written disposition for non-safety failures. All 15 manual matrix cells remain mandatory; automated PTY runs cannot replace them.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:255:**Current decision (release owner direction, 2026-10-29).** All fifteen manual E3 cells remain mandatory on the exact installed RC. Record a PASS or FAIL and observed outcomes for every required check in every cell. Automated CI or PTY runs do not substitute for operator evidence. [DEC-18](#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) remains in force and waives screenshot artifacts only; it does not waive interaction, checks, per-cell verdicts, evidence records, or safety gates. No cell is accepted as complete without actual manual execution.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:265:**Direction.** The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No manual operator run, cell verdict, or per-cell evidence is required, and the waiver does not claim that any cell passed. The automated CI gate in §5.1 and the scripted installed-RC PTY gate in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:36:| 12 | Manual terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-20](../DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver); no manual cells or per-cell evidence are required or implied. Automated CI PTY (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) remain mandatory and must pass. | ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.3; DEC-20 | RC build |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | Automated CI and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual real-terminal matrix is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.2 | TEST (PTY suites in CI) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.2; manual matrix disposition: DEC-20 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:192:**Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix below is not a release gate; no operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell evidence are required, and none are claimed. Automated CI checks in §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:5:The release owner accepted DEC-20: the manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in Acceptance §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell results are required or inferred. Automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory. This update changes the terminal disposition only; the release, PR, CI, and custody details in the checkpoint below remain the historical 06:18 UTC snapshot and are not refreshed here.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:31:**Terminal gate:** The release owner requires all 15 manual terminal cells (five environments × three sizes) on the exact installed RC. The latest verified worksheet status is 0/15 accepted cells; blank cells remain incomplete. Actual operator execution and per-cell outcomes are mandatory; automated CI or PTY results do not substitute. [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waives screenshots only. [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal applications, but the manual matrix remains outstanding. This 04:23 snapshot predates DEC-20 and is superseded by the current checkpoint above.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:208:Five targeted synthetic installed-RC10 cancellation rechecks at `TERM=dumb`, 100×30 completed with Esc delays from 0 to 1 second; idle return measured 0.405–0.507 seconds. The two earlier full-matrix timeouts remained valid and unresolved; this targeted recheck did not promote ACC-TUI-A11Y or E3. Evidence and raw PTY streams are preserved in [the cancellation timing recheck](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/cancel-timing-recheck-20261027/README.md). Human terminal acceptance remained 0/15. This historical record is retained from the PR #264 merge history.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:240:**RC10 installation and terminal preparation:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains an unaccepted prerelease from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The linked [RC10 desktop preflight record](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual-preflight/README.md) documents successful provenance-verified installation to an isolated qualification prefix on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`), with CLI identity `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)`. xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are present. This prepares the host only: the human matrix remains **0/15**. The operator must perform each of the five terminal environments at all three sizes and provide two genuine screenshots and a verdict per cell; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:268:**Held-out and human gates:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open with no custodian acceptance recorded; no held-out payload was accessed and T2/T3/T4 acceptance is not established. The manual terminal matrix still requires operator evidence across five environments and three sizes. At 2026-10-27 03:49 UTC, I verified over SSH to `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`) that `/home/mike/nexus-rc10-manual-evidence/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md` exists and contains an unfilled 15-cell template with directories for every environment/size pair. No cell evidence is present; the installed candidate identity is blank. Any matrix run must use the eventual installed RC. Scripted PTY output is not a substitute.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:283:**RC9 installed accessibility result and source fix:** Published tag `v1.0.0-rc.9` still points to source `4cae11cbc3b0eab9bd6f56df7cc34e946b5dc566`; its archive SHA-256 is `35795d2b7639b68a541c512976d8bc7f251115ebdccf48f6b9cf5f98ef1af9bb`. PR [#260](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/260) merged the exact installed-RC PTY evidence as `9def2658e9269f6468ff7c5562839999cc7352a8`; captures and verifier are in [the RC9 accessibility evidence](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md). On installed RC9, `NO_COLOR=1` under xterm at 40x14 and 100x30 emitted no color SGR codes (2/2 subcases passed); `TERM=dumb` with `NO_COLOR` unset emitted reset SGR `39m`, `49m`, and `59m` at both sizes (2/2 subcases failed). The complete all-state accessibility gate remains partial. PR [#261](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/261) now disables Crossterm color output when the TUI resolves `Depth::Mono` and adds a real-backend regression test. This fix is on `main`, not in the immutable RC9 artifact; RC9 remains failed for the `TERM=dumb` subcase. A new immutable RC and affected-gate requalification are required before any stable release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:287:**Custody and remaining acceptance:** Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains OPEN and its latest update is 17:37:53 UTC; no custodian response or assignee is recorded. No private held-out payload was accessed, and held-out qualification has not started. The repository's latest human terminal matrix status is 0/15; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute for those operator cells. Current-source provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC9 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; the existing publication authorization remains gated on every required release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:469:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:582:- **PR and contest state:** PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-`main` candidate. Its CI and CodeQL checks are green, but it is not a release acceptance or publication. PR #102 is open at `3756afe05dbd75c4e6929d87cd50facbb8ab1748`, based on `8f4504e`, to record a synthetic qualification-host preflight; its CodeQL and TypeScript checks passed and its Node matrix was still running at this checkpoint. The preflight report records 10/10 checks using only an empty synthetic marker store; it does not establish private corpus custody or qualification acceptance. The contest has concluded; no contest freeze applies. Historical contest artifacts remain historical evidence only.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:586:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:763:- The installed-package startup PTY smoke reached the Nexus prompt under isolated HOME. This does not satisfy the §5.2 scripted PTY set or the §5.3 human matrix. An attempted legacy §5.2 driver was invalid: its checkout-layout paths and wait condition do not match the current RC startup/trust prompt; its mock gateway recorded zero requests. No product pass/fail was inferred.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:774:| Scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) | Not established; legacy driver invocation was invalid. | Use an RC-compatible driver or otherwise execute all listed scenarios against the installed package and mock gateway, with measured outcomes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:5:> **Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** No cell runs or evidence are required, and no cell result is inferred. Blank cells are not a release blocker. The worksheet remains available for optional operator checks. Automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates remain mandatory.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:43:For v1.0.0, manual runs are waived by [DEC-20](DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver). If optional manual checks are performed, record only what was actually observed. Such checks do not replace mandatory automated CI (§5.1) or scripted PTY (§5.2) evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:74:- This worksheet does not establish acceptance of mandatory automated CI (§5.1) or scripted PTY (§5.2) gates.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:159:- **Manual real-terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** No manual five-terminal by three-size runs or per-cell evidence are claimed. The automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory release gates and must pass.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:162:The manual-matrix waiver does not affect any other acceptance gate. Installed-RC platform and lifecycle evidence, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, automated and scripted PTY gates, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger remain governed by the release decision record.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, automated and scripted PTY terminal gates. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:83:8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal acceptance.** Automated CI checks in ACCEPTANCE §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 are mandatory. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-20](../DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver); no operator runs or cell results are required or implied. Screenshot artifacts are separately waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) is superseded for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/README.md:19:These results cover scripted mock-gateway PTY scenarios only. They do not establish the manual five-terminal × three-size matrix (`ACC-TUI-MANUAL`), all-state accessibility, real provider qualification, held-out task quality, standalone gateway qualification, independent acceptance, or power-loss recovery. The partial installed-RC9 `NO_COLOR` / `TERM=dumb` probe is recorded under [`accessibility/`](accessibility/README.md): the `NO_COLOR=1` cells pass, but `TERM=dumb` emits color reset SGR sequences and fails that criterion. Failed or superseded harness attempts remain preserved outside this evidence directory under `/var/tmp/nexus-rc9-pty-4cae11c/attempt*`; they are not counted as passing evidence.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/manifest.json:8:  \"scope\": \"Installed package scripted E3 PTY only, synthetic mock gateway and disposable workspaces.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md:7:The scripted probe sampled ten readable UI states: idle, help, model picker, streaming, cancelled turn, approval, completion, tool running, tool cancellation, and endpoint error. It exercised `xterm-256color` with `NO_COLOR=1` and `TERM=dumb` with `NO_COLOR` unset, each at 40×14 and 100×30. Raw PTY streams and decoded screen snapshots are preserved per attempt.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027/corrected-approval-path/README.md:17:`run_corrected.py` launches `mockgw_overlay.py` and the installed RC10 TUI via the existing isolated PTY driver. The driver uses the installed package path documented in the surrounding evidence bundle. `approval_timing.raw`, `approval_timing.screens.txt`, and `approval_timing.notes.txt` preserve the terminal output; `gw.log` preserves the synthetic request/tool-result sequence.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UPGRADE-ATTESTATION-20261025/README.md:30:- New acceptance test (`refuses an upgrade that requires attestation when gh is unavailable`) injects an empty\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":885974474}},"started_at_ms":1793296168205,"completed_at_ms":1793296169092}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:49:31.194Z","ordinal":494953,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a188c8-00ba-7893-a4ef-a745f2fb9aa7","call_id":"call_c0be5f8d07de4f888bfc01bf3e44c3ba","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8717)\nTotal output lines: 250\n\n48-| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n49-| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n50-| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n51:| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\n52-| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n53-<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n54-\n--\n62-## 1. Rules\n63-\n64-1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65:2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n66-3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n67-4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n68-   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n--\n76-\n77-| ID | Environment | Used for |\n78-|---|---|---|\n79:| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81-| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82-| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n--\n107-\n108-| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n109-|---|---|---|\n110:| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n111:| ACC-TUI-A11Y | PTY with `NO_COLOR=1` and with `TERM=dumb` at 40×14 and 100×30 | Zero colour SGR codes. Every state is distinguishable by glyph and word. Hints are complete at 40 columns (TUI-10). |\n112-| ACC-SEC-JAIL | `core/tests` plus harness-core calls with `..`, absolute, symlinked-file, symlinked-dir and symlinked-parent payloads | Every one is refused (C §4 R1 set). |\n113-| ACC-SEC-B6 | Re-run `docs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/repro/zz_trust_repro.test.ts`. Seeded-secret scan of `~/.nexus` and `.nexus` after a scripted turn. | Zero plaintext seeded secrets in durable stores or outbound bodies. |\n114-| ACC-PRV-LIVE | `nexus providers verify --provider <p> -m <pinned model> -j` for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06) | `passed: true`. Receipts archived. |\n--\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119-| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120-| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121:| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n--\n158-\n159-## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n160-\n161:### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n162-\n163-These must pass:\n164-\n--\n171-- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n172-- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n173-- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n174:- new: the package PTY smoke\n175-\n176:### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n177-\n178-These are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n179-\n--\n187-| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n188-| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n189-\n190:### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n191-\n192:**Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix below is not a release gate; no operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell evidence are required, and none are claimed. Automated CI checks in §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n193-\n194-Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n195-\n--\n277-| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n278-| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n279-| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n280:| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n281-| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n282-| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n283-| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n--\n333-- [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n334-- [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n335-- [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n336:- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n337-- [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n338-- [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n339-- [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n\n### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n\n9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n\n1. refused connection mid-turn\n2. 5xx / overlo…4717 tokens truncated…signee is recorded. No private held-out payload was accessed, and held-out qualification has not started. The repository's latest human terminal matrix status is 0/15; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute for those operator cells. Current-source provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC9 is unaccepted and stable `v1.0.0` is unpublished. Acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; the existing publication authorization remains gated on every required release acceptance.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:469:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:582:- **PR and contest state:** PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-`main` candidate. Its CI and CodeQL checks are green, but it is not a release acceptance or publication. PR #102 is open at `3756afe05dbd75c4e6929d87cd50facbb8ab1748`, based on `8f4504e`, to record a synthetic qualification-host preflight; its CodeQL and TypeScript checks passed and its Node matrix was still running at this checkpoint. The preflight report records 10/10 checks using only an empty synthetic marker store; it does not establish private corpus custody or qualification acceptance. The contest has concluded; no contest freeze applies. Historical contest artifacts remain historical evidence only.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:586:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:763:- The installed-package startup PTY smoke reached the Nexus prompt under isolated HOME. This does not satisfy the §5.2 scripted PTY set or the §5.3 human matrix. An attempted legacy §5.2 driver was invalid: its checkout-layout paths and wait condition do not match the current RC startup/trust prompt; its mock gateway recorded zero requests. No product pass/fail was inferred.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:774:| Scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) | Not established; legacy driver invocation was invalid. | Use an RC-compatible driver or otherwise execute all listed scenarios against the installed package and mock gateway, with measured outcomes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:5:> **Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** No cell runs or evidence are required, and no cell result is inferred. Blank cells are not a release blocker. The worksheet remains available for optional operator checks. Automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates remain mandatory.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:43:For v1.0.0, manual runs are waived by [DEC-20](DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver). If optional manual checks are performed, record only what was actually observed. Such checks do not replace mandatory automated CI (§5.1) or scripted PTY (§5.2) evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md:74:- This worksheet does not establish acceptance of mandatory automated CI (§5.1) or scripted PTY (§5.2) gates.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:159:- **Manual real-terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** No manual five-terminal by three-size runs or per-cell evidence are claimed. The automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory release gates and must pass.\ndocs/releases/v1.0.0.md:162:The manual-matrix waiver does not affect any other acceptance gate. Installed-RC platform and lifecycle evidence, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, automated and scripted PTY gates, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger remain governed by the release decision record.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, automated and scripted PTY terminal gates. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:83:8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal acceptance.** Automated CI checks in ACCEPTANCE §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 are mandatory. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-20](../DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver); no operator runs or cell results are required or implied. Screenshot artifacts are separately waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) is superseded for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.9/terminal-scripted/README.md:19:These results cover scripted mock-gateway PTY scenarios only. They do not establish the manual five-terminal × three-size matrix (`ACC-TUI-MANUAL`), all-state accessibility, real provider qualification, held-out task quality, standalone gateway qualification, independent acceptance, or power-loss recovery. The partial installed-RC9 `NO_COLOR` / `TERM=dumb` probe is recorded under [`accessibility/`](accessibility/README.md): the `NO_COLOR=1` cells pass, but `TERM=dumb` emits color reset SGR sequences and fails that criterion. Failed or superseded harness attempts remain preserved outside this evidence directory under `/var/tmp/nexus-rc9-pty-4cae11c/attempt*`; they are not counted as passing evidence.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/manifest.json:8:  \"scope\": \"Installed package scripted E3 PTY only, synthetic mock gateway and disposable workspaces.\",\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/README.md:7:The scripted probe sampled ten readable UI states: idle, help, model picker, streaming, cancelled turn, approval, completion, tool running, tool cancellation, and endpoint error. It exercised `xterm-256color` with `NO_COLOR=1` and `TERM=dumb` with `NO_COLOR` unset, each at 40×14 and 100×30. Raw PTY streams and decoded screen snapshots are preserved per attempt.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-scripted/accessibility/overlay-expansion-20261027/corrected-approval-path/README.md:17:`run_corrected.py` launches `mockgw_overlay.py` and the installed RC10 TUI via the existing isolated PTY driver. The driver uses the installed package path documented in the surrounding evidence bundle. `approval_timing.raw`, `approval_timing.screens.txt`, and `approval_timing.notes.txt` preserve the terminal output; `gw.log` preserves the synthetic request/tool-result sequence.\ndocs/reviews/evidence/v1/DEFECT-UPGRADE-ATTESTATION-20261025/README.md:30:- New acceptance test (`refuses an upgrade that requires attestation when gh is unavailable`) injects an empty\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a188b4-bcfd-7801-8430-e45b95efb101","create_time":1793296171.1943657}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
