{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:55:17.064Z","ordinal":495196,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae38884608481a0807b361fd5cf2a0b","status":"completed","call_id":"call_165adb5309e547d2b7e7490ec1ab5714","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '159,194p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; find scripts/terminal-acceptance -maxdepth 3 -type f -print; sed -n '1,220p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:4500});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a188ca-3438-7770-bdcd-730c68c81c88","create_time":1793296516.3870845}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:55:17.191Z","ordinal":495197,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188ca-3438-7770-bdcd-730c68c81c88","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a188ca-3438-7770-bdcd-730c68c81c88","response_id":"resp_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae38878257081a096e8e52c21d52e3d","usage":{"input_tokens":181959,"cached_input_tokens":180736,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1300,"reasoning_output_tokens":1183,"total_tokens":183259},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":3325383,"cached_input_tokens":3304832,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":10544,"reasoning_output_tokens":7280,"total_tokens":3335927},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9182898395,"cached_input_tokens":9082980480,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26360580,"reasoning_output_tokens":15299669,"total_tokens":9209258975}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:55:19.172Z","ordinal":495198,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188ca-3438-7770-bdcd-730c68c81c88","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bb397855-3807-49a7-8058-b639d45fe476","process_id":"46961","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '159,194p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; find scripts/terminal-acceptance -maxdepth 3 -type f -print; sed -n '1,220p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '159,194p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"list_files","cmd":"find scripts/terminal-acceptance -maxdepth 3 -type f -print","path":"terminal-acceptance"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,220p' scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n|---|---|\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\n**Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix below is not a release gate; no operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell evidence are required, and none are claimed. Automated CI checks in §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/scope-procs.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/mockgw.py\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\n# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n\nA human may run this procedure against the **installed RC** for optional terminal checks. For v1.0.0, the manual matrix is waived by DEC-20; these runs are not a release gate. Automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) remain mandatory.\n\n**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n- xterm\n- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n- the VS Code integrated terminal\n- GNOME Terminal\n\n**Optional check:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition if these optional checks are run.\n\n**v1.0.0 disposition:** DEC-20 waives the manual 5×3 matrix. DEC-18 separately waives screenshot artifacts for\n`v1.0.0-rc.N`. Other release series retain their applicable terminal acceptance and screenshot requirements.\nAutomated PTY evidence remains mandatory under ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.2.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n   not resolve into a checkout.\n2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n3. You need `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n\n## Each cell\n\nOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n\n```sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\nthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n\n| # | You do | You judge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides |\n| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, and the mock request log. If you provide both optional screenshots, their hashes are also recorded.\nA cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed attempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Screenshot presence does not\nchange the gate. Commit the evidence directory to the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":897521137}},"started_at_ms":1793296518274,"completed_at_ms":1793296519172}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T17:55:20.341Z","ordinal":495199,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a188cd-5495-7d73-af11-f606d8c89f54","call_id":"call_165adb5309e547d2b7e7490ec1ab5714","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n### 5.1 CI PTY suites (E1)\n\nThese must pass:\n\n- `tui_approval_input_e2e`\n- `tui_diff_e2e`\n- `tui_maturity_e2e`\n- `tui_model_picker_e2e`\n- `tui_multiline_e2e`\n- `tui_surface_e2e`\n- new: `repl_approval_e2e`\n- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\n- new: `startup_unreachable_e2e`\n- new: the package PTY smoke\n\n### 5.2 Scripted PTY scenarios against the installed RC (E3, mock gateway)\n\nThese are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n\n| Scenario | Pass condition |\n|---|---|\n| s1 startup, unreachable endpoint | The endpoint is named, with a fix hint. The turn ends with guidance in ≤ 2.5 min. |\n| s2 approval under continuous typing, paste and burst, at 40×14 | No decision is made by stray input. A deliberate key decides. |\n| s3 completion | The outcome is shown in words: VERIFIED, REGRESSION_FREE or UNVERIFIED. |\n| s4–s6 cancel and steer | Cancel is acknowledged within 1 frame and idle within 5 s. Steering is applied. |\n| s7 resume | The prior conversation is shown. |\n| s8–s9 cancel or quit during a tool | Zero surviving processes. |\n| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\n**Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix below is not a release gate; no operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell evidence are required, and none are claimed. Automated CI checks in §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/test-scope-procs.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/scope-procs.sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/mockgw.py\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\n# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n\nA human may run this procedure against the **installed RC** for optional terminal checks. For v1.0.0, the manual matrix is waived by DEC-20; these runs are not a release gate. Automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) remain mandatory.\n\n**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n- xterm\n- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n- the VS Code integrated terminal\n- GNOME Terminal\n\n**Optional check:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition if these optional checks are run.\n\n**v1.0.0 disposition:** DEC-20 waives the manual 5×3 matrix. DEC-18 separately waives screenshot artifacts for\n`v1.0.0-rc.N`. Other release series retain their applicable terminal acceptance and screenshot requirements.\nAutomated PTY evidence remains mandatory under ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.2.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n   not resolve into a checkout.\n2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n3. You need `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n\n## Each cell\n\nOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n\n```sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\nthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n\n| # | You do | You judge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides |\n| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, and the mock request log. If you provide both optional screenshots, their hashes are also recorded.\nA cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed attempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Screenshot presence does not\nchange the gate. Commit the evidence directory to the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a188ca-3438-7770-bdcd-730c68c81c88","create_time":1793296520.341246}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
