t payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, standalone/provider qualification, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n240:**RC10 installation and terminal preparation:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains an unaccepted prerelease from `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; Linux x86_64 archive SHA-256 is `444d0812ad583b7f688890ac8536cb872e92364c977d9fbf298fa0408d98b3e7`. The linked [RC10 desktop preflight record](../reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/terminal-manual-preflight/README.md) documents successful provenance-verified installation to an isolated qualification prefix on `ubuntu-desktop` (`10.0.8.3`), with CLI identity `1.0.0-rc.10 (16ee8ca36438)`. xterm, kitty, GNOME Terminal, tmux, and VS Code are present. This prepares the host only: the human matrix remains **0/15**. The operator must perform each of the five terminal environments at all three sizes and provide two genuine screenshots and a verdict per cell; scripted PTY evidence does not substitute.\n242:**Remaining exact-RC and release gates:** PR [#264](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/264) archives RC10 scripted observations and keeps the manual matrix separate; its remote head is `73bdc7d91b1b8925b522b052d89228d99bad4893` on a stale base, with all reported exact-head checks successful. Its manual worksheet is blank. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) still lacks custodian acceptance; the sealed public manifest alone is not private custody acceptance, and no held-out payload was accessed or run. T2/T3/T4, standalone qualification, full installed-RC provider coverage, exact-RC cross-runner checks, the manual matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release is published; publication authorization remains granted but gated by acceptance.\n252:**Terminal observation and acceptance:** The user reports that the client rendered