C qualification, required human terminal behavior, and independent exact-RC acceptance gates remain outstanding. Stable publication remains gated.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Passing source CI and RC10-only provider/reproducibility evidence do not establish release acceptance. Existing publication authorization remains gated by acceptance.\n\nThe checkpoints below are retained as historical evidence; their source revision, PR, CI, and qualification statements are superseded by this observation.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 16:25 UTC; superseded)\n\n**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `145d464dd819a20bf918dfbb4f0176f2c4840a08`. Exact-head CI run [40720824591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40720824591) passed the Node 22 and Node 24 test matrices; the Linux packaging/reproducibility job was still running at observation time. CodeQL run [40720824319](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40720824319) passed. The CI jobs completed `sync-version --check` and the requirements checker successfully on this source. These results qualify the source revision only; they do not qualify an installed release candidate.\n\n**Release PRs:** PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is merged at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`, included in current main. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is based on `145d464` at exact head `49a2af0c1d556912d12b834aa7f2022ef63b528c`; its latest follow-up scopes checkout to the nested workspace and extends the regression to preserve both staged and unstaged sibling state. The prior nested-index delta at `662d084` was independently ACCEPTed (SHA-256 `61f4e40bc135152ffa003c82bdc31fc15703542b5bd9ba3b67f7b6b1edae1cb2`), and the checkout-scope delta was independently ACCEPTed by `review_pr302` (SHA-256 `26ce020bdc1f6865e194f02e45c6889eaa32415cc786a457fbcfae1ddaa78605`, tests not run). PR #302 CodeQL and JS/TS checks pass; Node 22/24 CI and Entire are running. TypeScript `--noEmit` and `git diff --check` passed on the prior delta; no local suite was run under the active SUITE claim.\n\nPR [#307](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/307) is based on `145d464` at `88bf19c817f8de7461faf9826e405e52630bb08f`. Its clean-checkout build-identity correction has an independent ACCEPT review for the exact diff (SHA-256 `c0c7b8be14de2cf1aab3246b2f34596ba4aae30c2d527c1afbe93e1ce0105295`); JS/TS, CodeQL and Node 22/24 pass, Linux packaging and Entire remain pending. PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) contains this readiness record at exact head `dded46ba54001bd511aefce4719839f4b77c85ef`; its corrected checkpoint has just been pushed and all exact-head checks are pending. PRs [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) and [#306](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/306) are explicitly v1.1 scope and are not part of the v1.0.0 merge path.\n\n**Requirements and qualification:** Current-main CI's requirements checker passes; the most recent explicit `--enforce` result was on PR #302 head `c3901774` before the nested-workspace-only follow-up: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to installed-RC qualification. RC10 has scope-limited exact-artifact evidence: OpenRouter pinned-model verification and one synthetic live task passed, and the cross-runner workflow passed for the six listed release artifacts across Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 and against published RC10 (run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805)). A later checkpoint correction incorrectly claimed this workflow failed because of an npm-version mismatch. That correction is superseded: GitHub records run `40564959805` and its `compare` job as completed successfully; the current checkpoint above reports that final result. This historical correction is retained here to preserve the audit trail. These results apply only to immutable RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`; they do not qualify a successor candidate or establish full release acceptance. The newly pushed #302 head must complete exact checks before its requirements evidence is refreshed. Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. GitHub installer is the selected distribution target; npm publication is inapplicable.\n\nIssue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; its last update was 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC, with no custodian response observed. No held-out payload was accessed and no held-out qualification was run. The manual terminal matrix's last recorded result is 0/15; terminal setup exists on Ubuntu, but no operator screenshots or cell verdicts have been supplied. Held-out/T2/T3/T4, remaining provider and standalone coverage, successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the human terminal matrix, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Source CI is mostly complete on `145d464`; PR #302's latest delta awaits independent review and exact Node 22/24 completion, while #307 has independent source review but exact PR checks remain pending. RC10 has passing, bounded provider and cross-runner evidence, but no accepted RC exists and mandatory qualification remains open. Publication authorization remains granted and gated by acceptance.\n\nThe checkpoint below (observed 2026-10-28 15:28 UTC) is retained as historical evidence and is superseded for source revision, CI, PR heads, and release-gate state.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 15:28 UTC; superseded)\n\n**Authoritative source and requirements gate:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212` (PR #304 merge). Current-main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) and CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) both completed SUCCESS on that exact revision. A clean detached worktree at that exact source ran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` with isolated `HOME`: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. This passes the source-stage enforcement gate only.\n\n**Release PRs and exact-head checks:** PRs [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) (`004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f`), [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) (`11dc196fcdd733f8de71dfc95ff70e109d8f4492`), [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) (`3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7`), and [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) (`97f1c6ead710bc059126ba65b37ad1e5fde17666`) are all based on `b2ae2fe`. Exact-head Node 22/24, Linux x86_64, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed for these candidates. Their Entire Gates checks are failures, so none is mergeable through the required workflow. PR #302's trail reports five high-severity findings and missing reviewer approval. The independent source reviewer ACCEPTed the cumulative diff after a partial source read and did not run tests as part of that review. A separate owner-authored PR update records `tsc --noEmit` and 53/53 targeted restore tests, and advises a second review of `checkpoint.ts` because of its size. PR #299, #300, and #305 also lack successful Entire approval. No findings were bypassed and no self-approval was recorded.\n\n**Local suite attempt:** On a disposable PR #302 snapshot at `3c52580ae1da6b7f1282018f4d3702dcb75f8bd7` plus a 30-line checkpoint-config patch (patch SHA-256 `c80330bc5eeab0ee0bfe73f32a1fcd40e5850c8bc4270e1e08b98758a6aee213`), `make build` completed, but `make test` exited nonzero at `cli/test/eval_version_probe_storage.test.ts:15` because the required `NEXUS_EVAL_TEST_WORKSPACE_ROOT` variable was not set in that run. CI provisions a 128 MiB tmpfs at `/mnt/nexus-eval-ci` and a public runtime root at `/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime`. At the latest host check, the tmpfs is mounted with the expected 0711 mode and the runtime root exists; that does not mean the failed run used those fixtures. The result is neither a full-suite pass nor evidence of a product defect. The `SUITE` claim remains held by `kimi-main` for focused `operation_git` regressions; its owner record remains in place, so no overlapping test was started.\n\n**Qualification, custody, and publication:** GitHub still lists [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) as the latest release; there is no `v1.0.0` tag or stable release. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned, with the last metadata-only custodian request at 2026-10-28 14:23 UTC and no response observed. No protected payload was accessed or qualification run. The manual terminal matrix remains 0/15; the final installed RC does not exist. Exact-RC held-out/T2/T3/T4, provider and standalone coverage, cross-runner reproducibility, human terminal evidence, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. The chosen distribution target remains the GitHub installer; npm publication is inapplicable.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. PR integration is blocked by required Entire review findings/approvals; exact-RC qualification is additionally blocked by independent held-out custody and the required human terminal matrix. Existing publication authorization remains granted but gated. The checkpoint below is retained as the 13:34 UTC snapshot and is superseded for current CI, requirements, PR checks, local suite result, and release status.\n\n## Superseded checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 13:34:51 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source:** `origin/main` is `b2ae2fe82640e44d58ef5418f49b46df03392212`, the PR #304 merge. Main CI [40693030763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030763) has Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs passed (13:23:35 and 13:23:05 UTC); Linux x86_64 remains in progress. CodeQL [40693030710](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40693030710) passed at 13:07:03 UTC. On a clean detached worktree at this exact head, `HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-home XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/tmp/nexus-req-xdg node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 requirements; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open, with 12 requirements deferred to exact-RC qualification. PR #304 adds opt-in v1.1 Git-aware operations to current main; its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. The independent review recorded an unresolved correctness defect: an explicit restart recreates a clean worktree while resuming the old agent conversation. That behavior must be fixed and requalified before an RC built from this main can be accepted.\n\n**Source PRs:** PR [#303](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/303) is integrated at `4cac22d`; its exact-head required CI and independent review passed. PR [#304](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/304) is integrated at `b2ae2fe`; its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, CodeQL and JS/TS checks passed and Entire Gates concluded neutral. Its independent review nevertheless found the restart/conversation defect above. PR [#305](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/305) addresses that defect at `f7e573ec8de98fb3ec24a96e148a84b4ccab151f`, with independent review ACCEPT at diff SHA-256 `cf1abd6ce5e7083aebe526efaaee85380dee295fced7814a7ddedcd609a11615`. Build and focused test TypeScript check passed; the runtime test was not run locally because `SUITE` is claimed by `kimi-main`. Exact-head Node 22 and Node 24 jobs in run `40694815985` both failed with 1,882 passed, 2 failed and 2 skipped: `durable_continuity.test.ts` expected the explicit-restart recovery warning, and `tdd_work_units.test.ts` uses a fake agent without `restartConversation`. JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed; Linux was skipped after the matrix failures, and Entire Gates remain pending. PR [#299](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/299) is at `004234de6d8599d71083b4f686c1bdbffe21dd2f` on base `b2ae2fe`; independent review ACCEPTed this exact head at diff SHA-256 `55afcdc8ed8044bb0aa0a54932c5ba6513763b564bc8fb76014b3334db33ae38`. Its Node 22/24 jobs are in progress, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, and Entire Gates are pending. Issue [#298](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/298) remains open until its fix is integrated and current-main checks pass. At the 13:34:51 UTC snapshot cutoff, before the readiness-only correction was pushed, PR [#300](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/300) was at `e1974fd82dba1aba8e5e2e5b1bc9cf964fe6db20` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24 and Entire were in progress, while JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed. The subsequent documentation-only update restarted exact-head checks; the claim record tracks its latest head and current statuses. The independent factual review found stale status/head references in the prior checkpoint; corrected evidence is pending re-review. PR [#302](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/302) is at `659d6a63a8708ebe98240ec1937b0f2acdcdfac4` on base `b2ae2fe`; Node 22/24, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL passed, while Linux x86_64 (run `40693955666`) is in progress and Entire Gates are pending. Independent read-only review ACCEPTed the final cumulative diff `1099e6ff6b68ab9907ac66c908bf45c8ab1af338d3b6a14227d45d60cf35dc29`; no tests were run as part of review. Exact-head CI is still pending.\n\n**Requested codebase-review findings:** The prior checkpoint's implementation and evidence summary remains applicable; the current main includes the capability-category split, scheduler extraction, operation-runner decomposition, bounded diagnostics, `DecisionRejected` guidance, lifecycle tests, and 100 fixed-seed scheduler invariants. The operator config remains intentionally limited to `operationPolicy`; general runtime-default customization is not claimed.\n\n**Runtime identity dogfooding defect:** The user-reported RC8 behavior in which a Claude-specific skill led the model to describe Nexus as Claude Code has a source fix in merged PR [#273](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/273), integrated at `d97ccb70c87db096c75e1bd4ff58dbcdf0aa8ab1` (PR merge commit `e94208d09cb4d5023e4379187fc6c603bba960d2`). The fixed system prompt states Nexus Code is the host and is appended after workspace skills; activated skills are also prefaced with `Host application: Nexus Code`. `cli/test/agent_runtime_identity.test.ts` reproduces a Claude model plus Claude-specific skill and verifies both boundaries. That test passed 1/1 in an isolated exact-main `b293b44` snapshot; PR #273's Node 22/24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript, and CodeQL checks passed, and exact-main CI also passed. The public RC10 tag (`16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`) predates the PR merge, so this fix still needs verification in the successor RC.\n\n**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` is still the latest release (published 2026-10-27); the package at `b293b44` is also `1.0.0-rc.10`, so source changes require a successor RC before installed-RC qualification. No accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 exists. Held-out issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open; its latest public status request was posted 2026-10-28 12:42 UTC, with no custodian response as of this checkpoint. The public 40-task manifest is not custody acceptance, and no held-out qualification has started. T2/T3/T4, evaluator/custody acceptance, remaining provider and standalone gates, cross-runner reproducibility, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix remains 0/15; the Ubuntu desktop has setup evidence only, with no qualifying screenshots or cell verdicts recorded.\n\n**Disposition:** Engineering convergence remains active; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. No RC is accepted and no stable release is published. Public RC10 remains the latest release; the repository target is the GitHub installer (npm publication is inapplicable per operator decision). Continue source remediation and exact-head review/CI, then build and qualify a successor RC only after pre-RC gates and PR #305's restart fix pass; keep all installed-RC gates bound to that exact artifact.\n\nThe 07:55 checkpoint below is retained as historical evidence; its source, CI, PR, and qualification state is superseded by this checkpoint.\n\n## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-28 07:55 UTC)\n\n**Authoritative source and source checks:** `origin/main` is `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4`, merge commit for PR [#297](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/297). Its exact-head Node 22/24, Linux, JS/TS, and CodeQL checks passed; Entire Gates was neutral. Post-merge CI [40652572596](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572596) is running and CodeQL [40652572591](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40652572591) passed. Exact-main CI [40647479745](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40647479745) completed successfully on its parent source commit `ceaf60072b7c364edac523d2517fb12df8f5f6cd`, including Node 22/24 tests, Linux tests, packaging, reproducibility, SBOM, and installer checks. The requirements gate also passed on exact current main `7970958749fc17be3b0ef4bb725b8e2f0d825ed4` in an isolated worktree (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 applicable release-qualifi\n... command output truncated for persistence ...\nPR #288 restored t