nd Node metadata claimed by the README; and the positive-cell script sets `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` without documenting that limitation. Treat the matrix as a recorded result, not independently accepted E2 evidence, until the archive and claims are corrected and reviewed. The single Ubuntu 22.04/Node 22 lifecycle script re-runs the installer for alpha.2→RC10, rollback, reinstall and repair; it does not exercise `nexus upgrade` or the separate self-test-failure, crash-recovery and backup-restore acceptance rows. Other lifecycle cases and platforms remain open. All evidence applies only to installed RC10.\n\n**PR #284 lifecycle follow-up:** PR [#284](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/284) added RC10 checksum-tamper, failed-self-test, backup-restore and updater-process-crash scripts and logs, then merged at `7ddce16a` despite an independent CHANGES_REQUIRED review. Its exact-head CI run [40586513330](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40586513330) passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL. The independent review found the updated checksum index still has 21 missing files out of 45; the earlier lifecycle path still does not test successful `nexus upgrade`; the `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` bypass is not clearly disclosed; and the process-crash script does not verify the claimed staging cleanup. The merged code therefore does not close the E2 archive or lifecycle evidence gaps. Its process-death recovery result explicitly does not test power loss. The post-merge main CI and CodeQL runs subsequently passed on `7ddce16a`.\n\n**Readiness PR #268:** Its remote head remains `eac6cdb452726368d37a8ca373b56c688e0274da` on the older base `fc582c66`; its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux, JavaScript/TypeScript and CodeQL checks all passed on that older candidate. The refreshed local readiness candidate `a3bb9e59e56e08de66ea5b7eaf682ce408b2e57f` includes current main `7ddce16a` and received independent ACCEPT from `rc5_