{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T18:09:04.473Z","ordinal":495683,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a188d9-e7d9-7f40-9e83-d916a035410c","call_id":"call_20699495c7704d49832a6a256dfcb42f","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/heldout_public_coverage_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"No ownership or handoff change is visible. At `origin/main` `cbb3b653a6bb6060071d8927e08e30d63765865e`, issue #1 remains open and unassigned; its latest comment (#6483900189) reports no custodian update and no qualification runs. The Agent Mail directory shows no active project windows or designated custodian, and the public claims log has no held-out handoff record.\\n\\nThe remaining external dependency is a reachable owner identifying the designated custodian or assigning a replacement, followed by an acknowledged handoff. That custodian must handle the legacy-to-`blackbox-v1` conversion or replacement, private validation, and renewed custody acceptance before qualification. I did not contact anyone or access private corpus material.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — reviewed base `fe1c91dbcb56693a34c06dd3719bea139f639833` to HEAD `7fe2981d6e9a379ff06804b829cb9200fe7a8dbe`, including the uncommitted two-file fix. Cumulative tracked-tree diff SHA-256: `41cb848ae19bdc60dc6d4e91c7558ea444079e584ff7569ba0c841dee1e526b3`.\\n\\nThe new `isUtf8` check validates the complete compiler-result buffer before writing it for the caller to decode ([`scan-compiler-exposure.mjs`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs:236)). The regression places an invalid-byte directory below a valid root-level directory, so it reaches the recursive compiler-result stream and exercises that exact check ([`eval_integrity.test.ts`](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds/cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts:579)). Invalid output causes a nonzero scanner result, which the caller treats as a failed preflight. I found no remaining fail-open path in this correction.\\n\\nThe earlier cancellation concern is also addressed by the killable root-enumeration child and SIGTERM/reaping regression. This is a static review only; I did not run suites or verify CI.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a188ca-3438-7770-bdcd-730c68c81c88","create_time":1793297344.4733663}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
