{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T18:11:07.360Z","ordinal":495766,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188ca-3438-7770-bdcd-730c68c81c88","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-aec5d46c-1549-4192-964e-cf7515dac224","process_id":"80798","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 324 --json title,body,files,commits --jq '{title,body,files:[.files[].path],commits:[.commits[].oid]}' && gh pr diff 324 | sed -n '1,240p'; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json -print | rg 'ACCEPTANCE|DECISION|REQUIREMENT' | head -30"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 324 --json title,body,files,commits --jq '{title,body,files:[.files[].path],commits:[.commits[].oid]}' && gh pr diff 324 | sed -n '1,240p'; find .git/nexus-claims -maxdepth 2 -name owner.json -print | rg 'ACCEPTANCE|DECISION|REQUIREMENT' | head -30"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- entire-trail-link-start --\\u003e\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/39/changes/nexus-code/39\\n\\u003c!-- entire-trail-link-end --\\u003e\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Record the release owner's v1.0.0 waiver of the manual five-terminal by three-size §5.3 matrix.\\n- Keep automated CI PTY (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) mandatory.\\n- Reconcile ACCEPTANCE, DECISIONS, SPEC-10, PLAN-10, REQUIREMENTS, READINESS, the worksheet, terminal procedure, and release notes.\\n- Keep REQ-QUAL-108 partial and do not imply any manual-cell pass.\\n\\n## Validation and review\\n\\n- `git diff --check` passed.\\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passed in report mode (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open).\\n- `node cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs test/check_requirements.test.ts` passed 27/27 with isolated HOME.\\n- An enforce-mode run on the dirty worktree correctly refused to evaluate it; no enforce-mode pass is claimed.\\n- Independent read-only review ACCEPTed exact diff SHA-256 `f184c64592df59452d60ebd575b9af500a43edb509535454538160135a46f620`.\\n- Exact-head CI and CodeQL are running for `965667501f87c26f164646e52b8633812518e8a5`.\\n\\nAcceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; this decision waives only ACC-TUI-MANUAL for v1.0.0.\",\"commits\":[\"965667501f87c26f164646e52b8633812518e8a5\"],\"files\":[\"docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/README.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\",\"scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\"],\"title\":\"docs(release): waive manual terminal matrix for v1.0.0\"}\ndiff --git a/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md b/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\nindex 314465cd..3b38c5d4 100644\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@ nexus doctor\n \n ## Release qualification and waivers\n \n-- **Manual real-terminal matrix: required and not yet accepted.** The fifteen-cell manual E3 matrix (xterm, kitty, tmux in GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60) requires actual operator runs on the exact installed RC with a verdict and observed outcomes recorded for each cell. Automated CI and PTY scenarios do not substitute for this evidence. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18; DEC-19 withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record.\n+- **Manual real-terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** No manual five-terminal by three-size runs or per-cell evidence are claimed. The automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory release gates and must pass.\n - **Screenshot artifacts: waived** for v1.0.0 by [DEC-18](../v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver).\n \n-The screenshot-artifact waiver does not affect any other acceptance gate. Installed-RC platform and lifecycle evidence, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, the manual terminal matrix, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger remain governed by the release decision record.\n+The manual-matrix waiver does not affect any other acceptance gate. Installed-RC platform and lifecycle evidence, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, automated and scripted PTY gates, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger remain governed by the release decision record.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nindex 80f4647a..3cf61ecb 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `\n | REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n | REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n | REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n-| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n+| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\n | REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n <!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n \n@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n | ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | All 15 cells have actual manual execution, recorded PASS/FAIL verdicts, observed outcomes, and evidence bound to the exact installed RC. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 do not substitute for these cells. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18. |\n+| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No manual-cell execution or evidence is required, and no result is inferred. Automated §5.1 and scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory. |\n \n ## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n \n@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@ These are ports of `evidence/D_pty/`.\n \n ### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n \n-**Required for v1.0.0.** Run every terminal × size combination below against the exact installed RC and record a verdict and observed outcomes for each cell. Automated suites in §5.1 and §5.2 remain required but do not replace operator execution. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. See [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n+**Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix below is not a release gate; no operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell evidence are required, and none are claimed. Automated CI checks in §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n \n Terminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n \n@@ -333,7 +333,7 @@ G6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable\n - [ ] G0–G4 automated gates pass on the final RC commit (§3).\n - [ ] RC artifact gates pass on the workflow-produced RC, including ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08; record the exact source commit, workflow run, and artifact digest.\n - [ ] §4 standalone and provider matrix: all rows PASS.\n-- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: CI and scripted gates PASS, and all 15 manual real-terminal cells have verified operator evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshots only.\n+- [ ] §5 terminal acceptance: automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates PASS. The manual 5×3 matrix (§5.3) is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n - [ ] §6 thresholds: all hold.\n - [ ] §7 install matrix: all rows PASS.\n - [ ] §8 independent acceptance: ACCEPT, or ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS with owner dispositions and no blocker defects outstanding.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\nindex d081f852..07353a01 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\n@@ -258,6 +258,20 @@ This amendment is **narrow by design**. It applies only to corpora where the mea\n \n **Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §5.3 / ACC-TUI-MANUAL; ACCEPTANCE §10 G6; SPEC-10 REQ-QUAL-108; `TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md`; PLAN-10 task 12; READINESS; release notes.\n \n+## DEC-20: v1.0.0 manual terminal-matrix waiver\n+\n+**Status: accepted by the release owner, 2026-10-29.** This decision supersedes DEC-19 for v1.0.0.\n+\n+**Direction.** The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in ACCEPTANCE §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No manual operator run, cell verdict, or per-cell evidence is required, and the waiver does not claim that any cell passed. The automated CI gate in §5.1 and the scripted installed-RC PTY gate in §5.2 remain mandatory and must pass.\n+\n+**Scope.** This waiver applies only to ACC-TUI-MANUAL and only for v1.0.0. It does not waive ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, exact-RC identity, any §5.1 or §5.2 scenario, safety checks, or any other release gate. DEC-18's screenshot-artifact waiver remains recorded; no screenshots are required for a matrix that is not run.\n+\n+**Qualification applicability:** REQ-QUAL-108 = ACC-TUI-STEER and ACC-TUI-A11Y remain required; ACC-TUI-MANUAL is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n+\n+**Disclosure.** Report ACC-TUI-MANUAL as waived by this decision, not passed and not outstanding. Preserve historical operator observations as observations only; do not promote them to cell results.\n+\n+**Affected:** ACCEPTANCE §§1.1, 3.1, 5, and 10; REQ-QUAL-108 exact-RC evidence mapping; stable v1.0.0 release notes; READINESS; terminal-matrix worksheet disposition.\n+\n ## Owner and external actions required (not performed by the audit)\n \n | # | Action | Why | When |\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex 35d905b7..29c34f53 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n-## Current release checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 06:18 UTC)\n+## Terminal waiver disposition update (observed 2026-10-29 13:12 UTC)\n+\n+The release owner accepted DEC-20: the manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in Acceptance §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0. No operator runs, cell verdicts, or per-cell results are required or inferred. Automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory. This update changes the terminal disposition only; the release, PR, CI, and custody details in the checkpoint below remain the historical 06:18 UTC snapshot and are not refreshed here.\n+\n+## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 06:18 UTC; superseded for terminal disposition by DEC-20 above)\n \n **Authoritative source and CI:** `origin/main` is `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`, merging PR #319 atop `6b786d54dd5bf60234c67fec6ef070c62af9b141`. `origin/v1/integration` remains at `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78`, an ancestor of main. Pre-merge main CodeQL run [40822684525](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684525) and CI run [40822684551](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40822684551) passed on `6b786d54`. Post-merge CI [40828157972](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40828157972) and CodeQL [40828157982](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40828157982) are in progress on exact main `a0356c4d8f0f0b9b943d4033aff59795fcab83b4`.\n \n@@ -10,9 +14,9 @@\n \n **Held-out custody and qualification:** The latest public metadata update on issue #1 (06:02 UTC) records unresolved custody ownership: a historical handoff log names SageBridge as an accepted successor, while the active custody record still names OpenCode. The latest posted T2 count is 20/40 tasks; no new custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. The custodian identity and acknowledged transfer must be reconciled before qualification. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\n \n-**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires actual operator execution for xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. There are **0/15 accepted cells**. The operator's partial RC10 report says the client rendered at tested sizes except tmux inside GNOME Terminal, which could not be resized below 43×13; other results “seemed okay.” The report lacks test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes, so it does not complete any cell. Automated PTY results do not count. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal programs; the successor RC is not yet available for the matrix. Screenshots are waived by DEC-18 only; all interactive checks and per-cell verdicts remain mandatory under DEC-19. The latest public release is `v1.0.0-rc.10`; the selected distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\n+**Terminal and release gates:** Acceptance §5.3 requires actual operator execution for xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. There are **0/15 accepted cells**. The operator's partial RC10 report says the client rendered at tested sizes except tmux inside GNOME Terminal, which could not be resized below 43×13; other results “seemed okay.” The report lacks test time, exact installed artifact identity, terminal versions, and per-cell check outcomes, so it does not complete any cell. Automated PTY results do not count. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal programs; the successor RC is not yet available for the matrix. Screenshots are waived by DEC-18 only; all interactive checks and per-cell verdicts remain mandatory under DEC-19. The latest public release at this checkpoint is `v1.0.0-rc.10`; the selected distribution target is the GitHub installer, not npm. No stable `v1.0.0` release exists.\n \n-**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on complete mandatory acceptance. PR #319 is integrated; main post-merge CI is running. PRs #320 and #322 are in exact-head Linux validation, PR #321 is rebased with fresh checks pending, and PR #318 needs the toolchain change integrated and its exact-base qualification rerun. Exact-RC construction and qualification remain gated on pre-RC source readiness and complete independent custody acceptance; terminal operator evidence is still required before independent RC acceptance.\n+**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on complete mandatory acceptance. PR #319 is integrated; main post-merge CI is running. PRs #320 and #322 are in exact-head Linux validation, PR #321 is rebased with fresh checks pending, and PR #318 needs the toolchain change integrated and its exact-base qualification rerun. Exact-RC construction and qualification remain gated on pre-RC source readiness and complete independent custody acceptance; terminal operator evidence is still required before independent RC acceptance at this checkpoint.\n \n ## Historical checkpoint (observed 2026-10-29 04:23 UTC; superseded)\n \n@@ -24,7 +28,7 @@\n \n **Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The claims identify OpenCode as the prior/current custodian workflow, but do not verify the responsible human identity; SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The successor T2 store remains 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust tasks need the reviewed, pinned-toolchain change integrated. Reported T3 digest/schema/isolation checks are 8/8, which is not full T3 task-quality qualification. At 04:23 UTC the OpenCode custodian holds SUITE for two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted tasks with isolated HOME; a live validator child process was observed. This is custody revalidation, not held-out qualification; no result or custody acceptance is recorded. Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; the latest metadata-only correction was posted at 04:18 UTC. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, full T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\n \n-**Terminal gate:** The release owner requires all 15 manual terminal cells (five environments × three sizes) on the exact installed RC. The latest verified worksheet status is 0/15 accepted cells; blank cells remain incomplete. Actual operator execution and per-cell outcomes are mandatory; automated CI or PTY results do not substitute. [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waives screenshots only. [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal applications, but the manual matrix remains outstanding.\n+**Terminal gate:** The release owner requires all 15 manual terminal cells (five environments × three sizes) on the exact installed RC. The latest verified worksheet status is 0/15 accepted cells; blank cells remain incomplete. Actual operator execution and per-cell outcomes are mandatory; automated CI or PTY results do not substitute. [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver) waives screenshots only. [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record. `ubuntu-desktop` at `10.0.8.3` has the required terminal applications, but the manual matrix remains outstanding. This 04:23 snapshot predates DEC-20 and is superseded by the current checkpoint above.\n \n **Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/README.md b/docs/v1.0.0/README.md\nindex 3d770c07..b15b7567 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/README.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/README.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n This package is the evidence-based path from `v0.1.0-alpha.2` (audited at `db1ca55`, 2026-10-14) to v1.0.0.\n \n-**Verdict: v1.0.0 readiness is BLOCKED.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. Held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete. See [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for exact open requirements and gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n+**Historical verdict: v1.0.0 readiness was BLOCKED at the 2026-10-16 source-suite checkpoint.** Candidate source revision `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a` passed an isolated `make build` and full `make test` run on 2026-10-16 (Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087; zero skipped). This is source-suite evidence, not RC qualification. At that checkpoint, held-out task quality, T3/T4 qualification, standalone/provider qualification, the manual terminal matrix, package/install matrix on the RC, and independent RC acceptance remained incomplete. For v1.0.0, the manual matrix was later waived by DEC-20; see [the current readiness reconciliation](READINESS.md) for the current disposition and remaining gates. The contest entry remains a separate track; judging has concluded and no contest freeze applies.\n \n ## How to read it\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\nindex 36a1d2ea..aa502f71 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\n@@ -238,7 +238,7 @@ Every row has status **open** at `db1ca55` unless stated otherwise. In the \"Evid\n | REQ-QUAL-105 | TOP_TIER Q6; DEC-05 | T4 fault injection: 9 classes × 5 runs (DEC-05 amendment 2026-10-17: union of the nine distinct scenarios retained), 100% truthful outcomes. | failure / recovery | `eval/model_proxy.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-001; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"the model proxy injects each scheduled fault\", test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T4 (ACCEPTANCE §6.2) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n | REQ-QUAL-106 | Audit | Scoring integrity (symmetric infra handling, contamination, hidden tests). | validity | `eval/infra.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs` | TEST (EVL-002, EVL-003; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"contaminated runs leave the pass rate\", test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"infrastructure reruns use one rule\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-002, EVL-003, VER-07 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n | REQ-QUAL-107 | Standalone; DEC-06 | Standalone and provider live matrix. | standalone | — | HIST | open | ACCEPTANCE §4.2, §4.3 | **B** | HIST-08 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n-| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n+| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | Automated CI and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual real-terminal matrix is waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.2 | TEST (PTY suites in CI) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.2; manual matrix disposition: DEC-20 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n | REQ-QUAL-109 | eval/README T3 | T3 long tasks: 8 × 5. | long-task workflow | `eval/` | — | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.3 | RR | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n | REQ-QUAL-110 | Audit | T1 self-test and a T4 smoke run in `make test`. | regression | `eval_harness.test.ts` | TEST (test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke: an overloaded endpoint is waited out\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | RR | — | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\nindex 7d190a19..111a79ea 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n For `REQ-QUAL-108` / `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`, following [`ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3](ACCEPTANCE.md#53-manual-real-terminal-matrix-e3).\n \n-> **Required for v1.0.0.** Complete all 15 cells against the exact installed RC. Blank cells are incomplete; no result is inferred. Automated PTY runs do not count as manual cell evidence. DEC-18 waives screenshot artifacts only. The prior waiver record is withdrawn by [DEC-19](DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver).\n+> **Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** No cell runs or evidence are required, and no cell result is inferred. Blank cells are not a release blocker. The worksheet remains available for optional operator checks. Automated CI (§5.1) and scripted PTY (§5.2) gates remain mandatory.\n \n ## Installed candidate identity\n \n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ Run each step against the installed candidate in the terminal and size named by\n 6. Press Ctrl-C twice; confirm clean terminal restoration (echo on, no stray escape codes).\n 7. Exercise `NO_COLOR`.\n \n-Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). This does not waive any live manual interaction, check, observation, per-cell verdict, or evidence record. Automated PTY runs do not count as completion of these manual real-terminal cells.\n+For v1.0.0, manual runs are waived by [DEC-20](DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver). If optional manual checks are performed, record only what was actually observed. Such checks do not replace mandatory automated CI (§5.1) or scripted PTY (§5.2) evidence.\n \n ## Partial operator report\n \n@@ -68,30 +68,12 @@ Select exactly one PASS or FAIL for each cell. Record observed outcomes for ever\n | 14 | GNOME Terminal | 40×14 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n | 15 | GNOME Terminal | 200×60 | [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL | | |\n \n-## Acceptance gate\n+## Optional observation summary\n \n-- Safety checks 2, 5, and 6: **zero failures across all 15 cells**. Any failure here blocks this gate.\n-- Any failure on another check requires a written disposition: fix, or a documented known limitation.\n-- All 15 cells have exactly one verdict, check outcomes, and per-cell evidence references: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n-- All non-safety failures have a written disposition: [ ] yes  [ ] no  [ ] no such failures\n-- Safety gate has zero failures: [ ] yes  [ ] no\n+- If optional checks are performed, record outcomes and failures truthfully; do not infer missing results.\n+- This worksheet does not establish acceptance of mandatory automated CI (§5.1) or scripted PTY (§5.2) gates.\n \n-§5.3 matrix gate: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n-\n-Mark the §5.3 matrix gate PASS when all 15 verdicts, check outcomes, and per-cell evidence\n-references are complete, checks 2, 5, and 6 have zero failures, and every\n-failure on another check has a written disposition. Mark it FAIL if any safety\n-check (2, 5, or 6) failed. Mark it INCOMPLETE when required evidence is missing\n-or a non-safety failure has no written disposition.\n-\n-ACC-TUI-MANUAL: [ ] PASS  [ ] FAIL  [ ] INCOMPLETE\n-\n-Mark ACC-TUI-MANUAL PASS only when all 15 cell verdicts are PASS and the\n-per-cell outcomes and evidence records are complete. Screenshots are waived per DEC-18. Mark it FAIL if any\n-cell is FAIL. Mark it INCOMPLETE when evidence is missing and no cell has\n-failed. A documented known limitation for a non-safety failure may satisfy the\n-§5.3 disposition requirement, but the cell remains FAIL and ACC-TUI-MANUAL\n-remains unmet until every cell passes.\n+§5.3 matrix disposition: WAIVED for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. Optional observations do not change that disposition.\n \n Operator summary / evidence index: ______________________________________________\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nindex 7e4ff63c..a7c5c337 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ Implements [SPEC-10](../specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md). Harne\n | 10 | Mark `nexus eval` experimental (help and docs). Fix its operator-workspace checkout: run in a worktree (VER-07a). | `index.ts:663-688`; `evaluator.ts:128` | — |\n | 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\n | 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n-| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Run the full checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3 and record all per-cell outcomes and evidence. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). | ACCEPTANCE §5.3; DEC-18 | RC build |\n+| 12 | Manual terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-20](../DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver); no manual cells or per-cell evidence are required or implied. Automated CI PTY (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) remain mandatory and must pass. | ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.3; DEC-20 | RC build |\n \n ## PR slices\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nindex 81822d95..c5b23cd3 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@\n | | |\n |---|---|\n | Status | Ready. Protocol and thresholds fixed by [DEC-05](../DECISIONS.md#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds); task authorship needs owner action X2. |\n-| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\n+| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, automated and scripted PTY terminal gates. |\n | Requirements | REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-102, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-QUAL-104, REQ-QUAL-105, REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 |\n | Findings | EVL-001, EVL-002, EVL-003, EVL-004, EVL-005, HIST-08, PRV G1/G2, TUI gaps (kitty/real terminals), VER-07 |\n | Plan | [PLAN-10](../plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) |\n@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal c\n    - The scorer logs every replacement.\n    - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n 7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n-8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts) are mandatory. A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. All 15 cells require actual operator execution and per-cell verdict/evidence bound to the exact installed RC; automated terminal evidence does not replace this gate. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix waiver record.\n+8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal acceptance.** Automated CI checks in ACCEPTANCE §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 are mandatory. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-20](../DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver); no operator runs or cell results are required or implied. Screenshot artifacts are separately waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) is superseded for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n 9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n 10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n \ndiff --git a/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md b/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\nindex 3f66cc7d..af4663e0 100644\n--- a/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\n+++ b/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n # Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n.git/nexus-claims/V1_DECISION_REJECTED_OPERATOR_DOCS_20261028/owner.json\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":452644942}},"started_at_ms":1793297465906,"completed_at_ms":1793297467360}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T18:11:08.622Z","ordinal":495767,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a188db-ccce-7ed2-aa1f-108e8cbc2cdd","call_id":"call_c72f62c905f6455b8f36ba832fb37134","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 4.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8079)\nTotal output lines: 242\n\n{\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- entire-trail-link-start --\\u003e\\nhttps://entire.com/gh/mikeholownych/-/trails/39/changes/nexus-code/39\\n\\u003c!-- entire-trail-link-end --\\u003e\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n- Record the release owner's v1.0.0 waiver of the manual five-terminal by three-size §5.3 matrix.\\n- Keep automated CI PTY (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) mandatory.\\n- Reconcile ACCEPTANCE, DECISIONS, SPEC-10, PLAN-10, REQUIREMENTS, READINESS, the worksheet, terminal procedure, and release notes.\\n- Keep REQ-QUAL-108 partial and do not imply any manual-cell pass.\\n\\n## Validation and review\\n\\n- `git diff --check` passed.\\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passed in report mode (123 rows: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open).\\n- `node cli/scripts/run_tests.mjs test/check_requirements.test.ts` passed 27/27 with isolated HOME.\\n- An enforce-mode run on the dirty worktree correctly refused to evaluate it; no enforce-mode pass is claimed.\\n- Independent read-only review ACCEPTed exact diff SHA-256 `f184c64592df59452d60ebd575b9af500a43edb509535454538160135a46f620`.\\n- Exact-head CI and CodeQL are running for `965667501f87c26f164646e52b8633812518e8a5`.\\n\\nAcceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; this decision waives only ACC-TUI-MANUAL for v1.0.0.\",\"commits\":[\"965667501f87c26f164646e52b8633812518e8a5\"],\"files\":[\"docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/README.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\",\"docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\",\"scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\"],\"title\":\"docs(release): waive manual terminal matrix for v1.0.0\"}\ndiff --git a/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md b/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\nindex 314465cd..3b38c5d4 100644\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.0.0.md\n@@ -156,7 +156,7 @@ nexus doctor\n \n ## Release qualification and waivers\n \n-- **Manual real-terminal matrix: required and not yet accepted.** The fifteen-cell manual E3 matrix (xterm, kitty, tmux in GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60) requires actual operator runs on the exact installed RC with a verdict and observed outcomes recorded for each cell. Automated CI and PTY scenarios do not substitute for this evidence. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18; DEC-19 withdraws the prior matrix-waiver record.\n+- **Manual real-terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.** No manual five-terminal by three-size runs or per-cell evidence are claimed. The automated CI checks (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios (§5.2) remain mandatory release gates and must pass.\n - **Screenshot artifacts: waived** for v1.0.0 by [DEC-18](../v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver).\n \n-The screenshot-artifact waiver does not affect any other acceptance gate. Installed-RC platform and lifecycle evidence, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, the manual terminal matrix, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger remain governed by the release decision record.\n+The manual-matrix waiver does not affect any other acceptance gate. Installed-RC platform and lifecycle evidence, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, automated and scripted PTY gates, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger remain governed by the release decision record.\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\nindex 80f4647a..3cf61ecb 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md\n@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@ The post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `\n | REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n | REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n | REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n-| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n+| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y | Installed-RC automated and scripted PTY acceptance; the manual E3 matrix is waived by DEC-20 |\n | REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n <!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n \n@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ These are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n | ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | All 15 cells have actual manual execution, recorded PASS/FAIL verdicts, observed outcomes, and evidence bound to the exact installed RC. Automated §5.1 and §5.2 do not substitute for these cells. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by DEC-18. |\n+| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five terminal environments and three sizes | Waived for v1.0.0 by DEC-20. No ma…5479 tokens truncated…qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\n | 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n-| 12 | Terminal matrix (manual): {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code, GNOME Terminal} × 3 sizes. Run the full checklist per ACCEPTANCE §5.3 and record all per-cell outcomes and evidence. Screenshot artifacts are waived for v1.0.0 per [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). | ACCEPTANCE §5.3; DEC-18 | RC build |\n+| 12 | Manual terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-20](../DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver); no manual cells or per-cell evidence are required or implied. Automated CI PTY (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) remain mandatory and must pass. | ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.3; DEC-20 | RC build |\n \n ## PR slices\n \ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\nindex 81822d95..c5b23cd3 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md\n@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@\n | | |\n |---|---|\n | Status | Ready. Protocol and thresholds fixed by [DEC-05](../DECISIONS.md#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds); task authorship needs owner action X2. |\n-| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, a PTY terminal matrix. |\n+| Release class | **BLOCKER** for any v1 maturity claim: held-out matched evaluation, fault-injection qualification, standalone live qualification, scoring integrity. RELEASE-REQUIRED: T3 long tasks, a T4 smoke test in CI, automated and scripted PTY terminal gates. |\n | Requirements | REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-102, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-QUAL-104, REQ-QUAL-105, REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-108 |\n | Findings | EVL-001, EVL-002, EVL-003, EVL-004, EVL-005, HIST-08, PRV G1/G2, TUI gaps (kitty/real terminals), VER-07 |\n | Plan | [PLAN-10](../plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md) |\n@@ -80,7 +80,7 @@ Standalone live inference evidence is absent (HIST-08; SPEC-05). Real-terminal c\n    - The scorer logs every replacement.\n    - `nexus eval` is labelled experimental and excluded from claims (DEC-07).\n 7. **REQ-QUAL-107. Standalone and provider matrix.** The live standalone set (a T2 subset of ≥ 10 tasks plus a T4 subset) is run through the gateway-stripping proxy in its plain profile and its emulated-server profiles (DEC-16). `providers verify` is run live for each provider listed as supported (DEC-06). Receipts are archived.\n-8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal matrix.** PTY scripted runs in CI (existing `tui_*_e2e`, plus the new ACC-SAFE and ACC-PROC scripts) are mandatory. A manual matrix covers {xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal} × {80x24, 40x14, 200x60}, checking: approval safety, paste, resize, cancel, narrow hints and NO_COLOR. All 15 cells require actual operator execution and per-cell verdict/evidence bound to the exact installed RC; automated terminal evidence does not replace this gate. Screenshot artifacts alone are waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) withdraws the prior matrix waiver record.\n+8. **REQ-QUAL-108. Terminal acceptance.** Automated CI checks in ACCEPTANCE §5.1 and scripted installed-RC PTY scenarios in §5.2 are mandatory. The manual five-terminal by three-size matrix in §5.3 is waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-20](../DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver); no operator runs or cell results are required or implied. Screenshot artifacts are separately waived by [DEC-18](../DECISIONS.md#dec-18-v100-terminal-screenshot-artifact-waiver). [DEC-19](../DECISIONS.md#dec-19-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver) is superseded for v1.0.0 by DEC-20.\n 9. **REQ-QUAL-109 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** T3 long tasks: at least 8 tasks × 5 runs, each over 60 steps and with at least 2 compactions. Gates: false-absence = 0, false-presence = 0 (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-18), and steering honoured ≥ 95% (eval/README thresholds).\n 10. **REQ-QUAL-110 (RELEASE-REQUIRED).** A T4 smoke (scripted model, 2 fault cases) and the T1 self-test run in `make test`.\n \ndiff --git a/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md b/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\nindex 3f66cc7d..af4663e0 100644\n--- a/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\n+++ b/scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n # Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n.git/nexus-claims/V1_DECISION_REJECTED_OPERATOR_DOCS_20261028/owner.json\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a188ca-3438-7770-bdcd-730c68c81c88","create_time":1793297468.6222665}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
