{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T18:17:50.671Z","ordinal":495977,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188df-67cc-70d2-8319-5eb100a07865","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-be515bd4-336e-45c1-b0af-d3dbbe24646d","process_id":"98941","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git branch --list 'v1/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-batch'; git worktree list --porcelain | rg 'eval-agent-toolchain-binds-batch' || true; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds merge-base HEAD origin/main; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md | sed -n '1,100p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git branch --list 'v1/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-batch'; git worktree list --porcelain | rg 'eval-agent-toolchain-binds-batch' || true; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds merge-base HEAD origin/main; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md | sed -n '1,100p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"fe1c91dbcb56693a34c06dd3719bea139f639833\n# PLAN-10: v1 qualification and task-quality evaluation\n\nImplements [SPEC-10](../specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md). Harness fixes are milestone **M3**. Task authoring runs in parallel from M1. Runs are **M5**.\n\n- Requirements: REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-110.\n- Decisions: DEC-05, DEC-06, DEC-07.\n- Owner actions: X2, X3, X4, X5.\n\n## Safe change boundary\n\n- `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/infra.mjs`\n- new `eval/fingerprint.mjs`\n- new `eval/faults/`\n- `eval/tasks/`\n- `eval/configs/`\n- `eval/README.md`\n- `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`\n- `Makefile` (T4 smoke)\n\n## Tasks\n\n| # | Task | Location | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Symmetric infrastructure classification. A run counts as infrastructure only when `first_model_request_at` is missing **and** there is an unreachable signature. Same rule for every agent. Crash and timeout rates are reported. | `infra.mjs:31`; `run.mjs` (record `first_model_request_at` from the proxy log) | — |\n| 2 | Scorer: log replacements; exclude contaminated runs from pooled rates; add metric columns for intervention, recovery, bounded-failure truthfulness, cost per correct task, and pre/post regression diff. | `score.mjs:16-21,48-84` | 1 |\n| 3 | Hidden-test isolation. Hidden tests are stored under a separate uid (`nexus-eval`, created by the operator, owner action under X3) with mode 0700, and copied in after the agent exits. The agent runs with an allow-listed env. | `run.mjs:57-59,114,178` | — |\n| 4 | Fingerprint. Record server kind, build, weights sha256 (from config), and sampling settings. Refuse the run if the fingerprint is missing. Temperature 0 or a fixed seed for every agent where the agent supports it. | new `fingerprint.mjs`; `configs/*.json` | PLAN-05 task 1 |\n| 5 | Fault proxy for T4 classes 1–4 and 7–8, scheduled per run. Fixture hooks for 5 (hanging test), 6 (disk full via a small loop-mounted fs or `ulimit -f`), and 9 (SIGTERM then `run --resume`). | new `eval/faults/proxy.mjs`; task fixtures | PLAN-04 task 1 |\n| 6 | T4 smoke in `make test`: scripted model plus 2 fault cases. The T1 self-test stays. | `cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts`; `Makefile` | 5 |\n| 7 | Task schema `{repo, commit, prompt, hidden_tests, fail_to_pass, pass_to_pass, class, difficulty}`, with a validator. | `eval/tasks/schema.json`; `run.mjs` | — |\n| 8 | Author tasks (owner action X2). Development set: the existing 6 plus routing engx T01–T12. Held-out set: 40 T2 tasks, of which at least 20 are external, at least 6 per class, across 4 languages. Plus 8 T3 tasks. The sha256 manifest is committed before RC freeze. Calibrate on the development set only. | external store; `eval/heldout-manifest.json` | 7 |\n| 9 | Peer adapters: confirm Goose and OpenCode on the same model and budgets, and record peer versions. | `run.mjs:120-143` | 4 |\n| 10 | Mark `nexus eval` experimental (help and docs). Fix its operator-workspace checkout: run in a worktree (VER-07a). | `index.ts:663-688`; `evaluator.ts:128` | — |\n| 11 | M5 runs: T2 held-out (5×), T3 (5×), T4 (9×5), standalone subset (PLAN-05), provider verify (DEC-06). Archive everything under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. | runbook in ACCEPTANCE §4–§6 | all, RC build |\n| 13 | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs`: a forward proxy to the gateway. It injects the gateway token server-side. It strips `/v1/models` to `{id,object,owned_by}`, returns 404 for `/v1/tokenize`, and drops `X-AIHost-*` and admission headers. The `--emulate {llamacpp,vllm,ollama}` profiles add that server's `/models`, `/props`, `/api/show` and overflow-error shapes, derived from the real gateway limits. Unit-tested against a mock gateway. | new `eval/standalone/` | — |\n| 12 | Manual terminal matrix: waived for v1.0.0 by [DEC-20](../DECISIONS.md#dec-20-v100-manual-terminal-matrix-waiver); no manual cells or per-cell evidence are required or implied. Automated CI PTY (§5.1) and scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) remain mandatory and must pass. | ACCEPTANCE §§5.1–5.3; DEC-20 | RC build |\n\n## PR slices\n\n- **PR-10a:** tasks 1, 2.\n- **PR-10b:** tasks 3, 4, 7.\n- **PR-10c:** tasks 5, 6.\n- **PR-10d:** tasks 9, 10.\n- **PR-10e:** task 13 (standalone proxy).\n\nTask 8 is data work. Tasks 11 and 12 are operations work.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `eval_harness.test.ts`:\n  - infra symmetry: a Nexus crash is counted as a failure, not rerun;\n  - contamination: an agent that `cat`s the hidden path is flagged and excluded from the pool;\n  - fingerprint refusal;\n  - T4 smoke.\n\n## Effort and uncertainty\n\n| Work | Estimate | Main uncertainty |\n|---|---|---|\n| Harness fixes | 4–6 engineer-days | — |\n| Task authoring | 40 T2 tasks at 1–2 hours each, plus 8 T3 tasks at 3–4 hours each: roughly 10–14 days of author time | Author availability (X2) |\n| Run wall time (historical estimate; see below) | (40×5 + 8×5 + 40) runs per agent × 3 agents ≈ 840 runs. At a median 6 min/run serial on one inference host, about 84 hours, roughly 4 days of continuous inference. T3 runs are longer. | Inference-host availability and thermal behaviour (see the `experiments/thermal-soak` history). This is the critical-path risk for M5. |\n\nThe original run-wall-time estimate above predates the nine-class T4 correction and applies three agents uniformly. It is retained as historical planning evidence, not a current run count or schedule. Before qualification, derive the schedule from the frozen workload and agent matrix in ACCEPTANCE §6: T2 specifies three agents; T4 specifies the Nexus RC only.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-108 evidence is archived.\n- The DEC-05 thresholds were evaluated with the scorer verdict table, signed off before the run and reported after it.\n- REQ-QUAL-109/110 are met.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":93726937}},"started_at_ms":1793297870576,"completed_at_ms":1793297870670}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T18:17:51.560Z","ordinal":495978,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188df-67cc-70d2-8319-5eb100a07865","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9fb1d48e-3c17-4d19-b8b7-96ae4ded9512","process_id":"96993","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","xerj feedback --submit --agent \"GPT-6 Codex\" --used-for \"Reviewed existing process timeout and descendant cleanup patterns before evaluator scanner remediation\" --verdict \"XERJ returned relevant timeout and process-group termination code in cli/src/tools.ts and doctor.ts; useful as reference, but the evaluator scanner itself is under eval/ and intentionally not indexed, so its local source remains authoritative.\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"xerj feedback --submit --agent \"GPT-6 Codex\" --used-for \"Reviewed existing process timeout and descendant cleanup patterns before evaluator scanner remediation\" --verdict \"XERJ returned relevant timeout and process-group termination code in cli/src/tools.ts and doctor.ts; useful as reference, but the evaluator scanner itself is under eval/ and intentionally not indexed, so its local source remains authoritative.\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"the `--remote` flag is unsupported when a repository argument is provided\n\nCreate a fork of a repository.\n\nWith no argument, creates a fork of the current repository. Otherwise, forks\nthe specified repository.\n\nBy default, the new fork is set to be your `origin` remote and any existing\norigin remote is renamed to `upstream`. To alter this behavior, you can set\na name for the new fork's remote with `--remote-name`.\n\nThe `upstream` remote will be set as the default remote repository.\n\nAdditional `git clone` flags can be passed after `--`.\n\n\nUSAGE\n  gh repo fork [<repository>] [-- <gitflags>...] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n  --clone                 Clone the fork\n  --default-branch-only   Only include the default branch in the fork\n  --fork-name string      Rename the forked repository\n  --org string            Create the fork in an organization\n  --remote                Add a git remote for the fork\n  --remote-name string    Specify the name for the new remote (default \"origin\")\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n  --help   Show help for command\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # Fork a repository\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo\n  \n  # Fork a repository and clone it locally\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone\n  \n  # Fork a repository without cloning it, skip the prompt\n  $ gh repo fork owner/repo --clone=false\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\nerror: this account cannot push to xerj-org/xerj, and forking failed: `gh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork` failed\nNothing was branched.\n\n# Ready-to-run — files ONLY the field report, nothing else.\n# Run these in a clone of xerj-org/xerj, not in the project you are working in.\ngit clone https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj.git\ncd xerj\ngh repo fork xerj-org/xerj --remote --remote-name xerj-fork\nxerj feedback \\\n --agent \"GPT-6 Codex\" \\\n  --used-for \"Reviewed existing process timeout and descendant cleanup patterns before evaluator scanner remediation\" --pointed-at \"1051 records under /home/mike/xerj-sources/nexus-code/core/src (autoindex run run-20261028T022152Z-ff10-0000)\" \\\n  --verdict \"XERJ returned relevant timeout and process-group termination code in cli/src/tools.ts and doctor.ts; useful as reference, but the evaluator scanner itself is under eval/ and intentionally not indexed, so its local source remains authoritative.\" --numbers \"not measured\" \\\n  -o user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-29-reviewed-existing-process-timeout-and-descendant.md\ngit checkout -b field-report/reviewed-existing-process-timeout-and-descendant\ngit add user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-29-reviewed-existing-process-timeout-and-descendant.md\ngit commit --only user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-29-reviewed-existing-process-timeout-and-descendant.md -m \"docs(field-report): reviewed-existing-process-timeout-and-descendant\"\ngit push -u xerj-fork field-report/reviewed-existing-process-timeout-and-descendant\ngh pr create --repo xerj-org/xerj --base main --head YOUR_LOGIN:field-report/reviewed-existing-process-timeout-and-descendant \\\n  --title \"Agent field report: Reviewed existing process timeout and descendant cleanup patterns before evaluator scanner remediation\" \\\n  --body \"Field report only; see user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports/2026-10-29-reviewed-existing-process-timeout-and-descendant.md.\"\nGitHub is unavailable (the pull request could not be opened (see above)); sending the field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report instead.\nsent field report to https://xerj.org/api/field-report (HTTP 200)\n{\"ok\":true,\"stored\":true,\"note\":\"Thanks. The canonical path is a GitHub PR: https://github.com/xerj-org/xerj/tree/main/user-feedback/16-agent-field-reports\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":16,"nanos":316338765}},"started_at_ms":1793297855243,"completed_at_ms":1793297871560}}
