{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T18:36:48.036Z","ordinal":496458,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188df-67cc-70d2-8319-5eb100a07865","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae3923dea6081a0b20855ef377dd16a","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The §5.3 manual terminal matrix is **waived** for v1.0.0, as recorded in merged PR #324/DEC-20. This does not count as a pass; automated CI PTY (§5.1) and installed-RC scripted PTY (§5.2) remain mandatory.\n\nI prepared a scanner fix on a separate worktree at `064244fa`. It batches sibling directories while preserving the full scan and fail-closed limits, and adds a synthetic compiler canary in a later batch. Static checks pass, but the new test has **not** run yet.\n\nPR #318’s exact CI run `40924670205` failed on Node 22 and 24: compiler-exposure scanning exceeded its 25-second deadline. The existing full suite is still active and progressing on the untouched snapshot under SUITE ownership; I’ll run the focused validation after it releases. The patch is not committed or integrated.\n\nAcceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**. RC10 is still the latest published candidate; no stable v1.0.0 release is verified.\n\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","memory_citation":{"entries":[{"path":"MEMORY.md","lineStart":765,"lineEnd":765,"note":"worktree and suite ownership protocol"}],"rolloutIds":[]}},"started_at_ms":1793299006157,"completed_at_ms":1793299008036}}
