 `switched`; `nexus upgrade --recover` restored the verified RC10 package, retained the failed target for diagnosis, asserted that the journal's staging directory and any `.tmp-upgrade-*` entry were removed, and was idempotent. **Power loss is not tested** | [log](ubuntu-22-04-node22-upgrade-process-crash-recovery.log) |\n+| Incompatible downgrade | A synthetic release (`prepare-incompatible-fixture.sh`) declares state schema 1; `nexus upgrade --version v1.0.0-rc.4 --allow-downgrade --yes` was refused with `uses state schema version 1, which cannot read current state schema version 2`. Installed version, launcher target and package hash were unchanged and no target directory was created | [log](ubuntu-22-04-node22-incompatible-downgrade.log) |\n | Provenance attestation | `gh attestation verify nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.10.tar.gz -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` exited 0 on the published archive (SHA-256 `444d0812…b3e7`) with a Sigstore bundle; `--format json` returned a 13,989-byte verification result | [log](attestation-rc10.log) |\n \n-The four additional lifecycle scripts do not set `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION`; their installer calls use the installer's default `auto` mode. Provenance attestation is verified independently by the attestation cell above.\n+The other additional lifecycle scripts do not set `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION`; their installer calls use the installer's default `auto` mode. The incompatible-downgrade script sets it to `0` explicitly. Provenance attestation is verified independently by the attestation cell above.\n \n Per-cell logs and results: `results.tsv`; image names and IDs: `prepared-images.json`; digests: `SHA256SUMS`.\n \n+## Incompatible-downgrade fixture\n+\n+`lifecycle/prepare-incompatible-fixture.sh <rc10-archive> <out>` builds a synthetic `v1.0.0-rc.4` release from the published RC10 package (same contents, `compatibility.json` rewritten to declare state schema 1 and the rc.4 archive binding) and writes a local API JSON. `lifecycle/run-incompatible-downgrade.sh` installs RC10 in a container, serves the fixture locally, and asserts the refusal plus an unchanged installation. No published RC declares an older state schema (rc.5–rc.10 all declare 2), which is why the fixture is synthetic.\n+\n ## Reproduce\n \n ```sh\n@@ -69,6 +74,6 @@ The positive cells use Docker `--network bridge` to download the published RC10\n \n ## Scope and residuals\n \n-- This covers the fresh-install / doctor / Node-preflight matrix plus the lifecycle cells (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 40 / Node 22) for E2 (ACC-PLAT) on RC10: install, installer-driven version switch and rollback, reinstall, repair and uninstall; checksum tamper; broken-candidate self-test; backup restore; updater process-crash recovery; and provenance-attestation verification. An ordinary successful `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 is not executable because alpha.2 has no updater command; the alpha.2 row is installer-driven. Power-loss durability, synthetic-journal recovery and incompatible downgrade remain separate: every published RC (rc.5–rc.10) declares state schema 2, so an incompatible downgrade needs a synthetic candidate or an explicit fixture.\n+- This covers the fresh-install / doctor / Node-preflight matrix plus the lifecycle cells (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 40 / Node 22) for E2 (ACC-PLAT) on RC10: install, installer-driven version switch and rollback, reinstall, repair and uninstall; checksum tamper; broken-candidate self-test; backup restore; updater process-crash recovery with staging cleanup; incompatible downgrade from a synthetic state-schema-1 release; and provenance-attestation verification. An ordinary successful `nexus upgrade` from alpha.2 is not executable because alpha.2 has no updater command; the alpha.2 row is installer-driven. Power-loss durability and synthetic-journal recovery remain untested and out of scope for this evidence.\n - `endpoint.reachable` failing is expected in the isolated containers and is not a product failure; the same doctor run on a host with a configured gateway is the installed-RC provider evidence path.\n - Images were prepared for the RC9 matrix (`prep-182e8addeee0`). `prepared-images.json` records each cell label, image reference and image ID; it does not store separate base-distribution or Node-version fields. Positive-cell logs print the container's `node --version`; Node 24 cells mount the host Node v24.11.1 runtime into the Node 22 image.\ndiff --git a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS\nindex 3822aab8..dd25135f 100644\n--- a/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS\n+++ b/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.10/platform-e2/SHA256SUMS\n@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ c95b7668035ea701f6e1c0a46172cf095a3a26c3f4f7b5dc166b1104e481b670  fedora-40-node\n f209d31e1d23f5566837104097483f1bde10ce6c051d9f77d82e8255b5b734ac  ubuntu-22-04-node22-backup-restore.log\n 8c3965667050b2b7c59fdba5e36ceadd264409307390138c33caada5e9c06a64  ubuntu-22-04-node22-checksum-tamper.log\n 96f867497b8c05cc781a2dbafc3d45f8e5986b69de78ea5cdc53b3a54a8796b0  ubuntu-22-04-node22-lifecycle.log\n-1b77adfbb60b60d183ea43bca59b996f1bcd425f31e00c44b5ea01a59f2272e5  ubuntu-22-04-node22-upgrade-process-crash-recovery.log\n+cb419ac9383d9558f4688b2896a974dbdb8d9fef8e773abaa4bd342b8b8bb1bc  ubuntu-22-04-node22-upgrade-process-crash-recovery.log\n 7ee7794cebe7cdef9c5759f03056a05350b0271e30664f3b4e0d53e7d4a0a94b  ubuntu-22-04-node22-upgrade-self-test-failure.log\n cf74e70bf27186c7f8858a719f773cd5e82a931a58e1569bc3026ff038d24b80  ubuntu-22-04-node22.log\n aca63b7a4eeb7dc4929fca7278ceb78f152ce255d5bcccf0730bdfea2164591f  ubuntu-22-04-node24.log\n@@ -39,12 +39,16 @@ fd4ec10b831834eb7060df9dbd311b6e716f716415f6a1f4c516856f61590c14  run-rc10-lifec\n 49d712164756b3fb784ba813006ac1dbd8574c4a5994ffb8696d0ae6a182c0c8  lifecycle/prepare-lifecycle-fixtures.sh\n 9f4a9b5a555ae955dcc9fc42089c38