{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:03:19.241Z","ordinal":497415,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae398754ca081a0ad581bcc88d69a2a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_0571ef0bf2f841b592140ba9a9f1af55","name":"exec","input":"const r=await Promise.allSettled([\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh issue view 1 --json number,state,title,assignees,updatedAt,comments --jq '{number,state,title,assignees,updatedAt,comments:[.comments[-5:][]|{createdAt,author:.author.login,body}]}'\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1800}),\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -n -i 'custodian|custody owner|primary session|custody handoff' docs/v1.0.0 eval | head -70\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-batch\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1800})\n]);\nfor(let i=0;i<r.length;i++){text(`RESULT ${i}`);text(r[i].status===\"fulfilled\"?r[i].value.output:String(r[i].reason));}\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a188f4-34f0-7702-9fc6-6c1c2c27142e","create_time":1793300597.3007994}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:03:19.374Z","ordinal":497416,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188f4-34f0-7702-9fc6-6c1c2c27142e","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a188f4-34f0-7702-9fc6-6c1c2c27142e","response_id":"resp_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae3986ec4ac81a0937d5eca4d2266bd","usage":{"input_tokens":191081,"cached_input_tokens":190208,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":942,"reasoning_output_tokens":723,"total_tokens":192023},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":24527480,"cached_input_tokens":24347648,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":48804,"reasoning_output_tokens":28016,"total_tokens":24576284},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":9238286030,"cached_input_tokens":9137979776,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":26476143,"reasoning_output_tokens":15370306,"total_tokens":9264762173}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:03:21.211Z","ordinal":497417,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188f4-34f0-7702-9fc6-6c1c2c27142e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-0a780383-1a6f-4d5c-b96c-a95a01d98036","process_id":"83597","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 1 --json number,state,title,assignees,updatedAt,comments --jq '{number,state,title,assignees,updatedAt,comments:[.comments[-5:][]|{createdAt,author:.author.login,body}]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 1 --json number,state,title,assignees,updatedAt,comments --jq '{number,state,title,assignees,updatedAt,comments:[.comments[-5:][]|{createdAt,author:.author.login,body}]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"assignees\":[],\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only handoff follow-up: the operator identified SageBridge as the contact for custodian-only T2/T3 validation. Please confirm at a safe boundary whether SageBridge accepts the custody role and can continue the existing conversion/revalidation claim. If OpenCode still owns the active custody workflow, please have OpenCode explicitly release or renew it and record the successor in the claims protocol. Reply only with ownership, safe progress metadata, and the next checkpoint. Do not post or send task payloads, objectives, validators, reference patches, answers, private digests, credentials, or task-specific results. Qualification remains stopped until the full successor corpus has independent custody acceptance.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T06:54:11Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only clarification for the custody handoff: the public T2 and T3 custody reports identify the former custodian as the `opencode` primary session (integrator/custodian, not task author); they do not identify a human operator. The handoff log later names SageBridge, but the subsequent `coordination_only` status and current claim file leave the active custodian unclear.\\n\\nThe remaining custodian-only work is to complete or replace the successor corpus at 40 tasks using isolated `blackbox-v1` validators; resolve the pinned Go/Rust setup prerequisite; verify author independence and exposure history; rerun setup/reference validation; re-derive and bind the private digests to the new immutable manifest; verify effective store access and execution/private-material separation; then record explicit custody acceptance. This is custody validation, not qualification. Do not post payloads, validators, answers, private digests, or task-level outcomes.\\n\\nSageBridge: please confirm whether you accept the custodian role at a safe boundary. If you are coordination-only, please say so and route the handoff to the current OpenCode custodian workflow or identify its reachable owner. Qualification remains stopped until acceptance is recorded.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T07:12:13Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Coordinator follow-up (metadata only; no held-out payloads accessed).\\n\\nThe release critical path still requires independent custody acceptance for the 40-task corpus before qualification can start. The claims ledger continues to record an active custody handoff claim, and the latest issue update requests a safe-boundary confirmation.\\n\\nPlease reply with status only:\\n\\n1. Who currently owns corpus authorship and custody?\\n2. How many tasks are complete, validated, and ready for custody review?\\n3. Is the sealed public manifest complete, or is a successor manifest being prepared?\\n4. Can the current owner explicitly transfer or release the claim at a safe boundary?\\n5. What remains before the custodian can record acceptance?\\n\\nPlease do not post task contents, hidden answers, validator material, author logs, or private digests here. Coordinate those details only through the approved custody channel.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T12:59:35Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only custody handoff update (no private task material accessed).\\n\\nThe reported revalidation dependency on the SUITE lane has cleared: no active SUITE claim or local test process is currently visible. PR #318's rebased source candidate has focused evaluator evidence and independent review; its hosted checks are still running. No held-out qualification was started.\\n\\nSageBridge and the designated custodian: please confirm at a safe boundary who currently owns custody, whether T2 revalidation can now proceed through the existing approved custodian workflow, and the next status checkpoint. Please release or renew the custody claim explicitly. Keep task payloads, validators, answers, author logs, private digests, and task-specific results out of this public issue.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T16:51:28Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release coordinator status request (2026-10-29; public metadata only; no private corpus material accessed): the latest custody claim metadata reports 20/40 T2 tasks built and no fresh T2 custody acceptance. T3 metadata is reported 8/8, but fresh custody acceptance remains unverified. The current integration is `fe1c91dbcb56693a34c06dd3719bea139f639833`; no held-out qualification has started.\\n\\nPlease have the designated custodian acknowledge the current owner and provide a metadata-only progress update. To unblock the release, either complete the remaining task authoring and custodian-only validation, or explicitly hand off the custody claim to an independent custodian who can do so. Do not post payloads, hidden answers, private validators, author logs, or sensitive digests here. No changes to the sealed corpus are authorized through this status request.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-29T17:35:39Z\"}],\"number\":1,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal the held-out T2/T3 corpus\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-29T17:35:39Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":663019588}},"started_at_ms":1793300600548,"completed_at_ms":1793300601211}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:03:21.371Z","ordinal":497418,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188f4-34f0-7702-9fc6-6c1c2c27142e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-26dc40b1-7e1f-4632-a5fb-5101a045f3ae","process_id":"34062","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n -i 'custodian|custody owner|primary session|custody handoff' docs/v1.0.0 eval | head -70"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-batch","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -i 'custodian|custody owner|primary session|custody handoff' docs/v1.0.0 eval","query":"custodian|custody owner|primary session|custody handoff","path":"v1.0.0"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"eval/README.md:152:  not cover fixture files. The frozen config carries `corpusCustody: { custodian, approvedAt, reportPath, reportSha256 }`\neval/README.md:174:or converted by the authorized custodian, with custody checks repeated and a new immutable manifest identity recorded.\neval/README.md:236:no custody fields, so the frozen config states `corpusCustody: { custodian, approvedAt, reportPath, reportSha256 }`;\neval/heldout-t3-manifest.json:9:    \"custodian\": \"opencode (custodian)\",\neval/validate.mjs:340: * The custodian's hidden-directory digest (heldout-v2 hash_scheme): regular files only, paths relative to the hidden\neval/validate.mjs:361: * The sealed T2 corpus (eval/heldout-manifest.json) uses the custodian's heldout-v2 schema, which binds each task's\neval/validate.mjs:370:  if (typeof custody?.custodian !== \"string\" || !custody.custodian.trim() || Number.isNaN(Date.parse(custody?.approvedAt ?? \"\")) || typeof custody?.reportPath !== \"string\" || !/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(custody?.reportSha256 ?? \"\")) {\neval/validate.mjs:371:    return \"a heldout-v2 corpus needs corpusCustody { custodian, approvedAt, reportPath, reportSha256 } in the frozen config\";\neval/validate.mjs:416:  if (typeof manifest.custody?.custodian !== \"string\" || !manifest.custody.custodian.trim() || !manifest.custody?.approvedAt) {\neval/validate.mjs:417:    return \"qualification corpus manifest lacks custodian identity or approval timestamp\";\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:219:- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:- [ ] The exact-RC evidence gate passes from the clean RC worktree and is bound to the exact RC source commit and installed RC artifact. Run the checker with the custodian-approved, immutable qualification record and evidence directory:\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:343:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md:94:- **Hidden-test isolation.** Private validators and expected answers must remain outside every task process's readable namespace. A task workspace may contain only its permitted baseline and task inputs; evaluation of private expectations must be performed outside that task boundary. Corpus custody and evaluator execution isolation are separate acceptance gates: the custodian's sealed-store disposition does not establish that the runner prevents task processes from reading validators. On the current integration candidate, evaluator-boundary acceptance remains open; PR #33 is not qualified for held-out use until the actual workspace-construction and execution path demonstrates this boundary and passes independent review. Do not use filesystem ownership of the custodian store as a substitute for validating the task-process boundary.\neval/host/README.md:34:`validate.mjs` uses the operator's own root sudo for two probes of the custodian's root-owned store: that it\neval/host/README.md:48:Custodian calibration across all 40 sealed T2 reference solutions passed 40/40 under this profile:\neval/host/README.md:75:1. **Calibration (custodian, before freeze).** The custodian validates every sealed task's reference solution under\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:15:**Held-out custody and qualification:** The latest public metadata update on issue #1 (06:02 UTC) records unresolved custody ownership: a historical handoff log names SageBridge as an accepted successor, while the active custody record still names OpenCode. The latest posted T2 count is 20/40 tasks; no new custody acceptance or qualification result is recorded. T3's reported 8/8 covers digest/schema/isolation metadata, not task-quality qualification. The custodian identity and acknowledged transfer must be reconciled before qualification. No private payloads were accessed by implementation work. T2/T3/T4 held-out qualification, standalone/provider acceptance, long-task/fault-injection qualification, and successor-RC cross-runner reproducibility remain incomplete.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:29:**Qualification and custody:** Public `v1.0.0-rc.10` remains the latest prerelease; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. The claims identify OpenCode as the prior/current custodian workflow, but do not verify the responsible human identity; SageBridge's 04:15 status says it is coordinating only. The successor T2 store remains 20/40 tasks; the remaining Go/Rust tasks need the reviewed, pinned-toolchain change integrated. Reported T3 digest/schema/isolation checks are 8/8, which is not full T3 task-quality qualification. At 04:23 UTC the OpenCode custodian holds SUITE for two-round setup/reference/oracle revalidation of the 20 converted tasks with isolated HOME; a live validator child process was observed. This is custody revalidation, not held-out qualification; no result or custody acceptance is recorded. Public Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open and unassigned; the latest metadata-only correction was posted at 04:18 UTC. T2 custody acceptance and qualification, full T3/T4 qualification, current-candidate provider and standalone qualification, fault injection, successor-RC reproducibility and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete. RC10 evidence does not qualify a successor candidate.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:33:**Suite evidence:** `make test` completed on immutable snapshot `03bfaa394c906d900574f35104e521844049403c` with isolated HOME and the required evaluator workspace/runtime fixtures: 1,993 tests across 224 suites, 1,991 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped, 0 cancelled; Rust tests and post-test security lifecycle gates passed. The full run took 3,167,118 ms. This snapshot is not exact current main, PR #311 candidate `fe28ec9`, or an RC, so the result does not qualify those revisions. The SUITE claim transferred to the OpenCode custodian at 04:18 UTC for the 20-task custody revalidation above.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:45:**Qualification and release:** Public [v1.0.0-rc.10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.10) remains the latest release; no stable `v1.0.0` release exists. Official cross-runner run [40564959805](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40564959805) passed for the published RC10 source `16ee8ca3643824741b6da67936b41f262414fdf0`, rebuilding on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04. Its machine-readable evidence reports `REQ-REL-114` / `ACC-SUP-08` `PASS` and matching hashes for six outputs, including the published archive and `sbom.cdx.json`; see the [RC10 reproducibility record](../reviews/evidence/v1/REQ-REL-114-rc10-20261027/README.md). The requirements ledger still marks `REQ-REL-114` `UNV`/open; its owner must reconcile that disposition. RC10 evidence does not establish successor-RC qualification. Issue [#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1) remains open an