{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:10:12.298Z","ordinal":497603,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188f4-34f0-7702-9fc6-6c1c2c27142e","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5571c711-3df4-424d-a540-7da9111b5ad4","process_id":"40230","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 327 --json number,state,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefName,mergeStateStatus,url,statusCheckRollup --jq '{number,state,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefName,mergeStateStatus,url,checks:[.statusCheckRollup[]|{name:.name,state:.status,conclusion:.conclusion}]}'\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- release note current wording ---'\ngit show fe1c91dbcb56693a34c06dd3719bea139f639833:docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md | rg -n -i -C 1 'terminal|matrix|waiv|§5\\.1|§5\\.2' | head -20\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- owner ---'\njq '{agent,branch,worktree,head,since,scope,status}' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_releases_v1_0_0-rc_11_md/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-batch","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 327 --json number,state,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefName,mergeStateStatus,url,statusCheckRollup --jq '{number,state,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefName,mergeStateStatus,url,checks:[.statusCheckRollup[]|{name:.name,state:.status,conclusion:.conclusion}]}'\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- release note current wording ---'\ngit show fe1c91dbcb56693a34c06dd3719bea139f639833:docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.11.md | rg -n -i -C 1 'terminal|matrix|waiv|§5\\.1|§5\\.2' | head -20\nprintf '%s\\n' '--- owner ---'\njq '{agent,branch,worktree,head,since,scope,status}' /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_docs_releases_v1_0_0-rc_11_md/owner.json 2>/dev/null || true"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"checks\":[{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"javascript-typescript\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"linux-x86_64\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":\"FAILURE\",\"name\":\"Entire Gates\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"name\":\"CodeQL\",\"state\":\"COMPLETED\"},{\"conclusion\":null,\"name\":null,\"state\":null}],\"headRefName\":\"codex/rc11-dec20-release-notes\",\"headRefOid\":\"801d4470cc4f7ef981999f3c75023ffdd706d2d0\",\"mergeStateStatus\":\"UNSTABLE\",\"number\":327,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/327\"}\n--- release note current wording ---\n13-- **Test-first work units (opt-in):** `NEXUS_TDD=1` (or `AgentWorkUnitExecutor({ tdd: true })`) runs implementer units as a RED turn that must record a failing, executed verifier and a changed test, then a GREEN turn. RED evidence is a private sidecar keyed by the unit task and prompt; the verifier baseline is rebased only onto the added tests, and a RED that narrows the operator's tests or verifier is refused. See `docs/v1.0.0/TDD-WORK-UNITS.md`.\n14:- **Read-only operation view:** `nexus operation status --dag [--json]` and `nexus operation watch` project the unit DAG, resource eligibility, open decisions and the event tail without taking the operation lock or writing a transition. Operation text is sanitised for terminal control sequences. See `docs/v1.1.0/OPERATION_OBSERVABILITY.md`.\n15-- **Git-aware isolated operations (opt-in):** `spec.git = { isolate: true, baseRef? }` gives each unit its own worktree and branch, integrates completions into an operation branch with receipts, re-verifies the merged tree, and blocks with `MERGE_CONFLICT` / `INTEGRATION_FAILED` decisions. Recovery is idempotent and fails closed when integration history is missing or rewritten. See `docs/v1.1.0/GIT_AWARE_OPERATIONS.md`.\n--\n24-- Clean-checkout build identity is recorded correctly, and packaged smoke startup no longer races its log.\n25:- CLI terminal output sanitises control characters in corrupt-resume errors; batch read paths preserve lossy UTF-8 and propagate read errors instead of continuing.\n26-- Credential handling: malformed credential origins can no longer be rebound, and credential-store writes are failure-atomic under the file guard.\n--\n32-\n33:- Readiness, terminal and qualification records were refreshed through 2026-10-29. The manual real-terminal matrix is **required** for v1.0.0; the earlier matrix-waiver record was withdrawn (DEC-19). Screenshot artifacts alone are waived (DEC-18).\n34-\n--\n48-\n49:This is a candidate, not an accepted release. The installed-RC gates — platform and lifecycle evidence, the fifteen-cell manual terminal matrix, provider and standalone qualification, held-out task quality, cross-runner reproducibility, independent exact-RC acceptance and the requirements ledger — remain outstanding for this artifact. Passing source CI does not satisfy them.\n--- owner ---\n{\n  \"agent\": \"OlivePeak\",\n  \"branch\": \"codex/rc11-dec20-release-notes\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc11-dec20-release-notes\",\n  \"head\": \"801d4470cc4f7ef981999f3c75023ffdd706d2d0\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-29T16:56:00Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Correct only RC11 release-note statements that contradict accepted DEC-20; keep §5.1 and §5.2 mandatory and do not claim qualification passes. Documentation-only; no product or held-out changes.\",\n  \"status\": \"PR #327 open; exact-head CI queued/in progress; awaiting checks and independent review\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":928996631}},"started_at_ms":1793301010369,"completed_at_ms":1793301012298}}
