{"timestamp":"2026-10-29T19:13:06.723Z","ordinal":497682,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a188f4-34f0-7702-9fc6-6c1c2c27142e","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0e1c614dbfb55a8c016ae39ac0422081a087a2c90263005c79","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"Confirmed. DEC-20 is present on `origin/main` at `fe1c91db` and supersedes DEC-19: the manual 5×3 matrix is **waived, not passed**. Automated CI PTY §5.1 and installed-RC scripted PTY §5.2 remain mandatory ([decision](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-batch/docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:261), [acceptance criteria](/home/mike/nexus-wt/eval-agent-toolchain-binds-batch/docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:159)).\n\nMain CI run `40919652186` and CodeQL run `40919651757` passed on that revision. The release remains in progress: RC10 is still the latest published candidate, with no accepted RC or stable v1.0.0 verified.\n\nPR #318’s Node 22/24 checks still fail on head `064244fa`. The local scanner-batching patch is uncommitted. Its first focused run failed because the worktree’s group-writable helper was rejected by the evaluator’s fail-closed check; I corrected the local mode. Another agent then claimed SUITE for a rerun. Its process is no longer visible, but its claim remains, so I recorded a request for the exact result and claim release/renewal without taking over or treating the run as pass or fail.\n\n**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE` — acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1793301184276,"completed_at_ms":1793301186723}}
